{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrUzisPRjoSF5he3D74","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011paortrMsutKXgCrgMofUP","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/PLAN.md","offset":470,"limit":390},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":330,"cache_read_input_tokens":41251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":330},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"d184d7a2-3c73-4d22-9102-7a4abf2c65f9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:02:34.757Z","request_id":"req_011CghrUzTjLrnZkkkhFxLdt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011paortrMsutKXgCrgMofUP":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/PLAN.md","offset":470,"limit":390}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011paortrMsutKXgCrgMofUP","type":"tool_result","content":"470\t- The field is flat (z = 0). Height comes from terrain types and props, as in the source's flat hex maps. Raised blocks\n471\t  (ramparts, gears, cliffs) are impassable shapes (§7.2).\n472\t\n473\t### 5.2 Sides and deployment\n474\t- Two sides, attacker and defender, each with up to 3 troops. A troop is one knight and up to 6 monsters.\n475\t- Troop anchors are hexes `1 2 3` (attacker) and `7 8 9` (defender). The defender's first troop takes the anchor next to\n476\t  the Keep. Skirmish and hub maps use seat anchors `1 2 3 4`.\n477\t- The knight stands on the anchor, and its monsters fill the free hexes nearest it according to its formation:\n478\t  - **Vanguard:** hexes 1–2 steps toward the enemy's side first.\n479\t  - **Shield:** the ring around the knight first.\n480\t  - **Column:** a line behind the knight, away from the enemy.\n481\t- Units face the enemy side.\n482\t\n483\t### 5.3 Bells and turn order\n484\t- A battle lasts up to `tune.bells` (12) bells.\n485\t- Each bell, troops act in order of their knight's AGI (descending; ties go to the defender, then the lower troop id).\n486\t- In a troop's turn, each of its units acts once, in any order its controller likes. The troop ends when all have acted\n487\t  or its controller ends it (the rest Wait). A troop whose knight has fallen is gone.\n488\t- **At the end of each bell:**\n489\t  1. effects tick (§5.8);\n490\t  2. the Keep heals its owner's unit standing on it by 10% of max HP;\n491\t  3. map rules run (the Sanctum's Hands and Dials, §6.10; the hub's season advance, §11);\n492\t  4. the win checks run (§5.10).\n493\t- Each new bell tolls a bell sound and the clock face's hand moves.\n494\t\n495\t### 5.4 A unit's turn\n496\t- **Move:** up to MOV, paying terrain costs (§5.7). A unit can't enter or pass enemies, can pass allies, and can't end\n497\t  on an occupied hex. Before acting, a move can be undone with Back.\n498\t- **Then one action, or one action with no move:**\n499\t\n500\t| Action | Rule |\n501\t|---|---|\n502\t| Attack | the unit's basic attack (range and power from its spec); allowed after moving |\n503\t| Special | a skill of kind `special`; after moving only if it is *mobile*; some (Charge, Dive) require moving at least 2 hexes this turn |\n504\t| Spell | a skill of kind `spell`; **only if the unit has not moved this turn** |\n505\t| Item | knights only: a consumable from the realm inventory, on itself or an adjacent ally |\n506\t| Guard | +30% DEF and +10 evasion until its next turn; allowed after moving |\n507\t| Retreat | knights only: the troop leaves the field at once (capture rolls, §5.9). A ruler's retreat loses the battle |\n508\t| Wait | end the unit's turn |\n509\t\n510\t- MP: skills cost MP. Each unit regains 2 MP at its troop's turn start.\n511\t\n512\t### 5.5 Stats\n513\t- HP, MP, ATK, DEF, INT (magic power and magic defense), AGI (evasion, hit, crit, turn order) and MOV.\n514\t- Tags: element (Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter or Hour), size (S, M, L), and flags: flier (ignores terrain cost and may\n515\t  cross blocked hexes but not end on ramparts), swimmer (water costs 1, deep water is walkable), floater (swamp and\n516\t  shallows cost 1).\n517\t- Knights also have Bond and Ward radius (§6.6).\n518\t- Levels run from 1 to 40, and 100 EXP gives a level, applied at once with a popup.\n519\t\n520\t### 5.6 Formulas (every constant is in `G.tune`, Appendix A)\n521\t- **Ward:** a monster outside its own knight's Ward (hex distance > radius) has ATK, DEF and INT × (1 − `wardPenalty`\n522\t  0.20).\n523\t- **Hit chance (physical):** `clamp(baseHit 85 + (A.AGI − D.AGI) + sizeHit[A.size][D.size] + flank − terrainEvade(D) −\n524\t  5 × max(0, dist − 2) − weather − (D guarding ? 10 : 0), 15, 99)`.\n525\t  - `sizeHit` (attacker row, target column S / M / L): S: 0 / 0 / +10; M: −10 / 0 / +10; L: −30 / −10 / 0 (the L row\n526\t    is `tune.largeVsSmall`).\n527\t  - `flank` = +5 for each other unit of A's side adjacent to D, at most +15.\n528\t- **Physical damage:** `max(1, round((A.ATK × P − D.DEF × defFactor 0.5) × dmgScale × elem × tide × terrainDef × guard ×\n529\t  surround × crit × var))`.\n530\t  - P is the attack's power (a basic attack is 1.0).\n531\t  - `elem` is 1.30 (`elemStrong`) when A's element opposes D's (Spring ↔ Autumn, Summer ↔ Winter), 0.80 (`elemSame`)\n532\t    when they match, and 1.0 otherwise. Hour is 1.0 both ways, except anti-Hour skills (§6.7).\n533\t  - `tide` = attacker factor × target factor, from §5.11.\n534\t  - `terrainDef` = 1 − D's terrain DEF bonus. `guard` = 0.7 if D guards.\n535\t  - `surround` = 1 + 0.10 × (A's allies adjacent to D, at most 3).\n536\t  - `crit` = 1.5 with chance `critBase` 3% + A.AGI / 4 % (at most 30%).\n537\t  - `var` is uniform between 0.9 and 1.1.\n538\t- **Magic damage (always hits):** `max(1, round((P + A.INT − D.INT × 0.5) × magicScale × elem × tide × var))`, where P\n539\t  is the spell's power (14, 22 or 34 for bolts, storms and tempests). Areas hit everyone in the shape, friends included.\n540\t- **Breath, cone and line specials** use the physical formula, always hit, and apply the element.\n541\t- **Healing:** `round((P + A.INT × 0.8) × healScale)`.\n542\t- **Status chance:** `clamp(base + A.INT − D.INT, 10, 90) × statusScale`. Bosses halve it; the Warding Charm makes its\n543\t  wearer immune to Sleep and Stop.\n544\t- **EXP:**\n545\t  - per damaging hit: `clamp(8 + 2 × (D.level − A.level), 2, 30) × expScale`;\n546\t  - a KO: +20 (a knight +40, a ruler +60);\n547\t  - a heal or buff: +8;\n548\t  - at the end: +10 for each survivor of the winning side, +4 for the losing side.\n549\t- **Level-up growth:** for each stat, `floor(g)` plus 1 more if a seeded roll falls under `g − floor(g)`.\n550\t\n551\t### 5.7 Terrain\n552\t\n553\t| Code | Terrain | Move cost | DEF | Evade | Season transform and notes |\n554\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n555\t| `.` | plain | 1 | 0 | 0 | Winter → snow |\n556\t| `,` | road | 1 | 0 | 0 | — |\n557\t| `f` | forest | 2 (L: 3; fliers 1) | +20% | +10 | Summer: burns under Summer area spells; Autumn: +10% DEF only (leaf-fall) |\n558\t| `h` | hill | 2 (fliers 1) | +10% | +5 | ranged attacks from a hill get +1 range; melee from a hill +10% damage |\n559\t| `m` | mountain | blocked (fliers 1) | +20% (a perched flier) | +10 | — |\n560\t| `~` | shallows | 2 (swimmers and fliers 1) | −10% | −10 | Spring on flood maps → deep water; Summer: cost 1; Winter → ice |\n561\t| `w` | deep water | blocked (swimmers and fliers 1) | 0 | 0 | Winter → ice |\n562\t| `L` | lake | as deep water | 0 | 0 | Winter → ice (a frozen lake opens the map) |\n563\t| `s` | swamp | 3 (fliers and floaters 1) | −10% | −10 | Summer → plain (dried); Winter: cost 2 |\n564\t| `F` | field | 1 | 0 | 0 | Summer: tall wheat, +10 evade; Autumn: stubble; Winter → snow |\n565\t| `r` | ruins | 1 | +10% | +5 | — |\n566\t| `#` | rampart, gear or building | blocked (fliers may cross but not end there) | — | — | drawn as a raised hex block (§7.2) |\n567\t| `g` | courtyard or gate | 1 | +10% | 0 | — |\n568\t| `b` | bridge | 1 | 0 | 0 | — |\n569\t| `K` | Keep | 1 | +25% for its owner | 0 | owner heals 10% per bell on it; the attacker's seize objective |\n570\t| `D` | season dial | 1 | 0 | 0 | the Sanctum only (§6.10) |\n571\t| — | snow | 2 for non-Winter walkers, 1 for Winter units and fliers | 0 | 0 | from plain or field in Winter |\n572\t| — | ice | 1 | 0 | −10 | from water in Winter; non-Winter units on ice −10 hit |\n573\t| — | burning forest | 2 | 0 | 0 | lasts 2 bells; a unit starting its turn there takes 10% max HP; then it becomes ash |\n574\t| — | ash | 1 | 0 | 0 | after burning |\n575\t\n576\t### 5.8 Effects (statuses, buffs and debuffs)\n577\t\n578\t| Effect | Kind | Rule | Lasts |\n579\t|---|---|---|---|\n580\t| Poison | status | −8% max HP at its troop's turn start | 3 bells |\n581\t| Burn | status | −5% max HP at turn start, DEF −10% | 2 bells |\n582\t| Chill | status | MOV −1, AGI −20% | 2 bells |\n583\t| Sleep | status | skips its turns; wakes when damaged | 2 bells |\n584\t| Stop | status | skips its next turn, then is immune to Stop for 1 bell | 1 turn |\n585\t| Valor | buff | ATK +20% | 2 bells |\n586\t| Haste | buff | MOV +1, AGI +20% | 2 bells |\n587\t| Warded | buff | DEF +20%, and magic damage taken −20% | 2 bells |\n588\t| Guarded | buff | the Guard action (§5.4) | until its next turn |\n589\t| Weakened | debuff | ATK −15% | 2 bells |\n590\t| Exposed | debuff | DEF −20% | 2 bells |\n591\t\n592\tA unit holds one copy of each effect; reapplying refreshes the duration. Remedy and Purify clear statuses and debuffs.\n593\t\n594\t### 5.9 Knights falling, retreat, capture and death\n595\t- When a knight drops to 0 HP or retreats, its troop leaves the field. Each of its monsters still standing rolls for\n596\t  capture if it is adjacent to an enemy knight or inside an enemy knight's Ward:\n597\t  - chance = `captureBase` 25% + 25% if it was outside its own knight's Ward + 15% if below 30% HP, at most 75%;\n598\t  - bosses and Hour elites (Pendulum Wyrm forms) never roll;\n599\t  - a captured monster is taken by the nearest enemy knight (shown with a chain of light). After the battle it joins\n600\t    the winner's reserve at the contested castle if its captor's side won, or the reserve of the captor's home castle\n601\t    if it lost;\n602\t  - every other monster retreats with its knight.\n603\t- If a ruler falls or retreats, every knight on its side retreats at once and the side loses.\n604\t- Monsters at 0 HP die and are gone for good (the Phoenix's Rebirth is the exception, §6.8). Knights at 0 HP are wounded\n605\t  for the next season.\n606\t\n607\t### 5.10 Winning\n608\t- A side loses the moment it has no knights on the field.\n609\t- At the end of the last bell, the attacker wins if one of its knights stands on a Keep hex; otherwise the defender wins\n610\t  and the attackers go home.\n611\t- The Clockwork Sanctum and the hub skirmish have their own rules (§6.10, §11).\n612\t\n613\t### 5.11 Seasons in battle (the Forseasons rules)\n614\t- **Seasonal Tide:** units whose element is the battle's season deal +15% (`tideBonus`) and take 10% less damage. Units\n615\t  of the opposed element deal −15%. Hour units ignore the Tide. Winter of Year 1 is the Long Winter: the Winter Tide is\n616\t  +30%.\n617\t- **Terrain transforms** apply when the battle is built (and at every bell in the hub skirmish): see the season column\n618\t  of §5.7. A map flagged `flood` turns its shallows to deep water in Spring, so bridges become the choke points.\n619\t- **Weather:** Spring rain gives −5 hit to ranged attacks. Summer is clear: Summer area spells set forests burning.\n620\t  Autumn gales give fliers −1 MOV. Winter's cold gives non-Winter units −5 hit.\n621\t- The HUD's season badge says all this in one line, and units affected show ▲ (Tide) or ▼ (against) on their cards.\n622\t\n623\t### 5.12 Forecast\n624\t`sim.forecast(unit, action, target, fromHex)` returns `{ hit, dmg: [min, max], crit, ko, status: [name, chance],\n625\telem: 'strong' | 'weak' | null, tide, captureRisk }` for each unit the action touches. The HUD shows it before every\n626\tconfirm (§8.5, item 14).\n627\t\n628\t### 5.13 Battle AI (`21-ai-battle.js`)\n629\t- **Per unit, in troop order:** first units that can cast or shoot without moving, then monsters nearest the enemy, and\n630\t  the knight last, so that its Ward covers the troop.\n631\t- For every reachable hex `h` (`grid.reach`, enemies blocked, allies passable) and every legal action and target from\n632\t  `h` (spells only from the start hex), score:\n633\t  - `+ Σ expected damage to foes × (1 + 0.5 × knight + 1.0 × ruler)`;\n634\t  - `+ expected KO bonus` (30, 70 for a knight, 110 for a ruler);\n635\t  - `− 1.5 × expected damage to friends`;\n636\t  - `+ 1.2 × healing × (knight ? 2 : 1)`;\n637\t  - `− danger(h) × (knight ? 1.5 : 0.6) × (HP < 40% ? 2 : 1)`, where `danger(h)` is the expected damage foes could deal\n638\t    at `h` next bell;\n639\t  - `− 12` if a monster ends outside its Ward;\n640\t  - `+ 10 × terrain DEF`;\n641\t  - objective terms: from bell 8, attackers `− 2 × distance(h, Keep)` and defending knights `− 3 × distance(h, Keep)`;\n642\t  - when no target is in reach: melee `− 1.2 × distance to the nearest foe`; ranged and casters `− 1.5 × |distance −\n643\t    3|`.\n644\t- Take the best score; ties go to the first in a fixed order.\n645\t- A non-ruler knight below 25% HP whose side is losing on power may Retreat. Rulers never retreat (their danger weight is\n646\t  ×3 instead).\n647\t- Easy picks among its top 3 (weights 3 : 2 : 1); Hard adds +15 for targets already damaged this bell.\n648\t- The same state always gives the same plan, so a bot running both sides is a repeatable test.\n649\t\n650\t### 5.14 Delegate (auto-resolve) and speed\n651\t- **Delegate** runs the same `BattleSim` with the AI on both sides to the end, in one synchronous loop with no drawing,\n652\t  and shows a summary card (losses, captures, level-ups).\n653\t- Animation speed comes from the setting (Full, Fast, Minimal). Holding ✕/Enter during AI turns plays at 4×.\n654\t\n655\t---\n656\t\n657\t## 6. Content\n658\t\n659\t### 6.1 The world: Forseason\n660\t- **Shape:** a round continent (radius about 470 world units) on a 1024 × 1024 map (64 × 64 tiles), with the sea all\n661\t  around it.\n662\t- **The centre:** the grey Hour plateau with Meridian, the Calendar City, whose great clock tower is visible from\n663\t  everywhere.\n664\t- **The four quarters, one realm each, each in its native season's look:**\n665\t  - north, Hoarfast: snowfields, pine forests, frozen lakes and the Rimewall mountains;\n666\t  - east, Verdance: green meadows, blossoming orchards, rivers and lakes, spring rain;\n667\t  - south, Solmark: golden savanna, red mesas, dunes and palms along the coast;\n668\t  - west, Amberlyn: amber farmland, oak woods, pumpkin fields, misty bogs and watermills.\n669\t- **The cross-quarter marches** (NE Thaw, SE Beltane, SW Lammas, NW Hallow) blend their two neighbours. Brigand free\n670\t  companies hold them.\n671\t- **The current season tints everything:** a dusting of snow in Winter, blossoms in Spring, gold in Summer, falling\n672\t  leaves in Autumn.\n673\t\n674\t### 6.2 Castles (positions in world units on the 1024 × 1024 map)\n675\t\n676\t| id | Name | Region | Tier | Start owner | Mana | Battle map | Summon circle (tier-1 species; a season in brackets means only then) | Quest site | Treasury | Pos |\n677\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n678\t| meridian | Meridian, the Calendar City | hour | capital | Dominion | 60 | meridian_clockyard | minute, clockwork, gearhound, stillwraith, pendulumwyrm | The Sleeping Court | Hourglass Rod | 512,512 |\n679\t| midnight | Midnight Keep | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | hill_fort | minute, stillwraith, gearhound | The Bell That Doesn't Ring | Writ of Knighthood | 512,392 |\n680\t| dawnwatch | Dawnwatch | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | hill_fort | minute, clockwork, gearhound | The Sunrise Stair | Swift Spurs | 632,512 |\n681\t| noonspire | Noonspire | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | crossroads | clockwork, gearhound, minute | The Shadowless Square | Signet of Command | 512,632 |\n682\t| vesperhall | Vesper Hall | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | ruined_abbey | stillwraith, minute, clockwork | The Evensong Crypt | Writ of Knighthood | 392,512 |\n683\t| rimeholt | Rimeholt | winter | capital | Hoarfast | 40 | capital_citadel | snowkit, frostwolf, icegolem, yeti, frostwyrm (Winter) | The Lake of Silent Bells | Frostplate | 512,92 |\n684\t| wolfsgate | Wolfsgate | winter | flank | Hoarfast | 20 | mountain_pass | frostwolf, snowkit, yeti | The Howling Scar | Winter Shard | 352,235 |\n685\t| frostmere | Frostmere | winter | flank | Hoarfast | 20 | lakeside | snowkit, icegolem, frostwolf | Nimue's Mere | Warding Charm | 672,235 |\n686\t| kestrel | Kestrel Spire | winter | inner | Hoarfast | 25 | forest_hold | frostwolf, yeti, snowkit | The Kestrel Eyrie | Yew Longbow | 512,277 |\n687\t| avalorn | Avalorn | spring | capital | Verdance | 40 | capital_citadel | sproutling, pixie, unicorn, treant, rillserpent (Spring) | The Queen's Orchard | Robe of Seasons | 932,512 |\n688\t| thornwick | Thornwick | spring | flank | Verdance | 20 | forest_hold | sproutling, treant, pixie | The Briar Maze | Thornmail | 789,352 |\n689\t| rainmere | Rainmere | spring | flank | Verdance | 20 | river_ford | rillserpent, sproutling, pixie | The Weeping Weir | Spring Seed | 789,672 |\n690\t| primrose | Primrose Ford | spring | inner | Verdance | 25 | lakeside | unicorn, pixie, sproutling | The Unicorn Glade | Tome of Thaw | 747,512 |\n691\t| brazenhold | Brazenhold | summer | capital | Solmark | 40 | capital_citadel | salamander, cinderhound, sunbird, sunmane, wyvern (Summer) | The Furnace Vaults | Sunforged Blade | 512,932 |\n692\t| goldspur | Goldspur | summer | flank | Solmark | 20 | crossroads | salamander, cinderhound, wyvern (Summer) | The Wyvern Roost | Summer Ember | 672,789 |\n693\t| cinderwall | Cinderwall | summer | flank | Solmark | 20 | mountain_pass | cinderhound, salamander, sunmane | The Ash Dunes | Mail Hauberk | 352,789 |\n694\t| lionsreach | Lionsreach | summer | inner | Solmark | 25 | hill_fort | sunmane, sunbird, cinderhound | The Lion Steps | Banner Pin | 512,747 |\n695\t| ambergate | Ambergate | autumn | capital | Amberlyn | 40 | capital_citadel | jacklamp, scarecrow, ghoul, tusker, griffin (Autumn) | The Harvest Vault | Lantern Staff | 92,512 |\n696\t| ashbarrow | Ashbarrow | autumn | flank | Amberlyn | 20 | ruined_abbey | ghoul, jacklamp, scarecrow | The Barrow Downs | Autumn Acorn | 235,352 |\n697\t| russetmoor | Russetmoor | autumn | flank | Amberlyn | 20 | marsh_keep | tusker, jacklamp, scarecrow | The Russet Bog | Lucky Horseshoe | 235,672 |\n698\t| lanternfall | Lanternfall | autumn | inner | Amberlyn | 25 | forest_hold | jacklamp, ghoul, scarecrow | The Lantern Road | Ring of Mending | 277,512 |\n699\t| thawgate | Thawgate | thaw (winter/spring) | cross | Brigands: Hob Mudspur | 30 | river_ford | snowkit, sproutling, slime, bat | The Breaking Ice | Golden Draught | 756,268 |\n700\t| beltane | Beltane Ford | beltane (spring/summer) | cross | Brigands: Mother Gerrow | 30 | marsh_keep | sproutling, salamander, slime, harpy | The Old Mill of Beltane | Amulet of Tides | 756,756 |\n701\t| lammas | Lammas Cross | lammas (summer/autumn) | cross | Brigands: Red Dafydd | 30 | crossroads | salamander, scarecrow, skeleton, ogre | The Lammas Fair | Thorn Whip | 268,756 |\n702\t| hallowmere | Hallowmere | hallow (autumn/winter) | cross | Brigands: the Hollow Abbot | 30 | ruined_abbey | jacklamp, snowkit, skeleton, bat | The Hollow Abbey Crypts | Hawthorn Bow | 268,268 |\n703\t\n704\tA battle map's dressing (tree kinds, palette, props, castle style) follows the castle's region; terrain then follows the\n705\tbattle's season (§5.11). A cross-quarter castle's season bonus applies in both of its seasons.\n706\t\n707\t### 6.3 Roads (36)\n708\t- **Hoarfast:** rimeholt–wolfsgate, rimeholt–frostmere, wolfsgate–kestrel, frostmere–kestrel.\n709\t- **Verdance:** avalorn–thornwick, avalorn–rainmere, thornwick–primrose, rainmere–primrose.\n710\t- **Solmark:** brazenhold–goldspur, brazenhold–cinderwall, goldspur–lionsreach, cinderwall–lionsreach.\n711\t- **Amberlyn:** ambergate–ashbarrow, ambergate–russetmoor, ashbarrow–lanternfall, russetmoor–lanternfall.\n712\t- **Cross-quarters:** thawgate–frostmere, thawgate–thornwick, beltane–rainmere, beltane–goldspur, lammas–cinderwall,\n713\t  lammas–russetmoor, hallowmere–ashbarrow, hallowmere–wolfsgate.\n714\t- **Into the Hourlands:** kestrel–midnight, primrose–dawnwatch, lionsreach–noonspire, lanternfall–vesperhall.\n715\t- **The Hour ring:** midnight–dawnwatch, dawnwatch–noonspire, noonspire–vesperhall, vesperhall–midnight.\n716\t- **To Meridian:** meridian–midnight, meridian–dawnwatch, meridian–noonspire, meridian–vesperhall.\n717\t\n718\tEvery realm has the same shape: a capital at the back, two flank castles that each face a brigand castle, and an inner\n719\tcastle that faces an Hour satellite. That keeps the realms fair. A test checks the graph is connected and symmetric.\n720\t\n721\t### 6.4 Realms\n722\t\n723\t| id | Realm | Season | Colours (main / trim) | Sigil | Banner | Ruler | Capital |\n724\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n725\t| verdance | Kingdom of Verdance | Spring | `#4caf50` / `#f0e6c8` | five-petal blossom | swallowtail | Prince Gareth Greenmantle | Avalorn |\n726\t| solmark | Sun-March of Solmark | Summer | `#e0a020` / `#b02a2a` | rayed sun | square | Queen Morgause the Brazen | Brazenhold |\n727\t| amberlyn | Harvest Throne of Amberlyn | Autumn | `#c86a1e` / `#5a3a2a` | oak leaf | pointed | King Pellam the Quiet | Ambergate |\n728\t| hoarfast | Duchy of Hoarfast | Winter | `#6ab0e8` / `#e8f4ff` | snowflake | triangle | Duke Mordrain the Frostbitten | Rimeholt |\n729\t| dominion | Hourless Dominion | Hour | `#3a3a46` / `#d8c070` | hourglass | long tapered | Lord Chancellor Meliant | Meridian |\n730\t| brigands | Free Companies | — | `#7a6a5a` / `#2a2a2a` | crossed axes | ragged | (four captains) | — |\n731\t\n732\tSides are never told apart by colour alone: every unit also carries its realm's sigil on a pennant over it, and the\n733\toutline colour, the banner shape and the sigil all agree.\n734\t\n735\t### 6.5 Knights\n736\tEach row gives the Humanoid look (§7.5) and the voice profile (§9.3). Each troop lists `species level`. Every realm's\n737\tcapital also starts with two tier-1 level-2 monsters in reserve: Verdance sproutlings, Solmark salamanders, Amberlyn\n738\tjack-o'-lamps and Hoarfast snowkits. Meridian starts with two level-10 minutes.\n739\t\n740\t#### 6.5.1 Verdance (Spring)\n741\t\n742\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n743\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n744\t| gareth | **Prince Gareth Greenmantle** (ruler) | Springwarden | 6 | Spring | Avalorn | unicorn 4, pixie 4, sproutling 4 | earnest, idealistic, quick to forgive; grieving his mother, the late Queen | heroic 1.25, armor, short golden hair, circlet, green cape, sword | bright tenor, quick |\n745\t| lynette | Dame Lynette of Thornwick | Squire | 7 | Spring | Thornwick | treant 4, sproutling 3 | his sworn shield; stern, dry humour, protective | heroic 1.2, armor, dark-red ponytail, band, white-and-green tabard | firm alto |\n746\t| pelleas | Sir Pelleas the Lovelorn | Archer | 5 | Spring | Primrose Ford | pixie 4, rillserpent 3 | a poet-archer, overdramatic and brave | heroic 1.15, tunic, long chestnut hair, cap | lilting, high |\n747\t| amris | Brother Amris | Acolyte | 6 | Winter | Avalorn | snowkit 3, sproutling 3 | an old monk from the north; gentle, wry | heroic 1.15, hunch .2, grey robe, bald, staff | slow, low |\n748\t| wren | Wren Ashfeather | Tamer | 5 | Spring | Rainmere | unicorn 3, pixie 3, sproutling 3 | raised among unicorns; few words | heroic 1.1, leaf-green tunic, ash-white spiky hair, hood | chirpy |\n749\t\n750\t#### 6.5.2 Solmark (Summer)\n751\t\n752\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n753\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n754\t| morgause | **Queen Morgause the Brazen** (ruler) | Sun Sovereign | 7 | Summer | Brazenhold | wyvern 4, cinderhound 4 | magnificent and war-loving, honourable on the field, ruthless at court | heroic 1.3, gold armor, crown, long copper hair, crimson cape, two-handed sword | commanding mezzo |\n755\t| agravain | Sir Agravain Cinderjaw | Squire | 7 | Summer | Cinderwall | cinderhound 4, salamander 3 | a hothead champion who craves glory | bulky 1.25, armor, helmet, red cape | growly baritone |\n756\t| elidure | Captain Elidure of Goldspur | Archer | 6 | Summer | Goldspur | sunbird 3, salamander 3 | disciplined, loyal and secretly kind | heroic 1.2, sand coat, black ponytail, band | clear soprano |\n757\t| hesper | Magus Hesper Vey | Adept | 6 | Hour | Lionsreach | salamander 3, minute 3 | an ambitious court sorcerer who dabbles in Hour magic | heroic 1.2, purple-and-gold robe, pointed hat, long silver hair | silky |\n758\t| brennoc | Old Brennoc | Tamer | 5 | Summer | Brazenhold | sunmane 3, cinderhound 3 | a grizzled, grandfatherly beastkeeper | bulky 1.2, hunch .3, leather coat, bald, whip | gravelly |\n759\t\n760\t#### 6.5.3 Amberlyn (Autumn)\n761\t\n762\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n763\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n764\t| pellam | **King Pellam the Quiet** (ruler) | Harvest King | 8 | Autumn | Ambergate | griffin 4, scarecrow 4 | silent and wise; speaks rarely and briefly; secretly ill | heroic 1.2, hunch .25, amber-and-umber robe, crown, long white hair, staff | soft, low, slow |\n765\t| enid | Lady Enid Russet | Acolyte | 6 | Autumn | Ambergate | jacklamp 3, scarecrow 3 | the king's daughter; gentle, firm, practical | heroic 1.15, cream-and-russet robe, long auburn hair, band | warm |\n766\t| dagonet | Sir Dagonet the Motley | Squire | 5 | Autumn | Russetmoor | tusker 3, jacklamp 3 | a jester-knight who jokes to hide his fear | heroic 1.1, two-colour tunic, pointed hat, sword | bouncy |\n767\t| vesna | Vesna of the Lanterns | Adept | 6 | Summer | Lanternfall | jacklamp 4, ghoul 3 | a lamplighter witch, kind to the dead | heroic 1.15, black-and-orange robe, pointed hat, long black hair | breathy |\n768\t| lamorak | Sir Lamorak Ashbarrow | Squire | 8 | Autumn | Ashbarrow | ghoul 4, scarecrow 3 | a gruff old veteran, loyal to Pellam | bulky 1.2, rusty armor, helmet, brown cape | gruff |\n769\t\n770\t#### 6.5.4 Hoarfast (Winter)\n771\t\n772\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n773\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n774\t| mordrain | **Duke Mordrain the Frostbitten** (ruler) | Rime Duke | 7 | Winter | Rimeholt | frostwyrm 3, snowkit 4 | theatrical, mad and brilliant; speaks in riddles; grief hidden under ice | heroic 1.25, white coat, icicle crown, long white hair, staff, pale-blue cape, faint eyeGlow | high, erratic pitch |\n775\t| ragnell | Dame Ragnell Ice-Eye | Squire | 8 | Winter | Kestrel Spire | frostwolf 4, icegolem 3 | his cold, calculating marshal, the sane one | heroic 1.25, steel armor, helmet, white ponytail, dark-blue cape | flat alto |\n776\t| safir | Sir Safir the Pale | Archer | 6 | Winter | Wolfsgate | frostwolf 3, snowkit 3 | a quiet, melancholic hunter | heroic 1.2, white hood, grey coat | soft |\n777\t| nimue | Nimue of Frostmere | Adept | 7 | Winter | Frostmere | snowkit 4, snowkit 3 | an enigmatic lake witch who makes bargains | heroic 1.15, teal robe, long pale-blue hair | echoing |\n778\t| gorm | Gorm the Bear | Tamer | 5 | Autumn | Rimeholt | yeti 3, tusker 3 | huge and gentle; raised in the western woods | bulky 1.35, brown fur coat, short hair, whip | very low |\n779\t\n780\t#### 6.5.5 The Hourless Dominion (Hour)\n781\t\n782\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n783\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n784\t| meliant | **Lord Chancellor Meliant** (ruler) | Chancellor of Hours | 14 | Meridian | pendulumwyrm 10, clockwork (tier 2: Tick Knight) 12, stillwraith 12 | cold, grieving and absolute; believes he is merciful | heroic 1.25, black-and-brass robe, brass band, short grey hair, brass rod | measured baritone |\n785\t| bertilak | Marshal Bertilak the Hourward | Knight | 12 | Midnight Keep | clockwork (tier 2) 12, gearhound 10, gearhound 9 | courteous, ruthless; loves a duel | bulky 1.3, brass armor, helmet, green-black cape | booming |\n786\t| aurelie | Countess Aurelie of Vespers | Sorcerer | 12 | Vesper Hall | stillwraith 10, minute 10, minute 9 | elegant, bored and cruel | heroic 1.2, violet-and-black robe, long black hair, band | drawling |\n787\t| morholt | Sir Morholt the Unmoving | Knight | 11 | Noonspire | clockwork 10, clockwork 9 | a silent giant | bulky 1.45, black armor, helmet | grunts only |\n788\t| tic | Tic | Ranger | 10 | Dawnwatch | gearhound 9, minute 9 | a clockwork twin who finishes Tac's sentences | chibi 1.0, brass armor, cap | squeaky, high |\n789\t| tac | Tac | Ranger | 10 | Dawnwatch | gearhound 9, minute 9 | the other twin | the same, colours swapped | squeaky, low |\n790\t| graynight | **The Gray Knight, Sir Nonesuch** | Knight of the Thirteenth Hour | 25 | the Sanctum only | minute (tier 3) 22 ×4, pendulumwyrm (tier 2) 22 | the month that never was: calm, ancient, faintly amused | heroic 1.6, grey armor, helmet, tattered grey cape, white eyeGlow, long sword, clock-hand halo | two detuned low voices |\n791\t\n792\tThe Gray Knight's stats are fixed: HP 900, MP 200, ATK 52, DEF 48, INT 50, AGI 30, MOV 5. His skills are Thirteenth\n793\tStroke, Still, Unmaking and Timeless.\n794\t\n795\t#### 6.5.6 Free knights (joined by event or quest)\n796\t\n797\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | How they join | Brings | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n798\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n799\t| lunete | Princess Lunete of Meridian | Hourmaiden | 8 | Hour | the Lunete chain (§6.12) | — | the Keeper's daughter; steady and kind; carries her father's broken watch | heroic 1.15, white-and-brass robe, long gold hair, band | clear, gentle |\n800\t| galeron | Sir Galeron the Wanderer | Knight | 10 | Spring | Wanderer outcome at Winter or Spring sites, from Autumn of Year 1 | frostwolf 8 | an errant knight looking for a cause | heroic 1.25, dented armor, faded green cape | weary tenor |\n801\t| blanchefleur | Blanchefleur the Sellsword | Ranger | 10 | Autumn | Wanderer at Summer or Autumn sites, or the Lammas Fair (pay 150 mana) | sunmane 8 | a mercenary with a code: coin first | heroic 1.2, red-brown coat, short blonde hair | brisk |\n802\t| owain | Owain the Dragonless | Beastlord | 11 | Summer | event `owain`: the first time your realm binds a wyvern or frost wyrm | — | lost his dragon in the Long Winter; will train yours | bulky 1.25, leather coat, short hair | husky |\n803\t| ettard | Sister Ettard | Priest | 10 | Winter | Wanderer at Hallowmere, Lanternfall or Frostmere | snowkit 7 | a sharp-tongued healer | heroic 1.15, white-and-blue robe, hood | crisp |\n804\t\n805\t#### 6.5.7 Brigand captains (Brigand Captain class)\n806\t\n807\t| id | Name | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are |\n808\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n809\t| hob | Hob Mudspur | 5 | Winter | Thawgate | snowkit 4, frostwolf 4, bat 3, slime 3 | swaggering, and a coward at heart |\n810\t| gerrow | Mother Gerrow | 5 | Spring | Beltane Ford | slime 4, harpy 4, sproutling 3, bat 3 | motherly and crafty; hides Lunete at her mill |\n811\t| dafydd | Red Dafydd | 6 | Summer | Lammas Cross | ogre 4, skeleton 4, salamander 3 | boisterous and proud |\n812\t| abbot | The Hollow Abbot | 6 | Autumn | Hallowmere | skeleton 5, ghoul 4, bat 4 | eerie and sorrowful; keeps the dead company |\n813\t\n814\t### 6.6 Knight classes\n815\t\n816\t**Stat rule:**\n817\t- At tier 1, `stat(L) = base + growth × (L − 1)`.\n818\t- At a class change, every stat (MP included) is multiplied by 1.10.\n819\t- After that, growth is ×1.15 (tier 2) or ×1.30 (tier 3) of the line's tier-1 growth.\n820\t- Knights who start at tier 2 or 3 are built the same way with expected values, as if they changed class at levels 10\n821\t  and 20.\n822\t- Bond = base + floor(level / 4). MOV and Ward come from the class.\n823\t\n824\t| id | Class | Line, tier | Weapons | Basic attack | MOV | Ward | Bond | Base at Lv 1: HP/MP/ATK/DEF/INT/AGI | Growth per level | Skills (level) | Next |\n825\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n826\t| squire | Squire | Warrior 1 | sword, spear, axe | Slash 1.0, range 1 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 70/8/17/15/7/11 | 7/.6/1.6/1.4/.4/.9 | Rally (3) | knight at 10 |\n827\t| knight | Knight | Warrior 2 | sword, spear, axe | Slash | 5 | 3 | 7 | ×1.1 at change | ×1.15 | Charge (10), Shield Wall (14) | paladin at 20 + Writ |\n828\t| paladin | Paladin | Warrior 3 | sword, spear | Slash | 5 | 3 | 9 | ×1.1 | ×1.30 | Holy Strike (20), Lay on Hands (24) | — |\n829\t| archer | Archer | Ranger 1 | bow | Shoot 0.9, range 2–4 | 5 | 2 | 4 | 58/10/16/10/9/15 | 5.5/.8/1.5/.9/.6/1.3 | Aimed Shot (4) | ranger at 10 |\n830\t| ranger | Ranger | Ranger 2 | bow | Shoot | 5 | 3 | 6 | | | Volley (10), Pinning Shot (14) | sentinel at 20 + Writ |\n831\t| sentinel | Sentinel | Ranger 3 | bow | Shoot, range 2–5 | 5 | 3 | 7 | | | Piercing Arrow (20), Eagle Eye (24) | — |\n832\t| adept | Adept | Mage 1 | staff, tome | Strike 0.6, range 1 | 4 | 2 | 4 | 50/30/8/8/18/11 | 4.5/2.2/.5/.7/1.8/.9 | own element's Bolt (1), Hex (6) | sorcerer at 10 |\n833\t| sorcerer | Sorcerer | Mage 2 | staff, tome | Strike | 4 | 3 | 6 | | | Storm (10), Mana Siphon (14) | archmage at 20 + Writ |\n834\t| archmage | Archmage | Mage 3 | staff, tome | Strike | 4 | 3 | 7 | | | Tempest (20), Haste (24) | — |\n835\t| acolyte | Acolyte | Cleric 1 | mace, staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 55/26/10/10/15/10 | 5/2/.7/.9/1.5/.8 | Mend (1), Purify (5) | priest at 10 |\n836\t| priest | Priest | Cleric 2 | mace, staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 3 | 7 | | | Renewal (10), Ward of Seasons (14) | hierophant at 20 + Writ |\n837\t| hierophant | Hierophant | Cleric 3 | staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 4 | 8 | | | Greater Renewal (20), Dawnlight (24) | — |\n838\t| tamer | Tamer | Beast 1 | whip, spear | Lash 0.8, range 1–2 | 5 | 3 | 7 | 62/12/14/12/10/13 | 6/.9/1.2/1.1/.7/1.1 | Goad (3) | beastlord at 10 |\n839\t| beastlord | Beastlord | Beast 2 | whip, spear | Lash | 5 | 4 | 10 | | | Pack Tactics (10), Roar (14) | beastsovereign at 20 + Writ |\n840\t| beastsovereign | Beast Sovereign | Beast 3 | spear, whip | Lash | 5 | 4 | 13 | | | Call of the Wild (20), Bond of Fang (24) | — |\n841\t| springwarden | Springwarden | ruler | sword | Slash 1.0 | 5 | 4 | 10 | 75/22/17/15/15/14 | 7/1.5/1.5/1.3/1.3/1.1 | Mend (1), Charge (1), Verdant Oath (6), Bramble Storm (10), Verdant Tempest (16) | — |\n842\t| sunsovereign | Sun Sovereign | ruler | greatsword | Cleave 1.1 | 5 | 4 | 11 | 85/14/21/16/10/12 | 8/1/1.9/1.4/.8/1 | Charge (1), Warcry (6), Cinder Storm (10), Solar Flare (16) | — |\n843\t| harvestking | Harvest King | ruler | staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 5 | 10 | 68/30/11/13/20/10 | 6/2/.8/1.2/1.8/.8 | Mend (1), Gale of Leaves (1), Quiet Counsel (6), Harvest Moon (12), Reaping (16) | — |\n844\t| rimeduke | Rime Duke | ruler | staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 4 | 10 | 70/28/15/13/19/13 | 6.5/1.8/1.3/1.1/1.7/1 | Hoarfrost (1), Mad Gambit (6), Frost Storm (10), Frozen Hour (12), Blizzard (16) | — |\n845\t| chancellor | Chancellor of Hours | ruler | rod | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 4 | 12 | 80/34/12/15/22/12 | 7/2/1/1.4/1.9/.9 | Time Shear (1), Stop (1), Restore (6), Hour Storm (10) | — |\n846\t| hourmaiden | Hourmaiden | unique | staff | Strike 0.8 | 5 | 3 | 6 | 58/34/9/11/19/15 | 5/2.2/.6/1/1.8/1.2 | Mend (1), Haste (1), Turning (8) | — |\n847\t| graynight | Knight of the Thirteenth Hour | boss | long sword | Slash 1.2 | 5 | 5 | — | fixed (§6.5.5) | — | Thirteenth Stroke, Still, Unmaking, Timeless | — |\n848\t| brigand | Brigand Captain | unique | axe | Hack 1.05 | 5 | 3 | 8 | 72/6/18/13/6/12 | 7/.4/1.6/1.2/.3/1 | Charge (1), Ambush (1) | — |\n849\t\n850\t**A knight's element picks its spells.** \"Bolt\", \"Hex\", \"Storm\" and \"Tempest\" mean that element's spell of that tier\n851\t(§6.7). An Adept of Winter learns Hoarfrost, then Frostbite.\n852\t\n853\t### 6.7 Skills and spells\n854\tAreas:\n855\t- `single`;\n856\t- `r1` / `r2`: the target hex plus every hex within 1 or 2 of it;\n857\t- `self-r1` / `self-r2`: around the user;\n858\t- `adj`: the 6 hexes around the user;\n859\t- `cone2` / `cone3`: hexes within 2 or 3 of the user, inside a 120° wedge facing one of the 6 directions;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"fd313f85-557e-4690-9439-90368b576b0e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:02:34.889Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/PLAN.md","content":"- The field is flat (z = 0). Height comes from terrain types and props, as in the source's flat hex maps. Raised blocks\n  (ramparts, gears, cliffs) are impassable shapes (§7.2).\n\n### 5.2 Sides and deployment\n- Two sides, attacker and defender, each with up to 3 troops. A troop is one knight and up to 6 monsters.\n- Troop anchors are hexes `1 2 3` (attacker) and `7 8 9` (defender). The defender's first troop takes the anchor next to\n  the Keep. Skirmish and hub maps use seat anchors `1 2 3 4`.\n- The knight stands on the anchor, and its monsters fill the free hexes nearest it according to its formation:\n  - **Vanguard:** hexes 1–2 steps toward the enemy's side first.\n  - **Shield:** the ring around the knight first.\n  - **Column:** a line behind the knight, away from the enemy.\n- Units face the enemy side.\n\n### 5.3 Bells and turn order\n- A battle lasts up to `tune.bells` (12) bells.\n- Each bell, troops act in order of their knight's AGI (descending; ties go to the defender, then the lower troop id).\n- In a troop's turn, each of its units acts once, in any order its controller likes. The troop ends when all have acted\n  or its controller ends it (the rest Wait). A troop whose knight has fallen is gone.\n- **At the end of each bell:**\n  1. effects tick (§5.8);\n  2. the Keep heals its owner's unit standing on it by 10% of max HP;\n  3. map rules run (the Sanctum's Hands and Dials, §6.10; the hub's season advance, §11);\n  4. the win checks run (§5.10).\n- Each new bell tolls a bell sound and the clock face's hand moves.\n\n### 5.4 A unit's turn\n- **Move:** up to MOV, paying terrain costs (§5.7). A unit can't enter or pass enemies, can pass allies, and can't end\n  on an occupied hex. Before acting, a move can be undone with Back.\n- **Then one action, or one action with no move:**\n\n| Action | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Attack | the unit's basic attack (range and power from its spec); allowed after moving |\n| Special | a skill of kind `special`; after moving only if it is *mobile*; some (Charge, Dive) require moving at least 2 hexes this turn |\n| Spell | a skill of kind `spell`; **only if the unit has not moved this turn** |\n| Item | knights only: a consumable from the realm inventory, on itself or an adjacent ally |\n| Guard | +30% DEF and +10 evasion until its next turn; allowed after moving |\n| Retreat | knights only: the troop leaves the field at once (capture rolls, §5.9). A ruler's retreat loses the battle |\n| Wait | end the unit's turn |\n\n- MP: skills cost MP. Each unit regains 2 MP at its troop's turn start.\n\n### 5.5 Stats\n- HP, MP, ATK, DEF, INT (magic power and magic defense), AGI (evasion, hit, crit, turn order) and MOV.\n- Tags: element (Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter or Hour), size (S, M, L), and flags: flier (ignores terrain cost and may\n  cross blocked hexes but not end on ramparts), swimmer (water costs 1, deep water is walkable), floater (swamp and\n  shallows cost 1).\n- Knights also have Bond and Ward radius (§6.6).\n- Levels run from 1 to 40, and 100 EXP gives a level, applied at once with a popup.\n\n### 5.6 Formulas (every constant is in `G.tune`, Appendix A)\n- **Ward:** a monster outside its own knight's Ward (hex distance > radius) has ATK, DEF and INT × (1 − `wardPenalty`\n  0.20).\n- **Hit chance (physical):** `clamp(baseHit 85 + (A.AGI − D.AGI) + sizeHit[A.size][D.size] + flank − terrainEvade(D) −\n  5 × max(0, dist − 2) − weather − (D guarding ? 10 : 0), 15, 99)`.\n  - `sizeHit` (attacker row, target column S / M / L): S: 0 / 0 / +10; M: −10 / 0 / +10; L: −30 / −10 / 0 (the L row\n    is `tune.largeVsSmall`).\n  - `flank` = +5 for each other unit of A's side adjacent to D, at most +15.\n- **Physical damage:** `max(1, round((A.ATK × P − D.DEF × defFactor 0.5) × dmgScale × elem × tide × terrainDef × guard ×\n  surround × crit × var))`.\n  - P is the attack's power (a basic attack is 1.0).\n  - `elem` is 1.30 (`elemStrong`) when A's element opposes D's (Spring ↔ Autumn, Summer ↔ Winter), 0.80 (`elemSame`)\n    when they match, and 1.0 otherwise. Hour is 1.0 both ways, except anti-Hour skills (§6.7).\n  - `tide` = attacker factor × target factor, from §5.11.\n  - `terrainDef` = 1 − D's terrain DEF bonus. `guard` = 0.7 if D guards.\n  - `surround` = 1 + 0.10 × (A's allies adjacent to D, at most 3).\n  - `crit` = 1.5 with chance `critBase` 3% + A.AGI / 4 % (at most 30%).\n  - `var` is uniform between 0.9 and 1.1.\n- **Magic damage (always hits):** `max(1, round((P + A.INT − D.INT × 0.5) × magicScale × elem × tide × var))`, where P\n  is the spell's power (14, 22 or 34 for bolts, storms and tempests). Areas hit everyone in the shape, friends included.\n- **Breath, cone and line specials** use the physical formula, always hit, and apply the element.\n- **Healing:** `round((P + A.INT × 0.8) × healScale)`.\n- **Status chance:** `clamp(base + A.INT − D.INT, 10, 90) × statusScale`. Bosses halve it; the Warding Charm makes its\n  wearer immune to Sleep and Stop.\n- **EXP:**\n  - per damaging hit: `clamp(8 + 2 × (D.level − A.level), 2, 30) × expScale`;\n  - a KO: +20 (a knight +40, a ruler +60);\n  - a heal or buff: +8;\n  - at the end: +10 for each survivor of the winning side, +4 for the losing side.\n- **Level-up growth:** for each stat, `floor(g)` plus 1 more if a seeded roll falls under `g − floor(g)`.\n\n### 5.7 Terrain\n\n| Code | Terrain | Move cost | DEF | Evade | Season transform and notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `.` | plain | 1 | 0 | 0 | Winter → snow |\n| `,` | road | 1 | 0 | 0 | — |\n| `f` | forest | 2 (L: 3; fliers 1) | +20% | +10 | Summer: burns under Summer area spells; Autumn: +10% DEF only (leaf-fall) |\n| `h` | hill | 2 (fliers 1) | +10% | +5 | ranged attacks from a hill get +1 range; melee from a hill +10% damage |\n| `m` | mountain | blocked (fliers 1) | +20% (a perched flier) | +10 | — |\n| `~` | shallows | 2 (swimmers and fliers 1) | −10% | −10 | Spring on flood maps → deep water; Summer: cost 1; Winter → ice |\n| `w` | deep water | blocked (swimmers and fliers 1) | 0 | 0 | Winter → ice |\n| `L` | lake | as deep water | 0 | 0 | Winter → ice (a frozen lake opens the map) |\n| `s` | swamp | 3 (fliers and floaters 1) | −10% | −10 | Summer → plain (dried); Winter: cost 2 |\n| `F` | field | 1 | 0 | 0 | Summer: tall wheat, +10 evade; Autumn: stubble; Winter → snow |\n| `r` | ruins | 1 | +10% | +5 | — |\n| `#` | rampart, gear or building | blocked (fliers may cross but not end there) | — | — | drawn as a raised hex block (§7.2) |\n| `g` | courtyard or gate | 1 | +10% | 0 | — |\n| `b` | bridge | 1 | 0 | 0 | — |\n| `K` | Keep | 1 | +25% for its owner | 0 | owner heals 10% per bell on it; the attacker's seize objective |\n| `D` | season dial | 1 | 0 | 0 | the Sanctum only (§6.10) |\n| — | snow | 2 for non-Winter walkers, 1 for Winter units and fliers | 0 | 0 | from plain or field in Winter |\n| — | ice | 1 | 0 | −10 | from water in Winter; non-Winter units on ice −10 hit |\n| — | burning forest | 2 | 0 | 0 | lasts 2 bells; a unit starting its turn there takes 10% max HP; then it becomes ash |\n| — | ash | 1 | 0 | 0 | after burning |\n\n### 5.8 Effects (statuses, buffs and debuffs)\n\n| Effect | Kind | Rule | Lasts |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Poison | status | −8% max HP at its troop's turn start | 3 bells |\n| Burn | status | −5% max HP at turn start, DEF −10% | 2 bells |\n| Chill | status | MOV −1, AGI −20% | 2 bells |\n| Sleep | status | skips its turns; wakes when damaged | 2 bells |\n| Stop | status | skips its next turn, then is immune to Stop for 1 bell | 1 turn |\n| Valor | buff | ATK +20% | 2 bells |\n| Haste | buff | MOV +1, AGI +20% | 2 bells |\n| Warded | buff | DEF +20%, and magic damage taken −20% | 2 bells |\n| Guarded | buff | the Guard action (§5.4) | until its next turn |\n| Weakened | debuff | ATK −15% | 2 bells |\n| Exposed | debuff | DEF −20% | 2 bells |\n\nA unit holds one copy of each effect; reapplying refreshes the duration. Remedy and Purify clear statuses and debuffs.\n\n### 5.9 Knights falling, retreat, capture and death\n- When a knight drops to 0 HP or retreats, its troop leaves the field. Each of its monsters still standing rolls for\n  capture if it is adjacent to an enemy knight or inside an enemy knight's Ward:\n  - chance = `captureBase` 25% + 25% if it was outside its own knight's Ward + 15% if below 30% HP, at most 75%;\n  - bosses and Hour elites (Pendulum Wyrm forms) never roll;\n  - a captured monster is taken by the nearest enemy knight (shown with a chain of light). After the battle it joins\n    the winner's reserve at the contested castle if its captor's side won, or the reserve of the captor's home castle\n    if it lost;\n  - every other monster retreats with its knight.\n- If a ruler falls or retreats, every knight on its side retreats at once and the side loses.\n- Monsters at 0 HP die and are gone for good (the Phoenix's Rebirth is the exception, §6.8). Knights at 0 HP are wounded\n  for the next season.\n\n### 5.10 Winning\n- A side loses the moment it has no knights on the field.\n- At the end of the last bell, the attacker wins if one of its knights stands on a Keep hex; otherwise the defender wins\n  and the attackers go home.\n- The Clockwork Sanctum and the hub skirmish have their own rules (§6.10, §11).\n\n### 5.11 Seasons in battle (the Forseasons rules)\n- **Seasonal Tide:** units whose element is the battle's season deal +15% (`tideBonus`) and take 10% less damage. Units\n  of the opposed element deal −15%. Hour units ignore the Tide. Winter of Year 1 is the Long Winter: the Winter Tide is\n  +30%.\n- **Terrain transforms** apply when the battle is built (and at every bell in the hub skirmish): see the season column\n  of §5.7. A map flagged `flood` turns its shallows to deep water in Spring, so bridges become the choke points.\n- **Weather:** Spring rain gives −5 hit to ranged attacks. Summer is clear: Summer area spells set forests burning.\n  Autumn gales give fliers −1 MOV. Winter's cold gives non-Winter units −5 hit.\n- The HUD's season badge says all this in one line, and units affected show ▲ (Tide) or ▼ (against) on their cards.\n\n### 5.12 Forecast\n`sim.forecast(unit, action, target, fromHex)` returns `{ hit, dmg: [min, max], crit, ko, status: [name, chance],\nelem: 'strong' | 'weak' | null, tide, captureRisk }` for each unit the action touches. The HUD shows it before every\nconfirm (§8.5, item 14).\n\n### 5.13 Battle AI (`21-ai-battle.js`)\n- **Per unit, in troop order:** first units that can cast or shoot without moving, then monsters nearest the enemy, and\n  the knight last, so that its Ward covers the troop.\n- For every reachable hex `h` (`grid.reach`, enemies blocked, allies passable) and every legal action and target from\n  `h` (spells only from the start hex), score:\n  - `+ Σ expected damage to foes × (1 + 0.5 × knight + 1.0 × ruler)`;\n  - `+ expected KO bonus` (30, 70 for a knight, 110 for a ruler);\n  - `− 1.5 × expected damage to friends`;\n  - `+ 1.2 × healing × (knight ? 2 : 1)`;\n  - `− danger(h) × (knight ? 1.5 : 0.6) × (HP < 40% ? 2 : 1)`, where `danger(h)` is the expected damage foes could deal\n    at `h` next bell;\n  - `− 12` if a monster ends outside its Ward;\n  - `+ 10 × terrain DEF`;\n  - objective terms: from bell 8, attackers `− 2 × distance(h, Keep)` and defending knights `− 3 × distance(h, Keep)`;\n  - when no target is in reach: melee `− 1.2 × distance to the nearest foe`; ranged and casters `− 1.5 × |distance −\n    3|`.\n- Take the best score; ties go to the first in a fixed order.\n- A non-ruler knight below 25% HP whose side is losing on power may Retreat. Rulers never retreat (their danger weight is\n  ×3 instead).\n- Easy picks among its top 3 (weights 3 : 2 : 1); Hard adds +15 for targets already damaged this bell.\n- The same state always gives the same plan, so a bot running both sides is a repeatable test.\n\n### 5.14 Delegate (auto-resolve) and speed\n- **Delegate** runs the same `BattleSim` with the AI on both sides to the end, in one synchronous loop with no drawing,\n  and shows a summary card (losses, captures, level-ups).\n- Animation speed comes from the setting (Full, Fast, Minimal). Holding ✕/Enter during AI turns plays at 4×.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Content\n\n### 6.1 The world: Forseason\n- **Shape:** a round continent (radius about 470 world units) on a 1024 × 1024 map (64 × 64 tiles), with the sea all\n  around it.\n- **The centre:** the grey Hour plateau with Meridian, the Calendar City, whose great clock tower is visible from\n  everywhere.\n- **The four quarters, one realm each, each in its native season's look:**\n  - north, Hoarfast: snowfields, pine forests, frozen lakes and the Rimewall mountains;\n  - east, Verdance: green meadows, blossoming orchards, rivers and lakes, spring rain;\n  - south, Solmark: golden savanna, red mesas, dunes and palms along the coast;\n  - west, Amberlyn: amber farmland, oak woods, pumpkin fields, misty bogs and watermills.\n- **The cross-quarter marches** (NE Thaw, SE Beltane, SW Lammas, NW Hallow) blend their two neighbours. Brigand free\n  companies hold them.\n- **The current season tints everything:** a dusting of snow in Winter, blossoms in Spring, gold in Summer, falling\n  leaves in Autumn.\n\n### 6.2 Castles (positions in world units on the 1024 × 1024 map)\n\n| id | Name | Region | Tier | Start owner | Mana | Battle map | Summon circle (tier-1 species; a season in brackets means only then) | Quest site | Treasury | Pos |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| meridian | Meridian, the Calendar City | hour | capital | Dominion | 60 | meridian_clockyard | minute, clockwork, gearhound, stillwraith, pendulumwyrm | The Sleeping Court | Hourglass Rod | 512,512 |\n| midnight | Midnight Keep | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | hill_fort | minute, stillwraith, gearhound | The Bell That Doesn't Ring | Writ of Knighthood | 512,392 |\n| dawnwatch | Dawnwatch | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | hill_fort | minute, clockwork, gearhound | The Sunrise Stair | Swift Spurs | 632,512 |\n| noonspire | Noonspire | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | crossroads | clockwork, gearhound, minute | The Shadowless Square | Signet of Command | 512,632 |\n| vesperhall | Vesper Hall | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | ruined_abbey | stillwraith, minute, clockwork | The Evensong Crypt | Writ of Knighthood | 392,512 |\n| rimeholt | Rimeholt | winter | capital | Hoarfast | 40 | capital_citadel | snowkit, frostwolf, icegolem, yeti, frostwyrm (Winter) | The Lake of Silent Bells | Frostplate | 512,92 |\n| wolfsgate | Wolfsgate | winter | flank | Hoarfast | 20 | mountain_pass | frostwolf, snowkit, yeti | The Howling Scar | Winter Shard | 352,235 |\n| frostmere | Frostmere | winter | flank | Hoarfast | 20 | lakeside | snowkit, icegolem, frostwolf | Nimue's Mere | Warding Charm | 672,235 |\n| kestrel | Kestrel Spire | winter | inner | Hoarfast | 25 | forest_hold | frostwolf, yeti, snowkit | The Kestrel Eyrie | Yew Longbow | 512,277 |\n| avalorn | Avalorn | spring | capital | Verdance | 40 | capital_citadel | sproutling, pixie, unicorn, treant, rillserpent (Spring) | The Queen's Orchard | Robe of Seasons | 932,512 |\n| thornwick | Thornwick | spring | flank | Verdance | 20 | forest_hold | sproutling, treant, pixie | The Briar Maze | Thornmail | 789,352 |\n| rainmere | Rainmere | spring | flank | Verdance | 20 | river_ford | rillserpent, sproutling, pixie | The Weeping Weir | Spring Seed | 789,672 |\n| primrose | Primrose Ford | spring | inner | Verdance | 25 | lakeside | unicorn, pixie, sproutling | The Unicorn Glade | Tome of Thaw | 747,512 |\n| brazenhold | Brazenhold | summer | capital | Solmark | 40 | capital_citadel | salamander, cinderhound, sunbird, sunmane, wyvern (Summer) | The Furnace Vaults | Sunforged Blade | 512,932 |\n| goldspur | Goldspur | summer | flank | Solmark | 20 | crossroads | salamander, cinderhound, wyvern (Summer) | The Wyvern Roost | Summer Ember | 672,789 |\n| cinderwall | Cinderwall | summer | flank | Solmark | 20 | mountain_pass | cinderhound, salamander, sunmane | The Ash Dunes | Mail Hauberk | 352,789 |\n| lionsreach | Lionsreach | summer | inner | Solmark | 25 | hill_fort | sunmane, sunbird, cinderhound | The Lion Steps | Banner Pin | 512,747 |\n| ambergate | Ambergate | autumn | capital | Amberlyn | 40 | capital_citadel | jacklamp, scarecrow, ghoul, tusker, griffin (Autumn) | The Harvest Vault | Lantern Staff | 92,512 |\n| ashbarrow | Ashbarrow | autumn | flank | Amberlyn | 20 | ruined_abbey | ghoul, jacklamp, scarecrow | The Barrow Downs | Autumn Acorn | 235,352 |\n| russetmoor | Russetmoor | autumn | flank | Amberlyn | 20 | marsh_keep | tusker, jacklamp, scarecrow | The Russet Bog | Lucky Horseshoe | 235,672 |\n| lanternfall | Lanternfall | autumn | inner | Amberlyn | 25 | forest_hold | jacklamp, ghoul, scarecrow | The Lantern Road | Ring of Mending | 277,512 |\n| thawgate | Thawgate | thaw (winter/spring) | cross | Brigands: Hob Mudspur | 30 | river_ford | snowkit, sproutling, slime, bat | The Breaking Ice | Golden Draught | 756,268 |\n| beltane | Beltane Ford | beltane (spring/summer) | cross | Brigands: Mother Gerrow | 30 | marsh_keep | sproutling, salamander, slime, harpy | The Old Mill of Beltane | Amulet of Tides | 756,756 |\n| lammas | Lammas Cross | lammas (summer/autumn) | cross | Brigands: Red Dafydd | 30 | crossroads | salamander, scarecrow, skeleton, ogre | The Lammas Fair | Thorn Whip | 268,756 |\n| hallowmere | Hallowmere | hallow (autumn/winter) | cross | Brigands: the Hollow Abbot | 30 | ruined_abbey | jacklamp, snowkit, skeleton, bat | The Hollow Abbey Crypts | Hawthorn Bow | 268,268 |\n\nA battle map's dressing (tree kinds, palette, props, castle style) follows the castle's region; terrain then follows the\nbattle's season (§5.11). A cross-quarter castle's season bonus applies in both of its seasons.\n\n### 6.3 Roads (36)\n- **Hoarfast:** rimeholt–wolfsgate, rimeholt–frostmere, wolfsgate–kestrel, frostmere–kestrel.\n- **Verdance:** avalorn–thornwick, avalorn–rainmere, thornwick–primrose, rainmere–primrose.\n- **Solmark:** brazenhold–goldspur, brazenhold–cinderwall, goldspur–lionsreach, cinderwall–lionsreach.\n- **Amberlyn:** ambergate–ashbarrow, ambergate–russetmoor, ashbarrow–lanternfall, russetmoor–lanternfall.\n- **Cross-quarters:** thawgate–frostmere, thawgate–thornwick, beltane–rainmere, beltane–goldspur, lammas–cinderwall,\n  lammas–russetmoor, hallowmere–ashbarrow, hallowmere–wolfsgate.\n- **Into the Hourlands:** kestrel–midnight, primrose–dawnwatch, lionsreach–noonspire, lanternfall–vesperhall.\n- **The Hour ring:** midnight–dawnwatch, dawnwatch–noonspire, noonspire–vesperhall, vesperhall–midnight.\n- **To Meridian:** meridian–midnight, meridian–dawnwatch, meridian–noonspire, meridian–vesperhall.\n\nEvery realm has the same shape: a capital at the back, two flank castles that each face a brigand castle, and an inner\ncastle that faces an Hour satellite. That keeps the realms fair. A test checks the graph is connected and symmetric.\n\n### 6.4 Realms\n\n| id | Realm | Season | Colours (main / trim) | Sigil | Banner | Ruler | Capital |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| verdance | Kingdom of Verdance | Spring | `#4caf50` / `#f0e6c8` | five-petal blossom | swallowtail | Prince Gareth Greenmantle | Avalorn |\n| solmark | Sun-March of Solmark | Summer | `#e0a020` / `#b02a2a` | rayed sun | square | Queen Morgause the Brazen | Brazenhold |\n| amberlyn | Harvest Throne of Amberlyn | Autumn | `#c86a1e` / `#5a3a2a` | oak leaf | pointed | King Pellam the Quiet | Ambergate |\n| hoarfast | Duchy of Hoarfast | Winter | `#6ab0e8` / `#e8f4ff` | snowflake | triangle | Duke Mordrain the Frostbitten | Rimeholt |\n| dominion | Hourless Dominion | Hour | `#3a3a46` / `#d8c070` | hourglass | long tapered | Lord Chancellor Meliant | Meridian |\n| brigands | Free Companies | — | `#7a6a5a` / `#2a2a2a` | crossed axes | ragged | (four captains) | — |\n\nSides are never told apart by colour alone: every unit also carries its realm's sigil on a pennant over it, and the\noutline colour, the banner shape and the sigil all agree.\n\n### 6.5 Knights\nEach row gives the Humanoid look (§7.5) and the voice profile (§9.3). Each troop lists `species level`. Every realm's\ncapital also starts with two tier-1 level-2 monsters in reserve: Verdance sproutlings, Solmark salamanders, Amberlyn\njack-o'-lamps and Hoarfast snowkits. Meridian starts with two level-10 minutes.\n\n#### 6.5.1 Verdance (Spring)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| gareth | **Prince Gareth Greenmantle** (ruler) | Springwarden | 6 | Spring | Avalorn | unicorn 4, pixie 4, sproutling 4 | earnest, idealistic, quick to forgive; grieving his mother, the late Queen | heroic 1.25, armor, short golden hair, circlet, green cape, sword | bright tenor, quick |\n| lynette | Dame Lynette of Thornwick | Squire | 7 | Spring | Thornwick | treant 4, sproutling 3 | his sworn shield; stern, dry humour, protective | heroic 1.2, armor, dark-red ponytail, band, white-and-green tabard | firm alto |\n| pelleas | Sir Pelleas the Lovelorn | Archer | 5 | Spring | Primrose Ford | pixie 4, rillserpent 3 | a poet-archer, overdramatic and brave | heroic 1.15, tunic, long chestnut hair, cap | lilting, high |\n| amris | Brother Amris | Acolyte | 6 | Winter | Avalorn | snowkit 3, sproutling 3 | an old monk from the north; gentle, wry | heroic 1.15, hunch .2, grey robe, bald, staff | slow, low |\n| wren | Wren Ashfeather | Tamer | 5 | Spring | Rainmere | unicorn 3, pixie 3, sproutling 3 | raised among unicorns; few words | heroic 1.1, leaf-green tunic, ash-white spiky hair, hood | chirpy |\n\n#### 6.5.2 Solmark (Summer)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| morgause | **Queen Morgause the Brazen** (ruler) | Sun Sovereign | 7 | Summer | Brazenhold | wyvern 4, cinderhound 4 | magnificent and war-loving, honourable on the field, ruthless at court | heroic 1.3, gold armor, crown, long copper hair, crimson cape, two-handed sword | commanding mezzo |\n| agravain | Sir Agravain Cinderjaw | Squire | 7 | Summer | Cinderwall | cinderhound 4, salamander 3 | a hothead champion who craves glory | bulky 1.25, armor, helmet, red cape | growly baritone |\n| elidure | Captain Elidure of Goldspur | Archer | 6 | Summer | Goldspur | sunbird 3, salamander 3 | disciplined, loyal and secretly kind | heroic 1.2, sand coat, black ponytail, band | clear soprano |\n| hesper | Magus Hesper Vey | Adept | 6 | Hour | Lionsreach | salamander 3, minute 3 | an ambitious court sorcerer who dabbles in Hour magic | heroic 1.2, purple-and-gold robe, pointed hat, long silver hair | silky |\n| brennoc | Old Brennoc | Tamer | 5 | Summer | Brazenhold | sunmane 3, cinderhound 3 | a grizzled, grandfatherly beastkeeper | bulky 1.2, hunch .3, leather coat, bald, whip | gravelly |\n\n#### 6.5.3 Amberlyn (Autumn)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| pellam | **King Pellam the Quiet** (ruler) | Harvest King | 8 | Autumn | Ambergate | griffin 4, scarecrow 4 | silent and wise; speaks rarely and briefly; secretly ill | heroic 1.2, hunch .25, amber-and-umber robe, crown, long white hair, staff | soft, low, slow |\n| enid | Lady Enid Russet | Acolyte | 6 | Autumn | Ambergate | jacklamp 3, scarecrow 3 | the king's daughter; gentle, firm, practical | heroic 1.15, cream-and-russet robe, long auburn hair, band | warm |\n| dagonet | Sir Dagonet the Motley | Squire | 5 | Autumn | Russetmoor | tusker 3, jacklamp 3 | a jester-knight who jokes to hide his fear | heroic 1.1, two-colour tunic, pointed hat, sword | bouncy |\n| vesna | Vesna of the Lanterns | Adept | 6 | Summer | Lanternfall | jacklamp 4, ghoul 3 | a lamplighter witch, kind to the dead | heroic 1.15, black-and-orange robe, pointed hat, long black hair | breathy |\n| lamorak | Sir Lamorak Ashbarrow | Squire | 8 | Autumn | Ashbarrow | ghoul 4, scarecrow 3 | a gruff old veteran, loyal to Pellam | bulky 1.2, rusty armor, helmet, brown cape | gruff |\n\n#### 6.5.4 Hoarfast (Winter)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| mordrain | **Duke Mordrain the Frostbitten** (ruler) | Rime Duke | 7 | Winter | Rimeholt | frostwyrm 3, snowkit 4 | theatrical, mad and brilliant; speaks in riddles; grief hidden under ice | heroic 1.25, white coat, icicle crown, long white hair, staff, pale-blue cape, faint eyeGlow | high, erratic pitch |\n| ragnell | Dame Ragnell Ice-Eye | Squire | 8 | Winter | Kestrel Spire | frostwolf 4, icegolem 3 | his cold, calculating marshal, the sane one | heroic 1.25, steel armor, helmet, white ponytail, dark-blue cape | flat alto |\n| safir | Sir Safir the Pale | Archer | 6 | Winter | Wolfsgate | frostwolf 3, snowkit 3 | a quiet, melancholic hunter | heroic 1.2, white hood, grey coat | soft |\n| nimue | Nimue of Frostmere | Adept | 7 | Winter | Frostmere | snowkit 4, snowkit 3 | an enigmatic lake witch who makes bargains | heroic 1.15, teal robe, long pale-blue hair | echoing |\n| gorm | Gorm the Bear | Tamer | 5 | Autumn | Rimeholt | yeti 3, tusker 3 | huge and gentle; raised in the western woods | bulky 1.35, brown fur coat, short hair, whip | very low |\n\n#### 6.5.5 The Hourless Dominion (Hour)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| meliant | **Lord Chancellor Meliant** (ruler) | Chancellor of Hours | 14 | Meridian | pendulumwyrm 10, clockwork (tier 2: Tick Knight) 12, stillwraith 12 | cold, grieving and absolute; believes he is merciful | heroic 1.25, black-and-brass robe, brass band, short grey hair, brass rod | measured baritone |\n| bertilak | Marshal Bertilak the Hourward | Knight | 12 | Midnight Keep | clockwork (tier 2) 12, gearhound 10, gearhound 9 | courteous, ruthless; loves a duel | bulky 1.3, brass armor, helmet, green-black cape | booming |\n| aurelie | Countess Aurelie of Vespers | Sorcerer | 12 | Vesper Hall | stillwraith 10, minute 10, minute 9 | elegant, bored and cruel | heroic 1.2, violet-and-black robe, long black hair, band | drawling |\n| morholt | Sir Morholt the Unmoving | Knight | 11 | Noonspire | clockwork 10, clockwork 9 | a silent giant | bulky 1.45, black armor, helmet | grunts only |\n| tic | Tic | Ranger | 10 | Dawnwatch | gearhound 9, minute 9 | a clockwork twin who finishes Tac's sentences | chibi 1.0, brass armor, cap | squeaky, high |\n| tac | Tac | Ranger | 10 | Dawnwatch | gearhound 9, minute 9 | the other twin | the same, colours swapped | squeaky, low |\n| graynight | **The Gray Knight, Sir Nonesuch** | Knight of the Thirteenth Hour | 25 | the Sanctum only | minute (tier 3) 22 ×4, pendulumwyrm (tier 2) 22 | the month that never was: calm, ancient, faintly amused | heroic 1.6, grey armor, helmet, tattered grey cape, white eyeGlow, long sword, clock-hand halo | two detuned low voices |\n\nThe Gray Knight's stats are fixed: HP 900, MP 200, ATK 52, DEF 48, INT 50, AGI 30, MOV 5. His skills are Thirteenth\nStroke, Still, Unmaking and Timeless.\n\n#### 6.5.6 Free knights (joined by event or quest)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | How they join | Brings | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| lunete | Princess Lunete of Meridian | Hourmaiden | 8 | Hour | the Lunete chain (§6.12) | — | the Keeper's daughter; steady and kind; carries her father's broken watch | heroic 1.15, white-and-brass robe, long gold hair, band | clear, gentle |\n| galeron | Sir Galeron the Wanderer | Knight | 10 | Spring | Wanderer outcome at Winter or Spring sites, from Autumn of Year 1 | frostwolf 8 | an errant knight looking for a cause | heroic 1.25, dented armor, faded green cape | weary tenor |\n| blanchefleur | Blanchefleur the Sellsword | Ranger | 10 | Autumn | Wanderer at Summer or Autumn sites, or the Lammas Fair (pay 150 mana) | sunmane 8 | a mercenary with a code: coin first | heroic 1.2, red-brown coat, short blonde hair | brisk |\n| owain | Owain the Dragonless | Beastlord | 11 | Summer | event `owain`: the first time your realm binds a wyvern or frost wyrm | — | lost his dragon in the Long Winter; will train yours | bulky 1.25, leather coat, short hair | husky |\n| ettard | Sister Ettard | Priest | 10 | Winter | Wanderer at Hallowmere, Lanternfall or Frostmere | snowkit 7 | a sharp-tongued healer | heroic 1.15, white-and-blue robe, hood | crisp |\n\n#### 6.5.7 Brigand captains (Brigand Captain class)\n\n| id | Name | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| hob | Hob Mudspur | 5 | Winter | Thawgate | snowkit 4, frostwolf 4, bat 3, slime 3 | swaggering, and a coward at heart |\n| gerrow | Mother Gerrow | 5 | Spring | Beltane Ford | slime 4, harpy 4, sproutling 3, bat 3 | motherly and crafty; hides Lunete at her mill |\n| dafydd | Red Dafydd | 6 | Summer | Lammas Cross | ogre 4, skeleton 4, salamander 3 | boisterous and proud |\n| abbot | The Hollow Abbot | 6 | Autumn | Hallowmere | skeleton 5, ghoul 4, bat 4 | eerie and sorrowful; keeps the dead company |\n\n### 6.6 Knight classes\n\n**Stat rule:**\n- At tier 1, `stat(L) = base + growth × (L − 1)`.\n- At a class change, every stat (MP included) is multiplied by 1.10.\n- After that, growth is ×1.15 (tier 2) or ×1.30 (tier 3) of the line's tier-1 growth.\n- Knights who start at tier 2 or 3 are built the same way with expected values, as if they changed class at levels 10\n  and 20.\n- Bond = base + floor(level / 4). MOV and Ward come from the class.\n\n| id | Class | Line, tier | Weapons | Basic attack | MOV | Ward | Bond | Base at Lv 1: HP/MP/ATK/DEF/INT/AGI | Growth per level | Skills (level) | Next |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| squire | Squire | Warrior 1 | sword, spear, axe | Slash 1.0, range 1 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 70/8/17/15/7/11 | 7/.6/1.6/1.4/.4/.9 | Rally (3) | knight at 10 |\n| knight | Knight | Warrior 2 | sword, spear, axe | Slash | 5 | 3 | 7 | ×1.1 at change | ×1.15 | Charge (10), Shield Wall (14) | paladin at 20 + Writ |\n| paladin | Paladin | Warrior 3 | sword, spear | Slash | 5 | 3 | 9 | ×1.1 | ×1.30 | Holy Strike (20), Lay on Hands (24) | — |\n| archer | Archer | Ranger 1 | bow | Shoot 0.9, range 2–4 | 5 | 2 | 4 | 58/10/16/10/9/15 | 5.5/.8/1.5/.9/.6/1.3 | Aimed Shot (4) | ranger at 10 |\n| ranger | Ranger | Ranger 2 | bow | Shoot | 5 | 3 | 6 | | | Volley (10), Pinning Shot (14) | sentinel at 20 + Writ |\n| sentinel | Sentinel | Ranger 3 | bow | Shoot, range 2–5 | 5 | 3 | 7 | | | Piercing Arrow (20), Eagle Eye (24) | — |\n| adept | Adept | Mage 1 | staff, tome | Strike 0.6, range 1 | 4 | 2 | 4 | 50/30/8/8/18/11 | 4.5/2.2/.5/.7/1.8/.9 | own element's Bolt (1), Hex (6) | sorcerer at 10 |\n| sorcerer | Sorcerer | Mage 2 | staff, tome | Strike | 4 | 3 | 6 | | | Storm (10), Mana Siphon (14) | archmage at 20 + Writ |\n| archmage | Archmage | Mage 3 | staff, tome | Strike | 4 | 3 | 7 | | | Tempest (20), Haste (24) | — |\n| acolyte | Acolyte | Cleric 1 | mace, staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 55/26/10/10/15/10 | 5/2/.7/.9/1.5/.8 | Mend (1), Purify (5) | priest at 10 |\n| priest | Priest | Cleric 2 | mace, staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 3 | 7 | | | Renewal (10), Ward of Seasons (14) | hierophant at 20 + Writ |\n| hierophant | Hierophant | Cleric 3 | staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 4 | 8 | | | Greater Renewal (20), Dawnlight (24) | — |\n| tamer | Tamer | Beast 1 | whip, spear | Lash 0.8, range 1–2 | 5 | 3 | 7 | 62/12/14/12/10/13 | 6/.9/1.2/1.1/.7/1.1 | Goad (3) | beastlord at 10 |\n| beastlord | Beastlord | Beast 2 | whip, spear | Lash | 5 | 4 | 10 | | | Pack Tactics (10), Roar (14) | beastsovereign at 20 + Writ |\n| beastsovereign | Beast Sovereign | Beast 3 | spear, whip | Lash | 5 | 4 | 13 | | | Call of the Wild (20), Bond of Fang (24) | — |\n| springwarden | Springwarden | ruler | sword | Slash 1.0 | 5 | 4 | 10 | 75/22/17/15/15/14 | 7/1.5/1.5/1.3/1.3/1.1 | Mend (1), Charge (1), Verdant Oath (6), Bramble Storm (10), Verdant Tempest (16) | — |\n| sunsovereign | Sun Sovereign | ruler | greatsword | Cleave 1.1 | 5 | 4 | 11 | 85/14/21/16/10/12 | 8/1/1.9/1.4/.8/1 | Charge (1), Warcry (6), Cinder Storm (10), Solar Flare (16) | — |\n| harvestking | Harvest King | ruler | staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 5 | 10 | 68/30/11/13/20/10 | 6/2/.8/1.2/1.8/.8 | Mend (1), Gale of Leaves (1), Quiet Counsel (6), Harvest Moon (12), Reaping (16) | — |\n| rimeduke | Rime Duke | ruler | staff | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 4 | 10 | 70/28/15/13/19/13 | 6.5/1.8/1.3/1.1/1.7/1 | Hoarfrost (1), Mad Gambit (6), Frost Storm (10), Frozen Hour (12), Blizzard (16) | — |\n| chancellor | Chancellor of Hours | ruler | rod | Strike 0.8 | 4 | 4 | 12 | 80/34/12/15/22/12 | 7/2/1/1.4/1.9/.9 | Time Shear (1), Stop (1), Restore (6), Hour Storm (10) | — |\n| hourmaiden | Hourmaiden | unique | staff | Strike 0.8 | 5 | 3 | 6 | 58/34/9/11/19/15 | 5/2.2/.6/1/1.8/1.2 | Mend (1), Haste (1), Turning (8) | — |\n| graynight | Knight of the Thirteenth Hour | boss | long sword | Slash 1.2 | 5 | 5 | — | fixed (§6.5.5) | — | Thirteenth Stroke, Still, Unmaking, Timeless | — |\n| brigand | Brigand Captain | unique | axe | Hack 1.05 | 5 | 3 | 8 | 72/6/18/13/6/12 | 7/.4/1.6/1.2/.3/1 | Charge (1), Ambush (1) | — |\n\n**A knight's element picks its spells.** \"Bolt\", \"Hex\", \"Storm\" and \"Tempest\" mean that element's spell of that tier\n(§6.7). An Adept of Winter learns Hoarfrost, then Frostbite.\n\n### 6.7 Skills and spells\nAreas:\n- `single`;\n- `r1` / `r2`: the target hex plus every hex within 1 or 2 of it;\n- `self-r1` / `self-r2`: around the user;\n- `adj`: the 6 hexes around the user;\n- `cone2` / `cone3`: hexes within 2 or 3 of the user, inside a 120° wedge facing one of the 6 directions;","numLines":390,"startLine":470,"totalLines":2417}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011paortrMsutKXgCrgMofUP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
