{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VVkKJ8nc9Ma7xvwUCBKo4c","type":"tool_result","content":"859\t- `cone2` / `cone3`: hexes within 2 or 3 of the user, inside a 120° wedge facing one of the 6 directions;\n860\t- `line3` / `line4`: a straight hex line from the user in one of the 6 directions.\n861\t\n862\t\"Foes\" or \"allies\" filters who is touched. Status numbers are the base chance (§5.6). P is the power; a heal's P is the\n863\tbase amount.\n864\t\n865\t| id | Name | Kind | Elem | P | Range | Area | MP | Mobile | Effect / notes |\n866\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n867\t| rally | Rally | special | — | — | self | self-r1 allies | 4 | yes | Valor 2 bells |\n868\t| charge | Charge | special | user's | 1.3 | 1 | single | 5 | yes | must move 2+ hexes first |\n869\t| shieldwall | Shield Wall | special | — | — | self | adj allies | 6 | yes | Warded 1 bell |\n870\t| holystrike | Holy Strike | special | none | 1.5 | 1 | single | 8 | yes | ignores element; ×1.5 vs Hour |\n871\t| layonhands | Lay on Hands | special | — | heal 60 | 1 | single ally | 10 | yes | |\n872\t| aimedshot | Aimed Shot | special | user's | 1.2 | 2–4 | single | 4 | no | +20 hit |\n873\t| volley | Volley | special | user's | 0.8 | 3–5 | r1 | 8 | no | |\n874\t| pinning | Pinning Shot | special | user's | 0.9 | 2–4 | single | 6 | yes | Chill 70 |\n875\t| piercing | Piercing Arrow | special | user's | 1.1 | — | line4 | 10 | no | every unit on the line |\n876\t| eagleeye | Eagle Eye | passive | | | | | | | bows +1 max range |\n877\t| bramble, cinder, galeleaves, hoarfrost, timeshear | Bramble / Cinder / Gale of Leaves / Hoarfrost / Time Shear (Bolts) | spell | Sp / Su / Au / Wi / Hour | 14 | 1–4 | single | 5 | no | Time Shear ignores the Tide |\n878\t| drowse, kindle, rot, frostbite, stophex | Drowse / Kindle / Rot / Frostbite / Stop (Hexes) | spell | Sp / Su / Au / Wi / Hour | — | 1–4 | single | 6 | no | Sleep 60 / Burn 70 / Poison 70 / Chill 70 / Stop 40 |\n879\t| bramblestorm, cinderstorm, leafstorm, froststorm, hourstorm | Bramble / Cinder / Leaf / Frost / Hour Storm | spell | Sp / Su / Au / Wi / Hour | 22 | 1–4 | r1 | 10 | no | Cinder Storm on a forest sets it burning (§5.7) |\n880\t| verdanttempest, solarflare, harvestmoon, blizzard | Verdant Tempest / Solar Flare / Harvest Moon / Blizzard (Tempests) | spell | Sp / Su / Au / Wi | 34 | 1–5 | r2 | 16 | no | Sleep 20 / Burn 30 (and burns forests) / drains 25% of damage to the caster / Chill 30 |\n881\t| manasiphon | Mana Siphon | spell | — | — | 1–4 | single | 2 | no | steals 12 MP |\n882\t| haste | Haste | spell | — | — | 0–3 | single ally | 8 | no | Haste 2 bells |\n883\t| mend | Mend | spell | — | heal 30 | 0–3 | single ally | 5 | no | |\n884\t| purify | Purify | spell | — | — | 0–3 | single ally | 4 | no | clears statuses and debuffs |\n885\t| renewal | Renewal | spell | — | heal 24 | 0–3 | r1 allies | 10 | no | |\n886\t| wardofseasons | Ward of Seasons | spell | — | — | 0–3 | r1 allies | 9 | no | Warded 2 bells |\n887\t| greaterrenewal | Greater Renewal | spell | — | heal 36 | 0–4 | r2 allies | 16 | no | |\n888\t| dawnlight | Dawnlight | spell | none | 26 | 1–4 | r1 foes | 14 | no | ×1.5 vs Hour; ignores the Tide |\n889\t| goad | Goad | special | — | — | 1–2 | one own monster | 3 | yes | Valor and Haste 1 bell |\n890\t| packtactics | Pack Tactics | passive | | | | | | | the knight's monsters +10 hit |\n891\t| roar | Roar | special | — | — | self | self-r2 foes | 6 | yes | Weakened 60 |\n892\t| callofwild | Call of the Wild | special | — | 20% max HP | self | own troop's monsters | 12 | yes | heals |\n893\t| bondoffang | Bond of Fang | special | — | — | Ward | one own monster in Ward | 10 | yes | Valor, Warded and Haste 2 bells |\n894\t| verdantoath | Verdant Oath | special | Sp | heal 10% | self | allies in Ward | 10 | yes | Warded 2 bells |\n895\t| warcry | Warcry | special | Su | — | self | allies in Ward | 8 | yes | Valor 2 bells |\n896\t| quietcounsel | Quiet Counsel | special | Au | — | self | allies in Ward | 10 | yes | Haste 1 bell |\n897\t| reaping | Reaping | spell | Au | 20 | 1–3 | single | 8 | no | heals the caster 50% of the damage |\n898\t| madgambit | Mad Gambit | special | Wi | 30 (magic) | 1–3 | single | 6 | yes | 25%: misfires and Chills the Duke instead |\n899\t| frozenhour | Frozen Hour | spell | Wi | — | 1–4 | single | 12 | no | Stop 70 |\n900\t| restore | Restore | spell | Hour | 50% max HP | 0–3 | single ally | 14 | no | |\n901\t| turning | Turning | special | none | 40 (magic) | 1–3 | r1 foes | 0, once per battle | yes | ×2 vs Hour; a Gray Knight it hits loses Timeless until the end of the next bell |\n902\t| ambush | Ambush | passive | | | | | | | +30% damage when attacking from a forest hex |\n903\t| thirteenthstroke | Thirteenth Stroke | special | Hour | 1.6 | 1 | r1 foes | 0 | yes | |\n904\t| still | Still | special | Hour | — | self | self-r2 foes | 0, every 3rd bell | yes | Stop 70 |\n905\t| unmaking | Unmaking | spell | Hour | 25% of target's max HP | 1–3 | single | 20 | no | ignores DEF, element and Tide |\n906\t| timeless | Timeless | passive | | | | | | | immune to effects and the Tide; takes ×0.5 damage until the four Season Dials are lit (§6.10) or Turning hits |\n907\t| pollenpuff | Pollen Puff | special | Sp | — | self | self-r1 foes | 6 | yes | Sleep 50 |\n908\t| entangle | Entangle | special | Sp | 0.6 | 1–2 | single | 5 | no | Chill 70 |\n909\t| scream | Mandrake Scream | special | Sp | — | self | self-r2 foes | 10 | no | Sleep 50 |\n910\t| sleepdust | Sleep Dust | spell | Sp | — | 1–3 | r1 foes | 8 | no | Sleep 60 |\n911\t| thorns | Thorns | passive | | | | | | | melee attackers take 10% of the damage they deal |\n912\t| rootsweep | Root Sweep | special | Sp | 0.9 | — | adj foes | 6 | yes | |\n913\t| dive | Dive | special | user's | 1.2 | 1 | single | 4 | yes | fliers; must move 2+ hexes first |\n914\t| torrent | Torrent | special | Sp | 1.0 | — | line3 | 6 | no | |\n915\t| coil | Coil | special | user's | 0.8 | 1 | single | 4 | yes | Chill 60 |\n916\t| emberspit | Ember Spit | special | Su | 0.9 | 1–2 | single | 3 | yes | Burn 30 |\n917\t| firebreath | Fire Breath | special | Su | 1.2 | — | cone2 (dragons: cone3) | 8 | no | Burn 25 |\n918\t| howl | Howl | special | — | — | self | self-r2 allies | 5 | yes | Valor 1 bell |\n919\t| pounce | Pounce | special | user's | 1.2 | 1 | single | 5 | yes | |\n920\t| rebirth | Rebirth | passive | | | | | | | once per battle, at 0 HP it rises again with 30% HP |\n921\t| sunriddle | Sun Riddle | special | Su | — | self | self-r1 foes | 8 | no | Sleep 50 |\n922\t| wispfire | Wisp Fire | special | Au | 0.9 (magic) | 1–3 | single | 4 | yes | |\n923\t| fear | Fear | special | Au | — | self | self-r1 foes | 5 | yes | Weakened 60 |\n924\t| drain | Drain | special | user's | 1.0 | 1 | single | 4 | yes | heals 50% of the damage |\n925\t| gravechill | Grave Chill | special | Wi | — | self | self-r1 foes | 7 | no | Chill 40 |\n926\t| gale | Gale | special | Au | 0.7 | 1 | single | 5 | yes | pushes the target 1 hex away; if blocked, 4 more damage |\n927\t| trample | Trample | special | user's | 1.0 | — | line3 | 6 | yes | |\n928\t| thickhide | Thick Hide | passive | | | | | | | DEF +10% |\n929\t| frostarmor | Frost Armor | special | Wi | — | self | self | 5 | yes | DEF +40% 2 bells |\n930\t| avalanche | Avalanche | special | Wi | 1.0 | 1–2 | r1 | 9 | no | |\n931\t| hurlice | Hurl Ice | special | Wi | 1.0 | 2–3 | single | 5 | no | |\n932\t| frostfang | Frost Fang | passive | | | | | | | basic attacks Chill 30 |\n933\t| frostbreath | Frost Breath | special | Wi | 1.2 | — | cone3 | 8 | no | Chill 40 |\n934\t| tailsweep | Tail Sweep | special | user's | 0.9 | — | adj foes | 6 | yes | |\n935\t| windup | Wind-up | special | — | — | self | self | 3 | yes | its next basic attack ×1.5 |\n936\t| pendulum | Pendulum | special | Hour | 1.1 | — | adj foes | 6 | yes | |\n937\t| stopbite | Stopping Bite | passive | | | | | | | basic attacks Stop 20 |\n938\t| engulf | Engulf | special | user's | 0.9 | 1 | single | 4 | yes | Poison 40 |\n939\t| regenerate | Regenerate | passive | | | | | | | heals 10% max HP at its turn start |\n940\t| groundpound | Ground Pound | special | user's | 1.0 | — | adj foes | 7 | yes | |\n941\t| screech | Screech | special | — | — | self | self-r1 foes | 5 | yes | Weakened 60 |\n942\t\n943\t### 6.8 Bestiary (30 species, 3 forms each)\n944\t**Form and level rules:**\n945\t- Tier 2 = tier 1 × 1.35 (HP, MP, ATK, DEF, INT), AGI +2. Tier 3 = tier 1 × 1.75, AGI +4, MOV +1 for fliers.\n946\t- At level L, every stat is `round(formBase × (1 + 0.05 × (L − 1)))`.\n947\t- Rank is the bond cost and doesn't change with form. Upkeep ×1.5 at tier 2 and ×2 at tier 3.\n948\t- Each form keeps the skills before it and adds its own (column \"Skills\").\n949\t\n950\tFlags: `fl` flier, `sw` swimmer, `fo` floater. The \"Rig\" column is the look; §7.5 defines the rig kinds.\n951\t\n952\t| id | Forms | Elem | Size | Rank | Flags | Tier 1: HP/MP/ATK/DEF/INT/AGI/MOV | Basic attack (P, range) | Skills: T1; +T2; +T3 | Cost / upkeep | Rig |\n953\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n954\t| sproutling | Sproutling → Bloomkin → Mandragora | Sp | S | 1 | | 38/12/12/9/12/13/4 | Headbutt 1.0, 1 | Pollen Puff; +Entangle; +Mandrake Scream | 30 / 2 | Blob R6, leaf ears, a sprout on top; Mandragora gets a root crown |\n955\t| pixie | Pixie → Sylph → Faerie Queen | Sp | S, S, M | 1 | fl | 30/24/8/6/16/20/6 | Prick 0.7, 1 | Mend; +Haste; +Sleep Dust | 45 / 3 | Humanoid chibi .55 + insect `E.Wings`, glow |\n956\t| treant | Thornback Treant → Elder Treant → Worldroot | Sp | L | 4 | | 120/10/22/22/8/5/3 | Slam 1.1, 1 | Thorns, Entangle; +Renewal; +Root Sweep | 120 / 8 | Humanoid bulky 1.6, bark colours, leaf crown, long arms, hunch .3 |\n957\t| unicorn | Unicorn → Alicorn → Dawnhorn | Sp | M, M, L | 3 | T2+ fl | 80/20/19/14/14/16/6 | Gore 1.1, 1 | Charge, Mend; +Dive; +Dawnlight | 90 / 5 | Beast quad `horse` + horn; feather wings from T2 |\n958\t| rillserpent | Rillserpent → Floodwyrm → Thaw Leviathan | Sp | L | 4 | sw | 110/18/21/16/14/9/4 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Torrent, Coil; +Bramble Storm; +Verdant Tempest | 130 / 8 | Beast serpent, fins, river-green scales |\n959\t| salamander | Salamander → Firedrake → Magma Drake | Su | S, M, M | 2 | | 50/12/16/12/10/12/4 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Ember Spit; +Fire Breath; +Cinder Storm | 45 / 3 | Beast quad `lizard` (low, long tail), ember glow |\n960\t| cinderhound | Cinderhound → Blazehound → Twinflame Hound | Su | M | 2 | | 70/10/20/12/8/14/5 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Fire Breath; +Howl; +Pounce | 70 / 4 | Beast quad `hound` + flame mane |\n961\t| sunbird | Sunbird → Phoenix → Solar Roc | Su | M, M, L | 3 | fl | 60/18/17/10/14/18/6 | Talon 1.0, 1 | Dive; +Rebirth; +Solar Flare | 90 / 5 | Beast `avian`, fire tail |\n962\t| wyvern | Wyvern → Sun Dragon → Elder Sun Dragon | Su | L | 4 | fl | 120/16/25/18/12/10/5 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Tail Sweep, Fire Breath (cone3); +Dive; +Solar Flare | 160 / 10 | Beast `drake`: 2 legs + wings (Wyvern), 4 legs + wings (dragons) |\n963\t| sunmane | Sunmane Lion → Solar Chimera → Noon Sphinx | Su | M, L, L | 3 | | 85/12/22/14/9/15/5 | Claw 1.0, 1 | Roar, Pounce; +Fire Breath; +Sun Riddle | 100 / 6 | Beast quad `cat` + mane; wings and a snake tail from T2 |\n964\t| jacklamp | Jack-o'-Lamp → Lantern Lord → Will of the Wisps | Au | S, S, M | 1 | fo | 36/20/10/8/15/14/4 | Spook 0.8, 1 | Wisp Fire; +Fear; +Leaf Storm | 30 / 2 | Blob: an orange pumpkin with a glowing carved face and a flame on top; floats |\n965\t| scarecrow | Scarecrow → Harvest Reaper → Grim Thresher | Au | M | 2 | | 65/10/18/12/10/12/4 | Scythe 1.1, 1 | Fear; +Reaping; +Trample | 60 / 4 | Humanoid, straw palette, pointed hat, patched coat, scythe drawn from the hands |\n966\t| ghoul | Barrow Ghoul → Wight → Barrow King | Au | M | 2 | | 70/12/19/13/9/10/4 | Claw 1.0, 1 (Poison 25) | Drain; +Grave Chill; +Rot | 55 / 3 | Humanoid, hunch .6, grey-green skin, eyeGlow, rags |\n967\t| griffin | Griffin → Gilded Griffin → Storm Griffin | Au | L | 4 | fl | 105/14/23/15/12/15/6 | Talon 1.0, 1 | Dive, Gale; +Leaf Storm; +Harvest Moon | 140 / 9 | Beast `griffin`: eagle front and wings, lion rear |\n968\t| tusker | Great Tusker → Ironhide Boar → Boar King | Au | M, M, L | 3 | | 85/6/21/16/4/10/5 | Gore 1.1, 1 | Trample; +Thick Hide; +Roar | 70 / 4 | Beast quad `boar`, tusks, bristles |\n969\t| snowkit | Snowkit → Rime Sprite → Aurora Wisp | Wi | S | 1 | T3 fo | 36/18/11/9/14/15/4 | Snowball 0.8, 1–2 | Frostbite; +Frost Armor; +Frost Storm | 30 / 2 | Blob, white, cat ears, frost sparkle; aurora glow at T3 |\n970\t| frostwolf | Frostwolf → Dire Frostwolf → Long-Night Wolf | Wi | M, M, L | 2 | | 68/8/20/11/7/16/6 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Howl, Frost Fang; +Pounce; +Frost Breath | 65 / 4 | Beast quad `wolf`, white-blue |\n971\t| icegolem | Ice Golem → Glacier Colossus → Hoarfrost Titan | Wi | L | 4 | | 130/8/24/26/6/4/3 | Slam 1.1, 1 | Frost Armor; +Avalanche; +Thorns | 130 / 8 | Humanoid bulky 1.5, ice-crystal colours, cyan eyeGlow |\n972\t| yeti | Yeti → Great Yeti → Yeti Matriarch | Wi | L | 4 | | 115/8/25/17/6/8/4 | Maul 1.15, 1 | Hurl Ice; +Roar; +Avalanche | 110 / 7 | Humanoid bulky 1.5, white fur, no weapon, hunch .3 |\n973\t| frostwyrm | Frost Wyrm → Rime Dragon → Winter's Heart | Wi | L | 5 | fl | 125/18/24/19/14/9/5 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Frost Breath, Tail Sweep; +Dive; +Blizzard | 170 / 11 | Beast `drake`, 4 legs + wings, crest, icy palette |\n974\t| minute | Minute → Hour-Wisp → Second Hand | Hour | S | 1 | fo | 34/16/11/10/13/17/5 | Tick 0.8, 1 | Stop (Hex); +Haste; +Time Shear | 40 / 2 | Blob: a brass sphere with a clock face, small orbiting gears |\n975\t| clockwork | Clockwork Sentinel → Tick Knight → Pendulum Paladin | Hour | M | 3 | | 80/8/21/20/8/9/4 | Slash 1.0, 1 | Wind-up; +Shield Wall; +Pendulum | 80 / 5 | Humanoid heroic 1.25, brass plate, helmet, gear halo |\n976\t| gearhound | Gearhound → Clockwork Hound → Chronohound | Hour | M | 2 | | 65/6/19/15/6/15/6 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Pounce; +Howl; +Stopping Bite | 60 / 4 | Beast quad `hound`, metal palette, gear joints |\n977\t| stillwraith | Stillwraith → Hollow Hour → Unhour | Hour | M | 3 | fo | 60/30/10/10/20/13/5 | Spook 0.8, 1 | Time Shear, Stop; +Drain; +Hour Storm | 85 / 5 | Humanoid robe and hood at alpha .75, a clock face for a head, floats 6 up |\n978\t| pendulumwyrm | Pendulum Wyrm → Great Pendulum → The Long Hand | Hour | L | 5 | | 150/20/26/22/18/8/4 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Pendulum, Time Shear; +Coil; +Hour Storm | 200 / 12 (Meridian only) | Beast serpent, metal segments, a swinging pendulum disc for a tail |\n979\t| skeleton | Skeleton → Skeleton Knight → Bone Lord | Au | M | 2 | | 60/6/18/12/5/11/4 | Slash 1.0, 1 | —; +Shield Wall; +Charge | 50 / 3 | Humanoid build `skeleton`, rusty sword |\n980\t| bat | Giant Bat → Vampire Bat → Night Bat | Wi | S, S, M | 1 | fl | 32/8/12/7/8/19/6 | Bite 0.9, 1 (heals 25% of damage) | Dive; +Drain; +Fear | 30 / 2 | Blob with wings and fangs, dark palette |\n981\t| slime | Slime → Royal Slime → Slime Sovereign | Sp | S | 1 | | 44/10/11/12/9/9/3 | Headbutt 0.9, 1 | Engulf; +Regenerate; +Bramble Storm | 25 / 2 | Blob, translucent teal; a crown from T2 |\n982\t| ogre | Ogre → Ogre Chieftain → Ogre Warlord | Su | L | 4 | | 125/6/27/16/4/7/4 | Maul 1.15, 1 | Roar; +Charge; +Ground Pound | 110 / 7 | Humanoid bulky 1.5, grey-green skin, club |\n983\t| harpy | Harpy → Harpy Matron → Storm Harpy | Sp | M | 2 | fl | 55/14/17/10/12/17/6 | Talon 1.0, 1 | Dive; +Gale; +Screech | 55 / 3 | Humanoid 1.0 with feather `E.Wings`, bare taloned feet |\n984\t\n985\t### 6.9 Items (33; there are no shops: items come from quests, events and castle treasuries)\n986\t\n987\t| id | Name | Slot | Who | Effect |\n988\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n989\t| ashspear | Ashwood Spear | weapon | Warrior, Beast | ATK +3 |\n990\t| rimesteel | Rimesteel Sword | weapon | Warrior | ATK +5; a Winter wielder +5% damage |\n991\t| sunforged | Sunforged Blade | weapon | Warrior, Sun Sovereign | ATK +7 |\n992\t| cleaver | Brigand's Cleaver | weapon | Warrior | ATK +6, DEF −2 |\n993\t| hawthornbow | Hawthorn Bow | weapon | Ranger | ATK +4 |\n994\t| yewlongbow | Yew Longbow | weapon | Ranger | ATK +6, max range +1 |\n995\t| willowstaff | Willow Staff | weapon | Mage, Cleric, staff rulers | INT +4 |\n996\t| lanternstaff | Lantern Staff | weapon | Mage, Cleric, staff rulers | INT +6; Autumn spells +10% |\n997\t| tomeofthaw | Tome of Thaw | weapon | Mage | INT +5; Spring spells +10% |\n998\t| hourglassrod | Hourglass Rod | weapon | Mage, Cleric, rulers | INT +8, MP +10 |\n999\t| thornwhip | Thorn Whip | weapon | Beast | ATK +4; Lash range 1–3 |\n1000\t| jerkin | Leather Jerkin | armor | all | DEF +3 |\n1001\t| hauberk | Mail Hauberk | armor | Warrior, Beast, rulers | DEF +6, AGI −1 |\n1002\t| thornmail | Thornmail | armor | Warrior | DEF +5; Thorns |\n1003\t| frostplate | Frostplate | armor | Warrior, rulers | DEF +8; immune to Chill |\n1004\t| robeofseasons | Robe of Seasons | armor | Mage, Cleric, rulers | DEF +3, INT +4 |\n1005\t| spurs | Swift Spurs | accessory | all | MOV +1 |\n1006\t| signet | Signet of Command | accessory | all | Bond +2 |\n1007\t| bannerpin | Banner Pin | accessory | all | Ward +1 |\n1008\t| amuletoftides | Amulet of Tides | accessory | all | the wearer's Tide bonus ×2 |\n1009\t| wardingcharm | Warding Charm | accessory | all | immune to Sleep and Stop |\n1010\t| mendingring | Ring of Mending | accessory | all | heals 10% max HP at its troop's turn start |\n1011\t| horseshoe | Lucky Horseshoe | accessory | all | good quest outcomes ×1.15 |\n1012\t| herb | Healing Herb | consumable | — | heals 40 HP |\n1013\t| draught | Golden Draught | consumable | — | heals to full HP |\n1014\t| ether | Ether Vial | consumable | — | +20 MP |\n1015\t| remedy | Remedy | consumable | — | clears statuses and debuffs |\n1016\t| manaseed | Mana Seed | consumable (Muster) | — | +60 realm mana |\n1017\t| springseed | Spring Seed | promotion | Spring monsters | promotes (T1 → T2 from Lv 6; T2 → T3 from Lv 16) |\n1018\t| summerember | Summer Ember | promotion | Summer monsters | as above |\n1019\t| autumnacorn | Autumn Acorn | promotion | Autumn monsters | as above |\n1020\t| wintershard | Winter Shard | promotion | Winter monsters | as above |\n1021\t| writ | Writ of Knighthood | special | knights | allows a tier-3 class change from Lv 20 |\n1022\t\n1023\tStarting inventories: each season-realm starts with 2 Healing Herbs and 1 Remedy, plus its season's promotion item. The\n1024\tDominion starts with 3 Ether Vials. Quest pools by region are listed in §6.11.\n1025\t\n1026\t### 6.10 Battle maps (13)\n1027\tEach map is a list of rows, top row first, one character per hex (codes in §5.7; anchors `1 2 3` attacker, `7 8 9` defender, `1 2 3 4` seats). Odd rows sit half a hex to the right. A script built and checked every map below: every row has the same length; each anchor appears once and has at least 7 free hexes within 2 steps; and the Keep can be reached from every attacker anchor in all four seasons, floods and ice included. Keep that check as a test (§14). `flood` marks maps whose shallows flood in Spring.\n1028\t\n1029\t**Border Meadow** (`border_meadow`, 13 × 9): used by the tutorial (§6.13) and Skirmish. A meadow with a stream, a bridge on the road and a ruined watchtower Keep. Two troops a side: anchors 1 2 against 7 8.\n1030\t```\n1031\t..f.....h.ff.\n1032\t.ff.1.....~.f\n1033\t......f...~h.\n1034\t..2..f...~...\n1035\t,,,,,,,,,b,K7\n1036\t....f....~.8.\n1037\t.f.......~h..\n1038\t..h..f...~..f\n1039\t...f.....~.ff\n1040\t```\n1041\t**River Ford** (`river_ford`, 15 × 11, flood): used by Rainmere, Thawgate. A river splits the field, with two fords and one bridge on the road. In Spring the fords flood and only the bridge crosses; in Winter the river freezes into open ground.\n1042\t```\n1043\tff..h..w...hfff\n1044\t.f.1...w....ff.\n1045\t.....h.~..8..f.\n1046\tf......w...h...\n1047\t..2.f..w..h....\n1048\t,,,,,,,b,,,K7..\n1049\t..3.f..w..h....\n1050\tf......w...h...\n1051\t.....h.~..9..f.\n1052\t.f.....w....ff.\n1053\tff..h..w...hfff\n1054\t```\n1055\t**Forest Hold** (`forest_hold`, 15 × 11): used by Kestrel Spire, Thornwick, Lanternfall. Thick woods, a winding road and a clearing Keep between two hills. Forest slows large units (cost 3); in Summer fire can burn it open.\n1056\t```\n1057\t...ff....ff..ff\n1058\t..fff...fff.fff\n1059\t..1ff.ff.f8..ff\n1060\t.....fff..h.h..\n1061\t......f,,,.....\n1062\t,2...,,..,,K7..\n1063\t..,,,,..ff.....\n1064\t....ff.fffh.h..\n1065\t.f3.fff.ff9..ff\n1066\tfff.ff..fff.fff\n1067\t.ff......ff..ff\n1068\t```\n1069\t**Mountain Pass** (`mountain_pass`, 15 × 11): used by Wolfsgate, Cinderwall. Peaks squeeze the field into a pass 3 to 5 hexes wide, with ruins in it. Fliers cross the peaks. The Keep holds the pass's mouth.\n1070\t```\n1071\tmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm\n1072\tmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm\n1073\t...mmmmmmmmm...\n1074\t..f.hmm.mm.8h..\n1075\t..1...r........\n1076\t,2,,,,,,,,,K7,.\n1077\t.f3.....r......\n1078\t....hmm.mm.9h..\n1079\t...mmmmmmmmm...\n1080\tmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm\n1081\tmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm\n1082\t```\n1083\t**Hill Fort** (`hill_fort`, 15 × 11): used by Midnight Keep, Dawnwatch, Lionsreach. The Keep crowns a ring of hills (+10% DEF, +1 range for bows) with woods on both flanks.\n1084\t```\n1085\t..ff.fff.....ff\n1086\t.fff.ff.....fff\n1087\t..ff.........ff\n1088\t.1..h....8hh...\n1089\t.........hhhh..\n1090\t,2,,,,,,,hK7hf.\n1091\t.........hhhh..\n1092\t.3..h....9hh...\n1093\t...ff........ff\n1094\t..fffff.....fff\n1095\t...fffff.....ff\n1096\t```\n1097\t**Marsh Keep** (`marsh_keep`, 15 × 11, flood): used by Russetmoor, Beltane Ford. Bogs and pools around a causeway road. Summer dries the swamp; Spring floods the pools.\n1098\t```\n1099\t...............\n1100\t..fss.fss......\n1101\t...sss.sss.8.f.\n1102\t.1.ss~.ss~..h..\n1103\t...............\n1104\t,2,,,,,,,,,K7..\n1105\t......sss......\n1106\t.3ss.ss~s...9..\n1107\t..ssssssss.~ss.\n1108\t..ss.sss~..sss.\n1109\t......sss...ss.\n1110\t```\n1111\t**Lakeside** (`lakeside`, 15 × 11): used by Frostmere, Primrose Ford. A lake fills the north and the land route bends south around it. In Winter the lake freezes and opens a straight path to the Keep.\n1112\t```\n1113\t.fff........ff.\n1114\t.ff..LLLL..fff.\n1115\t.....LLLLLh.ff.\n1116\t.1...LLLLL..8..\n1117\t......LLLL.....\n1118\t..2...LLL..K7..\n1119\t...........,...\n1120\t,3,.....,,,9...\n1121\t.ff,,,,,,h...ff\n1122\tffffff......fff\n1123\t.ff.ff.......ff\n1124\t```\n1125\t**Ruined Abbey** (`ruined_abbey`, 15 × 11): used by Vesper Hall, Ashbarrow, Hallowmere. Broken walls (blocked) and ruins (+10% DEF) around an abbey-tower Keep.\n1126\t```\n1127\t.ff........ffff\n1128\tfff........ffff\n1129\t.ff..#..#....ff\n1130\t.1...#.r...r8..\n1131\t........r.r....\n1132\t,2,,,,,,,,,K7..\n1133\t..........r....\n1134\t.3...r.r.#.r9..\n1135\t..ff..#..#...ff\n1136\t.fff........fff\n1137\t..ff.........ff\n1138\t```\n1139\t**Crossroads** (`crossroads`, 15 × 11): used by Noonspire, Goldspur, Lammas Cross. Two roads cross among fields, with houses (blocked) making lanes. Summer wheat hides units (+10 evade).\n1140\t```\n1141\tf......,.....f.\n1142\t..FF...,FF.....\n1143\t..FFF..,FFF.#..\n1144\t.1FF.#.,FF.8...\n1145\t.......,.#.....\n1146\t,2,,,,,,,,,K7,,\n1147\t.......,.#.....\n1148\t.3FF.#.,FF.9...\n1149\t..FFF..,FFF.#..\n1150\t..FF...,FF.....\n1151\tf......,.....f.\n1152\t```\n1153\t**Capital Citadel** (`capital_citadel`, 17 × 13): used by Rimeholt, Avalorn, Brazenhold, Ambergate. A ring of ramparts round the courtyard and Keep, with a west gate on the road and a south-west gate. Fliers cross the walls; walkers must use a gate. Dressing follows the realm (ice, blossom, sandstone, timber).\n1154\t```\n1155\t..fffff.......fff\n1156\t.fffff........ff.\n1157\t..ff.............\n1158\t......h...####...\n1159\t.1........#8gg#..\n1160\t.....h...#gggg#ff\n1161\t,,,,,,,,,,ggK7g#f\n1162\t.2.......#gggg#ff\n1163\t..........#g9g#..\n1164\t......h..,g###...\n1165\t.ff3....,,.......\n1166\tfff..,,,......ff.\n1167\t.ff.,,ff......fff\n1168\t```\n1169\t**Meridian Clockyard** (`meridian_clockyard`, 17 × 13): used by Meridian. The clock-city: an outer wall with three gates, gear blocks inside, and the Great Clock tower as the Keep.\n1170\t```\n1171\t..,,...........rr\n1172\t...,,,,.......rrr\n1173\t...rr..,g####..rr\n1174\t..rrr..#gg8g#....\n1175\t.1.rr..#g#gg##...\n1176\t......#gggggg#...\n1177\t,2,,,,,gggK7g##..\n1178\t......#gggggg#...\n1179\t.3.rr..#g#gg##...\n1180\t..rrr..#gg9g#....\n1181\t...rr..,g####..rr\n1182\t...,,,,.......rrr\n1183\t..,,...........rr\n1184\t```\n1185\t**Clockwork Sanctum** (`clockwork_sanctum`, 15 × 13): used by the final battle. A round dial chamber. The Gray Knight's troop starts at the centre (7 8 9) and the player's troops enter from the south (1 2 3). Season Dials D stand at north, east, south and west. Its rules follow the map.\n1186\t```\n1187\t###############\n1188\t####gggggg#####"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"8be1e860-9257-488b-a939-de451eda3c3f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:02:39.362Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/PLAN.md","content":"- `cone2` / `cone3`: hexes within 2 or 3 of the user, inside a 120° wedge facing one of the 6 directions;\n- `line3` / `line4`: a straight hex line from the user in one of the 6 directions.\n\n\"Foes\" or \"allies\" filters who is touched. Status numbers are the base chance (§5.6). P is the power; a heal's P is the\nbase amount.\n\n| id | Name | Kind | Elem | P | Range | Area | MP | Mobile | Effect / notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| rally | Rally | special | — | — | self | self-r1 allies | 4 | yes | Valor 2 bells |\n| charge | Charge | special | user's | 1.3 | 1 | single | 5 | yes | must move 2+ hexes first |\n| shieldwall | Shield Wall | special | — | — | self | adj allies | 6 | yes | Warded 1 bell |\n| holystrike | Holy Strike | special | none | 1.5 | 1 | single | 8 | yes | ignores element; ×1.5 vs Hour |\n| layonhands | Lay on Hands | special | — | heal 60 | 1 | single ally | 10 | yes | |\n| aimedshot | Aimed Shot | special | user's | 1.2 | 2–4 | single | 4 | no | +20 hit |\n| volley | Volley | special | user's | 0.8 | 3–5 | r1 | 8 | no | |\n| pinning | Pinning Shot | special | user's | 0.9 | 2–4 | single | 6 | yes | Chill 70 |\n| piercing | Piercing Arrow | special | user's | 1.1 | — | line4 | 10 | no | every unit on the line |\n| eagleeye | Eagle Eye | passive | | | | | | | bows +1 max range |\n| bramble, cinder, galeleaves, hoarfrost, timeshear | Bramble / Cinder / Gale of Leaves / Hoarfrost / Time Shear (Bolts) | spell | Sp / Su / Au / Wi / Hour | 14 | 1–4 | single | 5 | no | Time Shear ignores the Tide |\n| drowse, kindle, rot, frostbite, stophex | Drowse / Kindle / Rot / Frostbite / Stop (Hexes) | spell | Sp / Su / Au / Wi / Hour | — | 1–4 | single | 6 | no | Sleep 60 / Burn 70 / Poison 70 / Chill 70 / Stop 40 |\n| bramblestorm, cinderstorm, leafstorm, froststorm, hourstorm | Bramble / Cinder / Leaf / Frost / Hour Storm | spell | Sp / Su / Au / Wi / Hour | 22 | 1–4 | r1 | 10 | no | Cinder Storm on a forest sets it burning (§5.7) |\n| verdanttempest, solarflare, harvestmoon, blizzard | Verdant Tempest / Solar Flare / Harvest Moon / Blizzard (Tempests) | spell | Sp / Su / Au / Wi | 34 | 1–5 | r2 | 16 | no | Sleep 20 / Burn 30 (and burns forests) / drains 25% of damage to the caster / Chill 30 |\n| manasiphon | Mana Siphon | spell | — | — | 1–4 | single | 2 | no | steals 12 MP |\n| haste | Haste | spell | — | — | 0–3 | single ally | 8 | no | Haste 2 bells |\n| mend | Mend | spell | — | heal 30 | 0–3 | single ally | 5 | no | |\n| purify | Purify | spell | — | — | 0–3 | single ally | 4 | no | clears statuses and debuffs |\n| renewal | Renewal | spell | — | heal 24 | 0–3 | r1 allies | 10 | no | |\n| wardofseasons | Ward of Seasons | spell | — | — | 0–3 | r1 allies | 9 | no | Warded 2 bells |\n| greaterrenewal | Greater Renewal | spell | — | heal 36 | 0–4 | r2 allies | 16 | no | |\n| dawnlight | Dawnlight | spell | none | 26 | 1–4 | r1 foes | 14 | no | ×1.5 vs Hour; ignores the Tide |\n| goad | Goad | special | — | — | 1–2 | one own monster | 3 | yes | Valor and Haste 1 bell |\n| packtactics | Pack Tactics | passive | | | | | | | the knight's monsters +10 hit |\n| roar | Roar | special | — | — | self | self-r2 foes | 6 | yes | Weakened 60 |\n| callofwild | Call of the Wild | special | — | 20% max HP | self | own troop's monsters | 12 | yes | heals |\n| bondoffang | Bond of Fang | special | — | — | Ward | one own monster in Ward | 10 | yes | Valor, Warded and Haste 2 bells |\n| verdantoath | Verdant Oath | special | Sp | heal 10% | self | allies in Ward | 10 | yes | Warded 2 bells |\n| warcry | Warcry | special | Su | — | self | allies in Ward | 8 | yes | Valor 2 bells |\n| quietcounsel | Quiet Counsel | special | Au | — | self | allies in Ward | 10 | yes | Haste 1 bell |\n| reaping | Reaping | spell | Au | 20 | 1–3 | single | 8 | no | heals the caster 50% of the damage |\n| madgambit | Mad Gambit | special | Wi | 30 (magic) | 1–3 | single | 6 | yes | 25%: misfires and Chills the Duke instead |\n| frozenhour | Frozen Hour | spell | Wi | — | 1–4 | single | 12 | no | Stop 70 |\n| restore | Restore | spell | Hour | 50% max HP | 0–3 | single ally | 14 | no | |\n| turning | Turning | special | none | 40 (magic) | 1–3 | r1 foes | 0, once per battle | yes | ×2 vs Hour; a Gray Knight it hits loses Timeless until the end of the next bell |\n| ambush | Ambush | passive | | | | | | | +30% damage when attacking from a forest hex |\n| thirteenthstroke | Thirteenth Stroke | special | Hour | 1.6 | 1 | r1 foes | 0 | yes | |\n| still | Still | special | Hour | — | self | self-r2 foes | 0, every 3rd bell | yes | Stop 70 |\n| unmaking | Unmaking | spell | Hour | 25% of target's max HP | 1–3 | single | 20 | no | ignores DEF, element and Tide |\n| timeless | Timeless | passive | | | | | | | immune to effects and the Tide; takes ×0.5 damage until the four Season Dials are lit (§6.10) or Turning hits |\n| pollenpuff | Pollen Puff | special | Sp | — | self | self-r1 foes | 6 | yes | Sleep 50 |\n| entangle | Entangle | special | Sp | 0.6 | 1–2 | single | 5 | no | Chill 70 |\n| scream | Mandrake Scream | special | Sp | — | self | self-r2 foes | 10 | no | Sleep 50 |\n| sleepdust | Sleep Dust | spell | Sp | — | 1–3 | r1 foes | 8 | no | Sleep 60 |\n| thorns | Thorns | passive | | | | | | | melee attackers take 10% of the damage they deal |\n| rootsweep | Root Sweep | special | Sp | 0.9 | — | adj foes | 6 | yes | |\n| dive | Dive | special | user's | 1.2 | 1 | single | 4 | yes | fliers; must move 2+ hexes first |\n| torrent | Torrent | special | Sp | 1.0 | — | line3 | 6 | no | |\n| coil | Coil | special | user's | 0.8 | 1 | single | 4 | yes | Chill 60 |\n| emberspit | Ember Spit | special | Su | 0.9 | 1–2 | single | 3 | yes | Burn 30 |\n| firebreath | Fire Breath | special | Su | 1.2 | — | cone2 (dragons: cone3) | 8 | no | Burn 25 |\n| howl | Howl | special | — | — | self | self-r2 allies | 5 | yes | Valor 1 bell |\n| pounce | Pounce | special | user's | 1.2 | 1 | single | 5 | yes | |\n| rebirth | Rebirth | passive | | | | | | | once per battle, at 0 HP it rises again with 30% HP |\n| sunriddle | Sun Riddle | special | Su | — | self | self-r1 foes | 8 | no | Sleep 50 |\n| wispfire | Wisp Fire | special | Au | 0.9 (magic) | 1–3 | single | 4 | yes | |\n| fear | Fear | special | Au | — | self | self-r1 foes | 5 | yes | Weakened 60 |\n| drain | Drain | special | user's | 1.0 | 1 | single | 4 | yes | heals 50% of the damage |\n| gravechill | Grave Chill | special | Wi | — | self | self-r1 foes | 7 | no | Chill 40 |\n| gale | Gale | special | Au | 0.7 | 1 | single | 5 | yes | pushes the target 1 hex away; if blocked, 4 more damage |\n| trample | Trample | special | user's | 1.0 | — | line3 | 6 | yes | |\n| thickhide | Thick Hide | passive | | | | | | | DEF +10% |\n| frostarmor | Frost Armor | special | Wi | — | self | self | 5 | yes | DEF +40% 2 bells |\n| avalanche | Avalanche | special | Wi | 1.0 | 1–2 | r1 | 9 | no | |\n| hurlice | Hurl Ice | special | Wi | 1.0 | 2–3 | single | 5 | no | |\n| frostfang | Frost Fang | passive | | | | | | | basic attacks Chill 30 |\n| frostbreath | Frost Breath | special | Wi | 1.2 | — | cone3 | 8 | no | Chill 40 |\n| tailsweep | Tail Sweep | special | user's | 0.9 | — | adj foes | 6 | yes | |\n| windup | Wind-up | special | — | — | self | self | 3 | yes | its next basic attack ×1.5 |\n| pendulum | Pendulum | special | Hour | 1.1 | — | adj foes | 6 | yes | |\n| stopbite | Stopping Bite | passive | | | | | | | basic attacks Stop 20 |\n| engulf | Engulf | special | user's | 0.9 | 1 | single | 4 | yes | Poison 40 |\n| regenerate | Regenerate | passive | | | | | | | heals 10% max HP at its turn start |\n| groundpound | Ground Pound | special | user's | 1.0 | — | adj foes | 7 | yes | |\n| screech | Screech | special | — | — | self | self-r1 foes | 5 | yes | Weakened 60 |\n\n### 6.8 Bestiary (30 species, 3 forms each)\n**Form and level rules:**\n- Tier 2 = tier 1 × 1.35 (HP, MP, ATK, DEF, INT), AGI +2. Tier 3 = tier 1 × 1.75, AGI +4, MOV +1 for fliers.\n- At level L, every stat is `round(formBase × (1 + 0.05 × (L − 1)))`.\n- Rank is the bond cost and doesn't change with form. Upkeep ×1.5 at tier 2 and ×2 at tier 3.\n- Each form keeps the skills before it and adds its own (column \"Skills\").\n\nFlags: `fl` flier, `sw` swimmer, `fo` floater. The \"Rig\" column is the look; §7.5 defines the rig kinds.\n\n| id | Forms | Elem | Size | Rank | Flags | Tier 1: HP/MP/ATK/DEF/INT/AGI/MOV | Basic attack (P, range) | Skills: T1; +T2; +T3 | Cost / upkeep | Rig |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sproutling | Sproutling → Bloomkin → Mandragora | Sp | S | 1 | | 38/12/12/9/12/13/4 | Headbutt 1.0, 1 | Pollen Puff; +Entangle; +Mandrake Scream | 30 / 2 | Blob R6, leaf ears, a sprout on top; Mandragora gets a root crown |\n| pixie | Pixie → Sylph → Faerie Queen | Sp | S, S, M | 1 | fl | 30/24/8/6/16/20/6 | Prick 0.7, 1 | Mend; +Haste; +Sleep Dust | 45 / 3 | Humanoid chibi .55 + insect `E.Wings`, glow |\n| treant | Thornback Treant → Elder Treant → Worldroot | Sp | L | 4 | | 120/10/22/22/8/5/3 | Slam 1.1, 1 | Thorns, Entangle; +Renewal; +Root Sweep | 120 / 8 | Humanoid bulky 1.6, bark colours, leaf crown, long arms, hunch .3 |\n| unicorn | Unicorn → Alicorn → Dawnhorn | Sp | M, M, L | 3 | T2+ fl | 80/20/19/14/14/16/6 | Gore 1.1, 1 | Charge, Mend; +Dive; +Dawnlight | 90 / 5 | Beast quad `horse` + horn; feather wings from T2 |\n| rillserpent | Rillserpent → Floodwyrm → Thaw Leviathan | Sp | L | 4 | sw | 110/18/21/16/14/9/4 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Torrent, Coil; +Bramble Storm; +Verdant Tempest | 130 / 8 | Beast serpent, fins, river-green scales |\n| salamander | Salamander → Firedrake → Magma Drake | Su | S, M, M | 2 | | 50/12/16/12/10/12/4 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Ember Spit; +Fire Breath; +Cinder Storm | 45 / 3 | Beast quad `lizard` (low, long tail), ember glow |\n| cinderhound | Cinderhound → Blazehound → Twinflame Hound | Su | M | 2 | | 70/10/20/12/8/14/5 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Fire Breath; +Howl; +Pounce | 70 / 4 | Beast quad `hound` + flame mane |\n| sunbird | Sunbird → Phoenix → Solar Roc | Su | M, M, L | 3 | fl | 60/18/17/10/14/18/6 | Talon 1.0, 1 | Dive; +Rebirth; +Solar Flare | 90 / 5 | Beast `avian`, fire tail |\n| wyvern | Wyvern → Sun Dragon → Elder Sun Dragon | Su | L | 4 | fl | 120/16/25/18/12/10/5 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Tail Sweep, Fire Breath (cone3); +Dive; +Solar Flare | 160 / 10 | Beast `drake`: 2 legs + wings (Wyvern), 4 legs + wings (dragons) |\n| sunmane | Sunmane Lion → Solar Chimera → Noon Sphinx | Su | M, L, L | 3 | | 85/12/22/14/9/15/5 | Claw 1.0, 1 | Roar, Pounce; +Fire Breath; +Sun Riddle | 100 / 6 | Beast quad `cat` + mane; wings and a snake tail from T2 |\n| jacklamp | Jack-o'-Lamp → Lantern Lord → Will of the Wisps | Au | S, S, M | 1 | fo | 36/20/10/8/15/14/4 | Spook 0.8, 1 | Wisp Fire; +Fear; +Leaf Storm | 30 / 2 | Blob: an orange pumpkin with a glowing carved face and a flame on top; floats |\n| scarecrow | Scarecrow → Harvest Reaper → Grim Thresher | Au | M | 2 | | 65/10/18/12/10/12/4 | Scythe 1.1, 1 | Fear; +Reaping; +Trample | 60 / 4 | Humanoid, straw palette, pointed hat, patched coat, scythe drawn from the hands |\n| ghoul | Barrow Ghoul → Wight → Barrow King | Au | M | 2 | | 70/12/19/13/9/10/4 | Claw 1.0, 1 (Poison 25) | Drain; +Grave Chill; +Rot | 55 / 3 | Humanoid, hunch .6, grey-green skin, eyeGlow, rags |\n| griffin | Griffin → Gilded Griffin → Storm Griffin | Au | L | 4 | fl | 105/14/23/15/12/15/6 | Talon 1.0, 1 | Dive, Gale; +Leaf Storm; +Harvest Moon | 140 / 9 | Beast `griffin`: eagle front and wings, lion rear |\n| tusker | Great Tusker → Ironhide Boar → Boar King | Au | M, M, L | 3 | | 85/6/21/16/4/10/5 | Gore 1.1, 1 | Trample; +Thick Hide; +Roar | 70 / 4 | Beast quad `boar`, tusks, bristles |\n| snowkit | Snowkit → Rime Sprite → Aurora Wisp | Wi | S | 1 | T3 fo | 36/18/11/9/14/15/4 | Snowball 0.8, 1–2 | Frostbite; +Frost Armor; +Frost Storm | 30 / 2 | Blob, white, cat ears, frost sparkle; aurora glow at T3 |\n| frostwolf | Frostwolf → Dire Frostwolf → Long-Night Wolf | Wi | M, M, L | 2 | | 68/8/20/11/7/16/6 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Howl, Frost Fang; +Pounce; +Frost Breath | 65 / 4 | Beast quad `wolf`, white-blue |\n| icegolem | Ice Golem → Glacier Colossus → Hoarfrost Titan | Wi | L | 4 | | 130/8/24/26/6/4/3 | Slam 1.1, 1 | Frost Armor; +Avalanche; +Thorns | 130 / 8 | Humanoid bulky 1.5, ice-crystal colours, cyan eyeGlow |\n| yeti | Yeti → Great Yeti → Yeti Matriarch | Wi | L | 4 | | 115/8/25/17/6/8/4 | Maul 1.15, 1 | Hurl Ice; +Roar; +Avalanche | 110 / 7 | Humanoid bulky 1.5, white fur, no weapon, hunch .3 |\n| frostwyrm | Frost Wyrm → Rime Dragon → Winter's Heart | Wi | L | 5 | fl | 125/18/24/19/14/9/5 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Frost Breath, Tail Sweep; +Dive; +Blizzard | 170 / 11 | Beast `drake`, 4 legs + wings, crest, icy palette |\n| minute | Minute → Hour-Wisp → Second Hand | Hour | S | 1 | fo | 34/16/11/10/13/17/5 | Tick 0.8, 1 | Stop (Hex); +Haste; +Time Shear | 40 / 2 | Blob: a brass sphere with a clock face, small orbiting gears |\n| clockwork | Clockwork Sentinel → Tick Knight → Pendulum Paladin | Hour | M | 3 | | 80/8/21/20/8/9/4 | Slash 1.0, 1 | Wind-up; +Shield Wall; +Pendulum | 80 / 5 | Humanoid heroic 1.25, brass plate, helmet, gear halo |\n| gearhound | Gearhound → Clockwork Hound → Chronohound | Hour | M | 2 | | 65/6/19/15/6/15/6 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Pounce; +Howl; +Stopping Bite | 60 / 4 | Beast quad `hound`, metal palette, gear joints |\n| stillwraith | Stillwraith → Hollow Hour → Unhour | Hour | M | 3 | fo | 60/30/10/10/20/13/5 | Spook 0.8, 1 | Time Shear, Stop; +Drain; +Hour Storm | 85 / 5 | Humanoid robe and hood at alpha .75, a clock face for a head, floats 6 up |\n| pendulumwyrm | Pendulum Wyrm → Great Pendulum → The Long Hand | Hour | L | 5 | | 150/20/26/22/18/8/4 | Bite 1.0, 1 | Pendulum, Time Shear; +Coil; +Hour Storm | 200 / 12 (Meridian only) | Beast serpent, metal segments, a swinging pendulum disc for a tail |\n| skeleton | Skeleton → Skeleton Knight → Bone Lord | Au | M | 2 | | 60/6/18/12/5/11/4 | Slash 1.0, 1 | —; +Shield Wall; +Charge | 50 / 3 | Humanoid build `skeleton`, rusty sword |\n| bat | Giant Bat → Vampire Bat → Night Bat | Wi | S, S, M | 1 | fl | 32/8/12/7/8/19/6 | Bite 0.9, 1 (heals 25% of damage) | Dive; +Drain; +Fear | 30 / 2 | Blob with wings and fangs, dark palette |\n| slime | Slime → Royal Slime → Slime Sovereign | Sp | S | 1 | | 44/10/11/12/9/9/3 | Headbutt 0.9, 1 | Engulf; +Regenerate; +Bramble Storm | 25 / 2 | Blob, translucent teal; a crown from T2 |\n| ogre | Ogre → Ogre Chieftain → Ogre Warlord | Su | L | 4 | | 125/6/27/16/4/7/4 | Maul 1.15, 1 | Roar; +Charge; +Ground Pound | 110 / 7 | Humanoid bulky 1.5, grey-green skin, club |\n| harpy | Harpy → Harpy Matron → Storm Harpy | Sp | M | 2 | fl | 55/14/17/10/12/17/6 | Talon 1.0, 1 | Dive; +Gale; +Screech | 55 / 3 | Humanoid 1.0 with feather `E.Wings`, bare taloned feet |\n\n### 6.9 Items (33; there are no shops: items come from quests, events and castle treasuries)\n\n| id | Name | Slot | Who | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ashspear | Ashwood Spear | weapon | Warrior, Beast | ATK +3 |\n| rimesteel | Rimesteel Sword | weapon | Warrior | ATK +5; a Winter wielder +5% damage |\n| sunforged | Sunforged Blade | weapon | Warrior, Sun Sovereign | ATK +7 |\n| cleaver | Brigand's Cleaver | weapon | Warrior | ATK +6, DEF −2 |\n| hawthornbow | Hawthorn Bow | weapon | Ranger | ATK +4 |\n| yewlongbow | Yew Longbow | weapon | Ranger | ATK +6, max range +1 |\n| willowstaff | Willow Staff | weapon | Mage, Cleric, staff rulers | INT +4 |\n| lanternstaff | Lantern Staff | weapon | Mage, Cleric, staff rulers | INT +6; Autumn spells +10% |\n| tomeofthaw | Tome of Thaw | weapon | Mage | INT +5; Spring spells +10% |\n| hourglassrod | Hourglass Rod | weapon | Mage, Cleric, rulers | INT +8, MP +10 |\n| thornwhip | Thorn Whip | weapon | Beast | ATK +4; Lash range 1–3 |\n| jerkin | Leather Jerkin | armor | all | DEF +3 |\n| hauberk | Mail Hauberk | armor | Warrior, Beast, rulers | DEF +6, AGI −1 |\n| thornmail | Thornmail | armor | Warrior | DEF +5; Thorns |\n| frostplate | Frostplate | armor | Warrior, rulers | DEF +8; immune to Chill |\n| robeofseasons | Robe of Seasons | armor | Mage, Cleric, rulers | DEF +3, INT +4 |\n| spurs | Swift Spurs | accessory | all | MOV +1 |\n| signet | Signet of Command | accessory | all | Bond +2 |\n| bannerpin | Banner Pin | accessory | all | Ward +1 |\n| amuletoftides | Amulet of Tides | accessory | all | the wearer's Tide bonus ×2 |\n| wardingcharm | Warding Charm | accessory | all | immune to Sleep and Stop |\n| mendingring | Ring of Mending | accessory | all | heals 10% max HP at its troop's turn start |\n| horseshoe | Lucky Horseshoe | accessory | all | good quest outcomes ×1.15 |\n| herb | Healing Herb | consumable | — | heals 40 HP |\n| draught | Golden Draught | consumable | — | heals to full HP |\n| ether | Ether Vial | consumable | — | +20 MP |\n| remedy | Remedy | consumable | — | clears statuses and debuffs |\n| manaseed | Mana Seed | consumable (Muster) | — | +60 realm mana |\n| springseed | Spring Seed | promotion | Spring monsters | promotes (T1 → T2 from Lv 6; T2 → T3 from Lv 16) |\n| summerember | Summer Ember | promotion | Summer monsters | as above |\n| autumnacorn | Autumn Acorn | promotion | Autumn monsters | as above |\n| wintershard | Winter Shard | promotion | Winter monsters | as above |\n| writ | Writ of Knighthood | special | knights | allows a tier-3 class change from Lv 20 |\n\nStarting inventories: each season-realm starts with 2 Healing Herbs and 1 Remedy, plus its season's promotion item. The\nDominion starts with 3 Ether Vials. Quest pools by region are listed in §6.11.\n\n### 6.10 Battle maps (13)\nEach map is a list of rows, top row first, one character per hex (codes in §5.7; anchors `1 2 3` attacker, `7 8 9` defender, `1 2 3 4` seats). Odd rows sit half a hex to the right. A script built and checked every map below: every row has the same length; each anchor appears once and has at least 7 free hexes within 2 steps; and the Keep can be reached from every attacker anchor in all four seasons, floods and ice included. Keep that check as a test (§14). `flood` marks maps whose shallows flood in Spring.\n\n**Border Meadow** (`border_meadow`, 13 × 9): used by the tutorial (§6.13) and Skirmish. A meadow with a stream, a bridge on the road and a ruined watchtower Keep. Two troops a side: anchors 1 2 against 7 8.\n```\n..f.....h.ff.\n.ff.1.....~.f\n......f...~h.\n..2..f...~...\n,,,,,,,,,b,K7\n....f....~.8.\n.f.......~h..\n..h..f...~..f\n...f.....~.ff\n```\n**River Ford** (`river_ford`, 15 × 11, flood): used by Rainmere, Thawgate. A river splits the field, with two fords and one bridge on the road. In Spring the fords flood and only the bridge crosses; in Winter the river freezes into open ground.\n```\nff..h..w...hfff\n.f.1...w....ff.\n.....h.~..8..f.\nf......w...h...\n..2.f..w..h....\n,,,,,,,b,,,K7..\n..3.f..w..h....\nf......w...h...\n.....h.~..9..f.\n.f.....w....ff.\nff..h..w...hfff\n```\n**Forest Hold** (`forest_hold`, 15 × 11): used by Kestrel Spire, Thornwick, Lanternfall. Thick woods, a winding road and a clearing Keep between two hills. Forest slows large units (cost 3); in Summer fire can burn it open.\n```\n...ff....ff..ff\n..fff...fff.fff\n..1ff.ff.f8..ff\n.....fff..h.h..\n......f,,,.....\n,2...,,..,,K7..\n..,,,,..ff.....\n....ff.fffh.h..\n.f3.fff.ff9..ff\nfff.ff..fff.fff\n.ff......ff..ff\n```\n**Mountain Pass** (`mountain_pass`, 15 × 11): used by Wolfsgate, Cinderwall. Peaks squeeze the field into a pass 3 to 5 hexes wide, with ruins in it. Fliers cross the peaks. The Keep holds the pass's mouth.\n```\nmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm\nmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm\n...mmmmmmmmm...\n..f.hmm.mm.8h..\n..1...r........\n,2,,,,,,,,,K7,.\n.f3.....r......\n....hmm.mm.9h..\n...mmmmmmmmm...\nmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm\nmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm\n```\n**Hill Fort** (`hill_fort`, 15 × 11): used by Midnight Keep, Dawnwatch, Lionsreach. The Keep crowns a ring of hills (+10% DEF, +1 range for bows) with woods on both flanks.\n```\n..ff.fff.....ff\n.fff.ff.....fff\n..ff.........ff\n.1..h....8hh...\n.........hhhh..\n,2,,,,,,,hK7hf.\n.........hhhh..\n.3..h....9hh...\n...ff........ff\n..fffff.....fff\n...fffff.....ff\n```\n**Marsh Keep** (`marsh_keep`, 15 × 11, flood): used by Russetmoor, Beltane Ford. Bogs and pools around a causeway road. Summer dries the swamp; Spring floods the pools.\n```\n...............\n..fss.fss......\n...sss.sss.8.f.\n.1.ss~.ss~..h..\n...............\n,2,,,,,,,,,K7..\n......sss......\n.3ss.ss~s...9..\n..ssssssss.~ss.\n..ss.sss~..sss.\n......sss...ss.\n```\n**Lakeside** (`lakeside`, 15 × 11): used by Frostmere, Primrose Ford. A lake fills the north and the land route bends south around it. In Winter the lake freezes and opens a straight path to the Keep.\n```\n.fff........ff.\n.ff..LLLL..fff.\n.....LLLLLh.ff.\n.1...LLLLL..8..\n......LLLL.....\n..2...LLL..K7..\n...........,...\n,3,.....,,,9...\n.ff,,,,,,h...ff\nffffff......fff\n.ff.ff.......ff\n```\n**Ruined Abbey** (`ruined_abbey`, 15 × 11): used by Vesper Hall, Ashbarrow, Hallowmere. Broken walls (blocked) and ruins (+10% DEF) around an abbey-tower Keep.\n```\n.ff........ffff\nfff........ffff\n.ff..#..#....ff\n.1...#.r...r8..\n........r.r....\n,2,,,,,,,,,K7..\n..........r....\n.3...r.r.#.r9..\n..ff..#..#...ff\n.fff........fff\n..ff.........ff\n```\n**Crossroads** (`crossroads`, 15 × 11): used by Noonspire, Goldspur, Lammas Cross. Two roads cross among fields, with houses (blocked) making lanes. Summer wheat hides units (+10 evade).\n```\nf......,.....f.\n..FF...,FF.....\n..FFF..,FFF.#..\n.1FF.#.,FF.8...\n.......,.#.....\n,2,,,,,,,,,K7,,\n.......,.#.....\n.3FF.#.,FF.9...\n..FFF..,FFF.#..\n..FF...,FF.....\nf......,.....f.\n```\n**Capital Citadel** (`capital_citadel`, 17 × 13): used by Rimeholt, Avalorn, Brazenhold, Ambergate. A ring of ramparts round the courtyard and Keep, with a west gate on the road and a south-west gate. Fliers cross the walls; walkers must use a gate. Dressing follows the realm (ice, blossom, sandstone, timber).\n```\n..fffff.......fff\n.fffff........ff.\n..ff.............\n......h...####...\n.1........#8gg#..\n.....h...#gggg#ff\n,,,,,,,,,,ggK7g#f\n.2.......#gggg#ff\n..........#g9g#..\n......h..,g###...\n.ff3....,,.......\nfff..,,,......ff.\n.ff.,,ff......fff\n```\n**Meridian Clockyard** (`meridian_clockyard`, 17 × 13): used by Meridian. The clock-city: an outer wall with three gates, gear blocks inside, and the Great Clock tower as the Keep.\n```\n..,,...........rr\n...,,,,.......rrr\n...rr..,g####..rr\n..rrr..#gg8g#....\n.1.rr..#g#gg##...\n......#gggggg#...\n,2,,,,,gggK7g##..\n......#gggggg#...\n.3.rr..#g#gg##...\n..rrr..#gg9g#....\n...rr..,g####..rr\n...,,,,.......rrr\n..,,...........rr\n```\n**Clockwork Sanctum** (`clockwork_sanctum`, 15 × 13): used by the final battle. A round dial chamber. The Gray Knight's troop starts at the centre (7 8 9) and the player's troops enter from the south (1 2 3). Season Dials D stand at north, east, south and west. Its rules follow the map.\n```\n###############\n####gggggg#####","numLines":330,"startLine":859,"totalLines":2417}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VVkKJ8nc9Ma7xvwUCBKo4c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrVUPkVRcjzoseXcTfc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012uSfkVVDLRmkqWh1EurczD","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/PLAN.md","offset":1189,"limit":330},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13242,"cache_read_input_tokens":58767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13242},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"f1baec6b-77fb-4780-91f9-d29a5e9c2bba","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:02:41.933Z","request_id":"req_011CghrVUANYqbbtajHK9RN4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012uSfkVVDLRmkqWh1EurczD":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/PLAN.md","offset":1189,"limit":330}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012uSfkVVDLRmkqWh1EurczD","type":"tool_result","content":"1189\t####gggDggg####\n1190\t###gggggggg####\n1191\t###gg#ggg#gg###\n1192\t##gggg8ggggg###\n1193\t##gDgggK7ggDg##\n1194\t##gggg9ggggg###\n1195\t###gg#ggg#gg###\n1196\t###gggggggg####\n1197\t####gggDggg####\n1198\t####g1g2g3#####\n1199\t###############\n1200\t```\n1201\t**Wheel Shrine** (`wheel_shrine`, 15 × 13): used by Skirmish and the AI Hub. Four corners, seats 1 to 4 (Spring NE, Summer SE, Autumn SW, Winter NW), around the Hour Shrine (K) in its courtyard. With 2 sides use seats 1 and 3; with 3 sides use 1, 2 and 3.\n1202\t```\n1203\t..........~....\n1204\tf4.f..f..~...1~\n1205\t........~......\n1206\t..f..f.~....~..\n1207\t...........~...\n1208\t.f..f.gg..~....\n1209\tF.....gKg...h..\n1210\t....F.gg......h\n1211\t..F......h.....\n1212\tF.....F....h...\n1213\t....F..........\n1214\t.3......h....2.\n1215\tF.....F...h....\n1216\t```\n1217\t\n1218\t**Clockwork Sanctum rules (the final battle):**\n1219\t- The player wins when the Gray Knight falls; that is the ruler rule. If he stands at the end of bell 12, the thirteenth bell tolls and the battle is lost (§4.17).\n1220\t- **The Hour Hand:** at the end of each bell it points along one of the 6 hex directions from the centre, moving one step clockwise per bell. Every player unit on that `line6` (to the wall) rolls Stop 70. The next bell's line glows faintly all bell long, so players can step aside.\n1221\t- **Season Dials (`D`):** at the end of a bell, a dial with a player unit on it lights and stays lit. A Dominion unit standing on a lit dial at a bell's end puts it out. When all four are lit at once, \"The Wheel turns!\": Timeless breaks for the rest of the battle (full damage, effects apply), the Gray Knight's DEF drops 40%, and the Hour Hand stops.\n1222\t- **At 50% HP** the Gray Knight calls 2 Second Hands (tier-3 Minutes, level 22). They head for lit dials, and he uses Still every 2 bells instead of every 3.\n1223\t- **Lunete (if she is present):** her Turning (×2 against Hour) breaks Timeless for one bell, and a dial she stands on lights at once instead of at the bell's end.\n1224\t- The troops that took Meridian enter, healed to full (\"the Wheel's light\"), plus up to one more troop from a castle adjacent to Meridian.\n1225\t\n1226\t**Wheel Shrine rules (Skirmish \"Banners of the Wheel\" and the AI Hub):**\n1227\t- A free-for-all of 2 to 4 sides, one troop each (a ruler at level 10 with 2 monsters, §11.4), lasting 6 bells.\n1228\t- **The season turns every bell:** bell 1 Spring, 2 Summer, 3 Autumn, 4 Winter, 5 Spring, 6 Summer. The Tide and terrain transforms are applied again at each bell's start.\n1229\t- **Glory:** +1 for every 5 damage dealt, +10 per monster KO, +25 per knight KO, +5 at each bell's end for the side holding the Shrine (`K`), and +10 at the end if your knight still stands.\n1230\t- The Shrine (`K`) gives whoever stands on it the Keep's +25% DEF and 10% healing per bell. Highest glory wins; ties share a place. A knight that falls takes its troop out, but its glory still counts.\n1231\t\n1232\t### 6.11 Quest sites (one per castle; a quest is sent from the castle itself, and a story site from any owned castle adjacent to it)\n1233\t\n1234\t**Regional pools:**\n1235\t\n1236\t| Region | Items | Beasts | Wanderers |\n1237\t|---|---|---|---|\n1238\t| Winter | herb, wintershard, rimesteel, frostplate, wardingcharm, yewlongbow | snowkit, frostwolf, yeti, bat | galeron (from Autumn, Year 1), ettard |\n1239\t| Spring | herb, springseed, tomeofthaw, hawthornbow, spurs, willowstaff | sproutling, pixie, unicorn, slime | galeron |\n1240\t| Summer | herb, summerember, sunforged, hauberk, bannerpin, cleaver | salamander, cinderhound, sunbird, sunmane | blanchefleur |\n1241\t| Autumn | herb, autumnacorn, lanternstaff, horseshoe, robeofseasons, jerkin | jacklamp, scarecrow, ghoul, tusker | blanchefleur, ettard |\n1242\t| Hour | ether, writ, hourglassrod, signet, amuletoftides, spurs | minute, gearhound | — |\n1243\t\n1244\tA cross-quarter site uses both neighbours' pools.\n1245\t\n1246\t| Site | Castle | Seasons away | Focus (+10) | Extra |\n1247\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1248\t| The Lake of Silent Bells | Rimeholt | 2 | Training | Hoarfast: part of `w_lucid_hour` |\n1249\t| The Howling Scar | Wolfsgate | 1 | Beast | |\n1250\t| Nimue's Mere | Frostmere | 1 | Treasure | Ettard can be found |\n1251\t| The Kestrel Eyrie | Kestrel Spire | 2 | Wanderer | |\n1252\t| The Queen's Orchard | Avalorn | 1 | Treasure | |\n1253\t| The Briar Maze | Thornwick | 1 | Beast | unicorns ×2 |\n1254\t| The Weeping Weir | Rainmere | 1 | Beast | rillserpent added to the pool |\n1255\t| The Unicorn Glade | Primrose Ford | 2 | Beast | unicorns ×3 |\n1256\t| The Furnace Vaults | Brazenhold | 1 | Treasure | |\n1257\t| The Wyvern Roost | Goldspur | 2 | Beast | wyvern added at half weight |\n1258\t| The Ash Dunes | Cinderwall | 1 | Mana | |\n1259\t| The Lion Steps | Lionsreach | 1 | Wanderer | sunmane ×2 |\n1260\t| The Harvest Vault | Ambergate | 1 | Treasure | |\n1261\t| The Barrow Downs | Ashbarrow | 1 | Beast | Mishap +5 |\n1262\t| The Russet Bog | Russetmoor | 1 | Beast | tusker ×2 |\n1263\t| The Lantern Road | Lanternfall | 2 | Wanderer | Ettard can be found |\n1264\t| The Breaking Ice | Thawgate | 1 | Mana | draught added |\n1265\t| The Old Mill of Beltane | Beltane Ford | 1 | Treasure | the story site in `lunete_letter` |\n1266\t| The Lammas Fair | Lammas Cross | 1 | Wanderer | the hire choice in `blanchefleur_hire` |\n1267\t| The Hollow Abbey Crypts | Hallowmere | 2 | Treasure | skeleton and bat beasts; Ettard |\n1268\t| The Bell That Doesn't Ring | Midnight Keep | 2 | Treasure | |\n1269\t| The Sunrise Stair | Dawnwatch | 1 | Treasure | |\n1270\t| The Shadowless Square | Noonspire | 1 | Mana | |\n1271\t| The Evensong Crypt | Vesper Hall | 2 | Treasure | |\n1272\t| The Sleeping Court | Meridian | 2 | Treasure | a vignette of the sleeping Keeper |\n1273\t\n1274\tEach quest return plays a vignette of 2–4 lines with the knight's portrait, for example:\n1275\t- TREASURE: \"Sir Pelleas returns from the Briar Maze with thorns in his hair and a Spring Seed in his glove.\"\n1276\t- BEAST: \"A pixie followed Wren home from the Weeping Weir. It will not leave her shoulder.\"\n1277\t- MISHAP: \"Ragnell's patrol was ambushed at the Howling Scar. She will mend; the wolf will not.\"\n1278\t\n1279\tWrite 3 variants per outcome kind, and fill in `{$knight}`, `{$site}` and `{$thing}` with the story module's variables.\n1280\t\n1281\t### 6.12 Story\n1282\t\n1283\t#### 6.12.1 Premise (the back-story the scripts assume)\n1284\t- For three hundred years the four season-crowns kept the Concord of the Wheel. In Meridian, the Keeper of the Wheel,\n1285\t  King Aldous, wound the Great Clock that makes each season give way to the next.\n1286\t- Last winter Aldous fell into a sleep no physician could break, caught between two seconds, and the Clock began to\n1287\t  falter.\n1288\t- Lord Chancellor Meliant had lost his wife to an autumn and his son to a winter. He sealed the city, raised a banner\n1289\t  with no season and proclaimed the Hourless Dominion: when the Thirteenth Month comes, he will stop the Wheel, and no\n1290\t  one will ever grow old or die.\n1291\t- At his side stands the Gray Knight, Sir Nonesuch, who is not a man. He is the month that never was, and he feeds on\n1292\t  stopped time.\n1293\t- The Keeper's daughter, Princess Lunete, escaped through the Midnight Door and hides among the brigands of Beltane Ford.\n1294\t- Each crown claims the Hour Throne for its own reasons:\n1295\t  - Gareth of Verdance would wake the Keeper and restore the Concord;\n1296\t  - Morgause of Solmark would have Solmark set the Wheel and rule the calendar;\n1297\t  - Pellam of Amberlyn, old and ill, would end the war with the fewest dead;\n1298\t  - Mordrain of Hoarfast, mad with grief, would welcome an eternal winter \"where nothing rots and nothing ends\".\n1299\t- The chroniclers call the age the Brigantime: every knight a brigand, every road a war.\n1300\t\n1301\t#### 6.12.2 Style guide (match the source's register)\n1302\t- **Brief scenes:** 3 to 10 lines between seasons. Each line is at most about 90 characters, so a page shows it whole.\n1303\t- **An earnest, formal court register:** \"my liege\", \"Your Grace\", \"it is done\". No modern slang and no winking at the\n1304\t  player.\n1305\t- **Humour comes from the characters:** Pelleas's poetry, Dagonet's jests, Mordrain's riddles, Tic and Tac's\n1306\t  overlapping lines. It never mocks the stakes.\n1307\t- **Narration:** a heading per scene (\"Rimeholt. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime.\"), written in a pale colour with\n1308\t  markup `{c=#b8b0c8}...{/c}`.\n1309\t- **Markup is used sparingly:** `{w=.4}` for a beat, `{shake}` for a shout, `{s=12}` for dread, and colour for key words\n1310\t  (seasons in their colours, the Candle in red).\n1311\t- **Every speaker has a portrait and a voice** (§9.3). Emotes come from the story module: `!`, `?`, `dots`, `heart`,\n1312\t  `note`.\n1313\t- **Choices** are 2 short options, worded as intentions (\"Let him send it\", \"Burn the letter\").\n1314\t\n1315\t#### 6.12.3 How events run\n1316\t- Each event is `G.def('event', id, { when, realm, if, once: true, priority, stage, cast, nodes, effects })`.\n1317\t  - `when`: `tidings`, `muster` (on entering), `march`, `afterBattle`, `beforeBattle`, `questReturn` or `capture`.\n1318\t  - `realm`: a realm id, `'player'` (each human realm sees its own) or `'world'`.\n1319\t  - `if`: story-module conditions plus game tests: `season`, `year`, `owns:<castle>`, `holds:<knight>`,\n1320\t    `battle.vs:<realm>`, `flag`.\n1321\t- **At a Tidings:** play up to 3 eligible scenes in priority order (opening 100, story 50, recruit 30, flavour 10); the\n1322\t  rest roll over. An event marked `expires` drops after its window passes.\n1323\t- **Effects** are data: `{ addKnight, removeKnight, moveKnight, addMonster: [species, level, castle], addItem, mana,\n1324\t  flag, aiFlag: [realm, key, value], unlockSite, setTune }`, applied through `CampaignSim` commands, so effects are\n1325\t  saved and replayable.\n1326\t- **A stage** is one of 8 sets (§7.4). The cast stands on it, and the camera frames the speaker (`on.look`, as in the\n1327\t  tactics kit).\n1328\t\n1329\t#### 6.12.4 Scripts (write these as given; the rest follow the beats in §6.12.5)\n1330\t**`prologue` (an opening crawl over the title diorama; narrator; auto-advance every 5 s, or confirm):**\n1331\t1. In the Age of the Wheel, four crowns kept one calendar.\n1332\t2. Spring to Verdance. Summer to Solmark. Autumn to Amberlyn. Winter to Hoarfast.\n1333\t3. And in Meridian, the Calendar City, the Keeper of the Wheel wound the Great Clock, that each season might yield to the next.\n1334\t4. Last winter the Keeper fell into a sleep no physician could break, and the Great Clock began to falter.\n1335\t5. From the silent city rode Lord Chancellor Meliant, beneath a banner with no season.\n1336\t6. \"When the Thirteenth Month comes,\" he swore, \"I will stop the Wheel, and no one we love will ever grow old.\"\n1337\t7. Four crowns answered with steel. Every knight became a brigand; every road, a war.\n1338\t8. The chroniclers named the age the Brigantime.\n1339\t\n1340\t**`open_verdance` \"The Last Blossom\"** (stage: orchard court):\n1341\t- NARRATOR: Avalorn, the orchard court of Verdance. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime.\n1342\t- AMRIS: Your mother asked to rest beneath the oldest apple, my prince. It has not blossomed since the Clock faltered.\n1343\t- GARETH: Then it will blossom when the Wheel turns again. Not before.\n1344\t- LYNETTE: Brave words. Solmark is sharpening its swords, and Hoarfast's Duke laughs alone in his ice hall.\n1345\t- GARETH: Let them. We do not ride to take a throne, Lynette. We ride to wake a king.\n1346\t- PELLEAS: And should a throne fall into our laps along the way? I ask only for the ballads.\n1347\t- WREN: The unicorns won't graze. They smell the Clock's sickness on the east wind.\n1348\t- GARETH: Then we march before the petals fall. {shake}Sound the horn!{/shake}\n1349\t\n1350\t**`open_solmark` \"Noon Without End\"** (stage: sun hall):\n1351\t- NARRATOR: Brazenhold, the furnace-throne of Solmark. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime.\n1352\t- HESPER: Majesty, the Chancellor promises the Wheel will stop. Imagine it: a summer without end.\n1353\t- MORGAUSE: I have imagined it, Hesper. Every harvest burned to dust. Every child born into drought.\n1354\t- AGRAVAIN: Then we take Meridian and set the Wheel ourselves! Our summer, on our terms!\n1355\t- MORGAUSE: Now you sound like a Solmarker. {w=.4}A long noon, Sir Agravain, is still a noon that ends.\n1356\t- ELIDURE: The brigands at Beltane and Lammas grow fat on our roads. Shall I clear them, my queen?\n1357\t- BRENNOC: Take the wyverns. They've not flown proper since the Clock went sick.\n1358\t- MORGAUSE: We march. Let every crown in Forseason learn what the sun can do.\n1359\t\n1360\t**`open_amberlyn` \"The Quiet King\"** (stage: harvest hall):\n1361\t- NARRATOR: Ambergate, the harvest hall of Amberlyn. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime.\n1362\t- LAMORAK: The granaries stand half full, Majesty. The rest rotted where the Clock's sickness touched the fields.\n1363\t- ENID: Father has not slept. He watches the old sundial in the garden, as if it might tell him something.\n1364\t- DAGONET: It tells me it's noon, my lady. But it told me that yesterday as well.\n1365\t- VESNA: The lanterns on the Lantern Road burn blue now. The dead grow restless when time limps.\n1366\t- PELLAM: {w=.8}...\n1367\t- PELLAM: We will end this.\n1368\t- LAMORAK: Then we ride, my king. Four words from you are worth a hundred from any other crown.\n1369\t\n1370\t**`open_hoarfast` \"A Crown of Icicles\"** (stage: ice hall):\n1371\t- NARRATOR: Rimeholt, the frozen court of Hoarfast. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime. The snow has not melted.\n1372\t- MORDRAIN: Ragnell! What has a face and hands, and never stops running?\n1373\t- RAGNELL: A clock, Your Grace. You asked me yesterday.\n1374\t- MORDRAIN: Did I? Then the clock has not stopped yet. Pity. {w=.3}In winter nothing rots, Ragnell. Nothing ends.\n1375\t- NIMUE: The Chancellor would agree with you, Duke. That is what frightens me.\n1376\t- GORM: My yeti won't eat. They don't like the stopped hour. I don't like it either.\n1377\t- SAFIR: Wolves are out of Thawgate, and brigands ride with them.\n1378\t- MORDRAIN: Then we go hunting! Safir, the bows. Ragnell, the banners. Gorm, bring the bears.\n1379\t- RAGNELL: And I shall bring the sense. As always.\n1380\t\n1381\t**`banner_without_season`** (stage: Meridian clock chamber, with the Keeper asleep on a bier):\n1382\t- NARRATOR: Meridian. Within the Great Clock, the hands tremble between two seconds.\n1383\t- MELIANT: Do you hear it, Sir Nonesuch? Every tick is a funeral bell.\n1384\t- GRAY KNIGHT: I hear nothing, Chancellor. That is the gift I bring.\n1385\t- MELIANT: My wife died in the turning of an autumn. My son, in a winter. I will not give the Wheel another year.\n1386\t- GRAY KNIGHT: Then hold the city until the Thirteenth Month. When it comes, the hands will stop. So will grief.\n1387\t- MELIANT: The four crowns will come for it.\n1388\t- GRAY KNIGHT: Let them spend their springs and summers on one another. Time is the only army I need.\n1389\t\n1390\t**`candle_lit`** (stage: clock chamber):\n1391\t- NARRATOR: Meridian. Spring, Year 2 of the Brigantime.\n1392\t- GRAY KNIGHT: A candle of hours, Chancellor. Twelve seasons tall. When it is ash, the Thirteenth Month begins.\n1393\t- MELIANT: And the Keeper?\n1394\t- GRAY KNIGHT: He will sleep through the end of time. Is that not a mercy? *(emote: dots)*\n1395\t- *Effect: the Hour-Candle appears on the HUD showing 12 (difficulty-adjusted, §4.1).*\n1396\t\n1397\t**`meridian_falls`** (stage: clock chamber; the player's ruler and the knights who took the city):\n1398\t- MELIANT: *(kneels)* So it is done. {w=.5}Forgive me, Keeper. I only wanted the clocks to stop.\n1399\t- GRAY KNIGHT: And they shall, Chancellor. You were a key, nothing more. A stopped city is only a seed.\n1400\t- RULER: GARETH \"Who are you?\" / MORGAUSE \"Name yourself, before I burn the name off your tomb.\" / PELLAM \"...Who?\" /\n1401\t  MORDRAIN \"A riddle for you: who are you?\"\n1402\t- GRAY KNIGHT: The month that never was. The hour between hours. Every season you ever lost belongs to me.\n1403\t- GRAY KNIGHT: Come down into the Sanctum, little crown. Let us see whether your Wheel still turns.\n1404\t- If Lunete is with you, LUNETE: \"My father's clock is not yours to break. Stand on the dials with me, and we will turn\n1405\t  it together.\" If not, a knight of yours: \"The dials, my liege. The old tales say the Wheel answers four seasons\n1406\t  together.\"\n1407\t- *Effect: the Clockwork Sanctum battle starts at once (§6.10).*\n1408\t\n1409\t**`ending_verdance` \"The Wheel Turns Again\":**\n1410\t- NARRATOR: The thirteenth bell never rang.\n1411\t- GRAY KNIGHT: *(fading)* Then turn, little Wheel. Turn, and lose everything again. I will wait between the seconds.\n1412\t- NARRATOR: The Great Clock shuddered, and its hands moved on.\n1413\t- KEEPER: Spring... I dreamed of spring. Thank you, child of the Bough.\n1414\t- GARETH: Rest now, Keeper. The Wheel is in good hands.\n1415\t- NARRATOR: In Avalorn, the oldest apple blossomed that very morning.\n1416\t- Epilogue cards, one per surviving named knight (2 lines each), for example:\n1417\t  - \"Sir Pelleas wrote four hundred verses about the Sanctum. Captain Elidure read none of them, and married him anyway.\"\n1418\t    (if `v_elidure_joins`)\n1419\t  - \"Dame Lynette kept the Concord's peace for forty years, and never once admitted she enjoyed it.\"\n1420\t  - With Lunete: \"Lunete was crowned Keeper of the Wheel. Gareth knelt first.\" Without her: \"Gareth wound the Great\n1421\t    Clock each midwinter until a new Keeper was found.\"\n1422\t\n1423\t**`brigands_no_more_hob`** (an example of the captain pattern; the other three follow it in their own voices):\n1424\t- HOB: All right, all right! I yield! Mind the boots, they're new.\n1425\t- RULER: You robbed our roads all winter, Hob Mudspur.\n1426\t- HOB: And I'd rob 'em for you all summer, if the pay's honest. Better a brigand who knows the passes.\n1427\t- Choice: \"Take his oath\" (Hob joins your realm with his surviving monsters) or \"Exile him\" (+60 mana from his hoard).\n1428\t\n1429\t#### 6.12.5 Event list (beats; write each scene in the style above)\n1430\t\n1431\t| id | When / if | Cast and stage | Beats | Effects |\n1432\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1433\t| `prologue` | new campaign | narrator, title diorama | §6.12.4 | — |\n1434\t| `open_<realm>` | Tidings, Spring Y1, each human realm | its court | §6.12.4 | an objective toast: \"Take a brigand castle. Reach Meridian before the Thirteenth Month.\" |\n1435\t| `tutorial` | after `open_<realm>` | ruler | \"A brigand patrol blocks the border road.\" Choice: fight (tutorial) or skip | starts Border Meadow (§6.13) |\n1436\t| `banner_without_season` | Spring Y1, world | clock chamber | §6.12.4 | — |\n1437\t| `free_companies` | the player's first March | herald card | brigand castles hold the cross-quarter roads; the Keep rule | tutorial tip |\n1438\t| `first_victory` / `first_loss` | after the first battle won / lost | ruler and a knight | pride or grief; a tip on EXP and promotions, or on Delegate and Retreat | tip |\n1439\t| `long_winter` | Tidings, Winter Y1, world | ice hall (Mordrain) or herald | \"The thaw did not come.\" Mordrain laughs at the snow | the Winter Tide is +30% this season |\n1440\t| `candle_lit` | Tidings, Spring Y2, world | clock chamber | §6.12.4 | the candle appears |\n1441\t| `dominion_awakens` | Tidings, Summer Y2, world | war tent (Bertilak) | \"The Hour marches.\" Bertilak salutes his foes | Dominion aggression on (§4.15) |\n1442\t| `lunete_letter` | Autumn Y1 if the player holds Rainmere, Goldspur or Beltane; otherwise Spring Y2 | road | a letter signed \"L.\": \"the Keeper's daughter lives; seek the Old Mill\" | unlocks the story site at Beltane Ford |\n1443\t| `lunete_joins` | the Old Mill quest returns | mill | Gerrow: \"Take her, then. She eats more than my bats.\" Lunete: \"I am no prize, my lord. I am a promise.\" | adds Lunete (Lv 8) |\n1444\t| `lunete_arrives` | Spring Y3 if she hasn't joined | your capital's court | she walks in alone, soaked from the road | adds Lunete |\n1445\t| `brigands_no_more_<hob, gerrow, dafydd, abbot>` | the player captures that brigand castle | that castle | the yield; §6.12.4 | the choice: captain joins, or +60 mana |\n1446\t| `owain` | the player's realm first binds a wyvern or frost wyrm | stable | Owain: \"I lost my Kerrow in the Long Winter. Let me teach yours to fly.\" | adds Owain |\n1447\t| `galeron`, `ettard`, `blanchefleur` | a Wanderer outcome | road | the meeting, and why they join | adds the knight |\n1448\t| `blanchefleur_hire` | the Lammas Fair quest returns | fair | \"One hundred and fifty, and I don't fight children.\" | choice: pay 150 mana for Blanchefleur, or refuse |\n1449\t| `stillness` | the first stilling (Autumn Y3) | clock chamber | Gray Knight: \"Listen. A castle has stopped breathing.\" | — |\n1450\t| `thirteenth_warning` | the candle at 1 | herald | \"One season remains.\" | — |\n1451\t| `meridian_falls` | the player takes Meridian | clock chamber | §6.12.4 | the Sanctum battle |\n1452\t| `sanctum_retry` | the Sanctum battle is lost | clock chamber | \"The Wheel trembles, but it holds.\" | the Sanctum can be attacked again |\n1453\t| `rival_meridian` / `rival_failed` | an AI realm takes Meridian / loses its Sanctum battle | herald | the warning, then the relief | — |\n1454\t| `realm_falls_<realm>` | a realm is eliminated | that ruler | a lament (Gareth: \"Forgive me, Mother\"; Morgause: \"Even suns set\"; Pellam: \"...Enough.\"; Mordrain: \"Ice melts. Who knew?\") | knights freed |\n1455\t| `v_pelleas_letter` | Summer Y1, Verdance | orchard | Pelleas has written to Captain Elidure, whom he met at the last Concord | choice: send it (flag `v_letter`) or burn it |\n1456\t| `v_elidure_joins` | `v_letter`, and Verdance beats a troop led by Elidure or takes Goldspur | war tent | Elidure: \"Your poetry is dreadful. Your cause is not.\" | Elidure moves to Verdance |\n1457\t| `v_unicorn_herd` | Autumn Y1, Verdance holds Thornwick, Wren alive | glade | Wren finds a herd | a unicorn (Wren's level) and a Spring Seed |\n1458\t| `v_green_oath` | Verdance takes its first Hour satellite | war tent | Gareth swears to wake the Keeper | Gareth +2 Bond; learns Verdant Tempest now |\n1459\t| `v_amris_past` | Winter Y2, Verdance | chapel | Amris was once a knight of Hoarfast. Choice: write to the Duke, or keep silent | write: Hoarfast won't march on Verdance for 2 seasons (`aiFlag`) |\n1460\t| `s_hesper_offer` | Autumn Y1, Solmark | sun hall | Hesper offers the Hour's magic | accept: Lionsreach may summon minutes and stillwraiths, and `s_hesper_betrays` will come; refuse: Hesper +2 levels |\n1461\t| `s_hesper_betrays` | Summer Y3 if accepted | sun hall | Hesper: \"Time was always the better master, Majesty.\" | Hesper and her troop join the Dominion at the nearest satellite |\n1462\t| `s_wyvern_eggs` | Spring Y2, Solmark holds Goldspur | roost | Brennoc hatches eggs | a wyvern (Lv 5) and a Summer Ember |\n1463\t| `s_agravain_duel` | before the first Solmark–Hoarfast battle with Agravain | battlefield | he challenges Ragnell | Agravain has Valor in bell 1 |\n1464\t| `a_dagonet_jest` | Summer Y1, Amberlyn | harvest hall | a prank unmasks an Hourless spy | a Signet of Command |\n1465\t| `a_kings_cough` | Winter Y1, Amberlyn | bedchamber | Pellam's illness. Choice: name Enid heir now, or wait | name her: Enid +3 levels and learns Renewal |\n1466\t| `a_lanterns` | Autumn Y2, Amberlyn (All-Hallows) | the Lantern Road | Vesna lights the lanterns for the dead | 2 jack-o'-lamps (Lv 6) and an Autumn Acorn |\n1467\t| `a_lamorak_stand` | before a battle where Lamorak defends Ashbarrow | battlefield | the old knight's oath | Lamorak is Warded for bells 1–2 |\n1468\t| `w_nimue_bargain` | Summer Y1, Hoarfast | frozen mere | an egg for a memory. Choice: accept or refuse | accept: a frost wyrm (Lv 4) and Mordrain \"forgets a name\" (flag); refuse: Nimue +1 level |\n1469\t| `w_gorm_cub` | Autumn Y1, Hoarfast | snowfield | Gorm's lost yeti cub comes home | a yeti (Lv 5) |\n1470\t| `w_ragnell_doubt` | Winter Y2, Hoarfast | battlements | \"Do I follow a madman?\" Choice: trust him, or watch him | trust: Ragnell +2 levels; watch: Ragnell gets a Warding Charm |\n1471\t| `w_lucid_hour` | Hoarfast takes its first Hour satellite | ice hall | lucid for once, Mordrain tells of his sister, drowned in the lake beneath Rimeholt: if winter never ends, the lake never gives her back | Mad Gambit never misfires again |\n1472\t| `ending_<realm>` | the Gray Knight falls | per realm | Verdance in §6.12.4; Solmark \"The Long Noon Ends\" (Morgause: \"Even the sun must set, or it is only a fire.\"); Amberlyn \"The Last Harvest\" (Pellam's last word: \"Turn.\" Enid is crowned); Hoarfast \"Spring Thaw\" (Mordrain: \"Let the ice go, Ragnell. Let her go.\") | credits |\n1473\t| `ending_candle` | the candle burns out | clock chamber | Gray Knight: \"Hush now. Nothing will ever end again.\" The picture drains to grey: THE LEGEND ENDS IN SILENCE | Retry (latest save) or Title |\n1474\t| `ending_wheel_<realm>` | a rival sets the Wheel | Hour Throne | that ruler's line; the land floods, burns, rots or freezes: THE LEGEND ENDS IN FLOOD / FIRE / DUST / ICE | Retry or Title |\n1475\t| `ending_fallen` | the player's last castle falls | road | the ruler in exile: THE LEGEND FORGETS YOU | Retry or Title |\n1476\t\n1477\t#### 6.12.6 Rival lines (2 lines before a battle when both are on the field; the first match plays)\n1478\t- AGRAVAIN / RAGNELL: \"Ice-Eye! I've waited all summer to melt you.\" / \"Then you'll wait all winter to stand back up.\"\n1479\t- PELLEAS / ELIDURE: \"Captain! Did you read my letter?\" / \"I'm reading your formation, Sir Pelleas. It's worse.\"\n1480\t- GARETH / MORGAUSE: \"The Wheel isn't yours to take, Your Majesty.\" / \"Then come and stop me, princeling. Bring your blossoms.\"\n1481\t- MORDRAIN / PELLAM: \"The Quiet King! Say something, old man!\" / \"...No.\"\n1482\t- LYNETTE / AGRAVAIN: \"Cinderjaw. Still shouting?\" / \"Still standing in my way?\"\n1483\t- DAGONET / HOB: \"A brigand with a funny name! Finally, a rival.\" / \"Oi! Mudspur is a proud name!\"\n1484\t- MORGAUSE / PELLAM: \"Step aside, old king. Summer has no patience for harvests.\" / \"...Patience.\"\n1485\t- MORDRAIN / GARETH: \"Little sprout! Do you know why snow is so quiet?\" / \"Because it's waiting for spring.\"\n1486\t- MELIANT / LUNETE: \"Princess... you should be asleep beside your father.\" / \"Somebody has to stay awake, Chancellor.\"\n1487\t- BERTILAK / anyone: \"Courtesy first: I shall kill you slowly, and with every respect.\"\n1488\t- TIC and TAC / anyone: \"Tic says—\" / \"—Tac agrees!\"\n1489\t- AURELIE / anyone: \"Must you? I was enjoying the silence.\"\n1490\t- GRAY KNIGHT (the Sanctum opens): \"Twelve bells, little crown. Then nothing, ever again.\"\n1491\t\n1492\t### 6.13 Tutorial: \"The Border Road\" (Border Meadow, Spring)\n1493\t- **Sides:** the player's ruler and the realm's Squire (Lynette, Agravain, Lamorak or Ragnell) with their troops, against\n1494\t  a brigand patrol: a Brigand Captain, the \"Patrol Sergeant\" at Lv 3, with a slime, two bats and a skeleton at Lv 2–3.\n1495\t- **Teaching:** non-modal tip cards walk through these steps. Each one appears when its situation first arises, waits for\n1496\t  the action it asks for, and never blocks other play:\n1497\t  1. Choose a unit.\n1498\t  2. Move (the blue hexes).\n1499\t  3. Attack (reading the forecast: hit, damage, ▲ ▼ elements).\n1500\t  4. Ward rings (a monster outside its ring is weaker).\n1501\t  5. Spells need planted feet (cast before moving).\n1502\t  6. The season badge (the Spring Tide).\n1503\t  7. Surround a foe for more damage.\n1504\t  8. Fell the captain, and his monsters flee or are captured.\n1505\t  9. Twelve bells and the Keep rule.\n1506\t- Winning returns to the campaign map. The first opening of each Muster panel shows its own one-card tip (turn tips off\n1507\t  in Settings).\n1508\t\n1509\t---\n1510\t\n1511\t## 7. Presentation: art, rendering and animation\n1512\t\n1513\t### 7.1 Look target and palettes\n1514\tFollow the engine's look target (API.md, \"Look target\") in every scene:\n1515\t- `res: 'ps1', expand: true`; HD Humanoids at size 1.1–1.6, dressed;\n1516\t- textured floors; 3–8 props per screen; lights in every scene; effects on every hit; the title font; shading with\n1517\t  `E.tones` everywhere.\n1518\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"40ee60fc-7e94-4251-840d-221b5c54a4e7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:02:42.081Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/PLAN.md","content":"####gggDggg####\n###gggggggg####\n###gg#ggg#gg###\n##gggg8ggggg###\n##gDgggK7ggDg##\n##gggg9ggggg###\n###gg#ggg#gg###\n###gggggggg####\n####gggDggg####\n####g1g2g3#####\n###############\n```\n**Wheel Shrine** (`wheel_shrine`, 15 × 13): used by Skirmish and the AI Hub. Four corners, seats 1 to 4 (Spring NE, Summer SE, Autumn SW, Winter NW), around the Hour Shrine (K) in its courtyard. With 2 sides use seats 1 and 3; with 3 sides use 1, 2 and 3.\n```\n..........~....\nf4.f..f..~...1~\n........~......\n..f..f.~....~..\n...........~...\n.f..f.gg..~....\nF.....gKg...h..\n....F.gg......h\n..F......h.....\nF.....F....h...\n....F..........\n.3......h....2.\nF.....F...h....\n```\n\n**Clockwork Sanctum rules (the final battle):**\n- The player wins when the Gray Knight falls; that is the ruler rule. If he stands at the end of bell 12, the thirteenth bell tolls and the battle is lost (§4.17).\n- **The Hour Hand:** at the end of each bell it points along one of the 6 hex directions from the centre, moving one step clockwise per bell. Every player unit on that `line6` (to the wall) rolls Stop 70. The next bell's line glows faintly all bell long, so players can step aside.\n- **Season Dials (`D`):** at the end of a bell, a dial with a player unit on it lights and stays lit. A Dominion unit standing on a lit dial at a bell's end puts it out. When all four are lit at once, \"The Wheel turns!\": Timeless breaks for the rest of the battle (full damage, effects apply), the Gray Knight's DEF drops 40%, and the Hour Hand stops.\n- **At 50% HP** the Gray Knight calls 2 Second Hands (tier-3 Minutes, level 22). They head for lit dials, and he uses Still every 2 bells instead of every 3.\n- **Lunete (if she is present):** her Turning (×2 against Hour) breaks Timeless for one bell, and a dial she stands on lights at once instead of at the bell's end.\n- The troops that took Meridian enter, healed to full (\"the Wheel's light\"), plus up to one more troop from a castle adjacent to Meridian.\n\n**Wheel Shrine rules (Skirmish \"Banners of the Wheel\" and the AI Hub):**\n- A free-for-all of 2 to 4 sides, one troop each (a ruler at level 10 with 2 monsters, §11.4), lasting 6 bells.\n- **The season turns every bell:** bell 1 Spring, 2 Summer, 3 Autumn, 4 Winter, 5 Spring, 6 Summer. The Tide and terrain transforms are applied again at each bell's start.\n- **Glory:** +1 for every 5 damage dealt, +10 per monster KO, +25 per knight KO, +5 at each bell's end for the side holding the Shrine (`K`), and +10 at the end if your knight still stands.\n- The Shrine (`K`) gives whoever stands on it the Keep's +25% DEF and 10% healing per bell. Highest glory wins; ties share a place. A knight that falls takes its troop out, but its glory still counts.\n\n### 6.11 Quest sites (one per castle; a quest is sent from the castle itself, and a story site from any owned castle adjacent to it)\n\n**Regional pools:**\n\n| Region | Items | Beasts | Wanderers |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Winter | herb, wintershard, rimesteel, frostplate, wardingcharm, yewlongbow | snowkit, frostwolf, yeti, bat | galeron (from Autumn, Year 1), ettard |\n| Spring | herb, springseed, tomeofthaw, hawthornbow, spurs, willowstaff | sproutling, pixie, unicorn, slime | galeron |\n| Summer | herb, summerember, sunforged, hauberk, bannerpin, cleaver | salamander, cinderhound, sunbird, sunmane | blanchefleur |\n| Autumn | herb, autumnacorn, lanternstaff, horseshoe, robeofseasons, jerkin | jacklamp, scarecrow, ghoul, tusker | blanchefleur, ettard |\n| Hour | ether, writ, hourglassrod, signet, amuletoftides, spurs | minute, gearhound | — |\n\nA cross-quarter site uses both neighbours' pools.\n\n| Site | Castle | Seasons away | Focus (+10) | Extra |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| The Lake of Silent Bells | Rimeholt | 2 | Training | Hoarfast: part of `w_lucid_hour` |\n| The Howling Scar | Wolfsgate | 1 | Beast | |\n| Nimue's Mere | Frostmere | 1 | Treasure | Ettard can be found |\n| The Kestrel Eyrie | Kestrel Spire | 2 | Wanderer | |\n| The Queen's Orchard | Avalorn | 1 | Treasure | |\n| The Briar Maze | Thornwick | 1 | Beast | unicorns ×2 |\n| The Weeping Weir | Rainmere | 1 | Beast | rillserpent added to the pool |\n| The Unicorn Glade | Primrose Ford | 2 | Beast | unicorns ×3 |\n| The Furnace Vaults | Brazenhold | 1 | Treasure | |\n| The Wyvern Roost | Goldspur | 2 | Beast | wyvern added at half weight |\n| The Ash Dunes | Cinderwall | 1 | Mana | |\n| The Lion Steps | Lionsreach | 1 | Wanderer | sunmane ×2 |\n| The Harvest Vault | Ambergate | 1 | Treasure | |\n| The Barrow Downs | Ashbarrow | 1 | Beast | Mishap +5 |\n| The Russet Bog | Russetmoor | 1 | Beast | tusker ×2 |\n| The Lantern Road | Lanternfall | 2 | Wanderer | Ettard can be found |\n| The Breaking Ice | Thawgate | 1 | Mana | draught added |\n| The Old Mill of Beltane | Beltane Ford | 1 | Treasure | the story site in `lunete_letter` |\n| The Lammas Fair | Lammas Cross | 1 | Wanderer | the hire choice in `blanchefleur_hire` |\n| The Hollow Abbey Crypts | Hallowmere | 2 | Treasure | skeleton and bat beasts; Ettard |\n| The Bell That Doesn't Ring | Midnight Keep | 2 | Treasure | |\n| The Sunrise Stair | Dawnwatch | 1 | Treasure | |\n| The Shadowless Square | Noonspire | 1 | Mana | |\n| The Evensong Crypt | Vesper Hall | 2 | Treasure | |\n| The Sleeping Court | Meridian | 2 | Treasure | a vignette of the sleeping Keeper |\n\nEach quest return plays a vignette of 2–4 lines with the knight's portrait, for example:\n- TREASURE: \"Sir Pelleas returns from the Briar Maze with thorns in his hair and a Spring Seed in his glove.\"\n- BEAST: \"A pixie followed Wren home from the Weeping Weir. It will not leave her shoulder.\"\n- MISHAP: \"Ragnell's patrol was ambushed at the Howling Scar. She will mend; the wolf will not.\"\n\nWrite 3 variants per outcome kind, and fill in `{$knight}`, `{$site}` and `{$thing}` with the story module's variables.\n\n### 6.12 Story\n\n#### 6.12.1 Premise (the back-story the scripts assume)\n- For three hundred years the four season-crowns kept the Concord of the Wheel. In Meridian, the Keeper of the Wheel,\n  King Aldous, wound the Great Clock that makes each season give way to the next.\n- Last winter Aldous fell into a sleep no physician could break, caught between two seconds, and the Clock began to\n  falter.\n- Lord Chancellor Meliant had lost his wife to an autumn and his son to a winter. He sealed the city, raised a banner\n  with no season and proclaimed the Hourless Dominion: when the Thirteenth Month comes, he will stop the Wheel, and no\n  one will ever grow old or die.\n- At his side stands the Gray Knight, Sir Nonesuch, who is not a man. He is the month that never was, and he feeds on\n  stopped time.\n- The Keeper's daughter, Princess Lunete, escaped through the Midnight Door and hides among the brigands of Beltane Ford.\n- Each crown claims the Hour Throne for its own reasons:\n  - Gareth of Verdance would wake the Keeper and restore the Concord;\n  - Morgause of Solmark would have Solmark set the Wheel and rule the calendar;\n  - Pellam of Amberlyn, old and ill, would end the war with the fewest dead;\n  - Mordrain of Hoarfast, mad with grief, would welcome an eternal winter \"where nothing rots and nothing ends\".\n- The chroniclers call the age the Brigantime: every knight a brigand, every road a war.\n\n#### 6.12.2 Style guide (match the source's register)\n- **Brief scenes:** 3 to 10 lines between seasons. Each line is at most about 90 characters, so a page shows it whole.\n- **An earnest, formal court register:** \"my liege\", \"Your Grace\", \"it is done\". No modern slang and no winking at the\n  player.\n- **Humour comes from the characters:** Pelleas's poetry, Dagonet's jests, Mordrain's riddles, Tic and Tac's\n  overlapping lines. It never mocks the stakes.\n- **Narration:** a heading per scene (\"Rimeholt. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime.\"), written in a pale colour with\n  markup `{c=#b8b0c8}...{/c}`.\n- **Markup is used sparingly:** `{w=.4}` for a beat, `{shake}` for a shout, `{s=12}` for dread, and colour for key words\n  (seasons in their colours, the Candle in red).\n- **Every speaker has a portrait and a voice** (§9.3). Emotes come from the story module: `!`, `?`, `dots`, `heart`,\n  `note`.\n- **Choices** are 2 short options, worded as intentions (\"Let him send it\", \"Burn the letter\").\n\n#### 6.12.3 How events run\n- Each event is `G.def('event', id, { when, realm, if, once: true, priority, stage, cast, nodes, effects })`.\n  - `when`: `tidings`, `muster` (on entering), `march`, `afterBattle`, `beforeBattle`, `questReturn` or `capture`.\n  - `realm`: a realm id, `'player'` (each human realm sees its own) or `'world'`.\n  - `if`: story-module conditions plus game tests: `season`, `year`, `owns:<castle>`, `holds:<knight>`,\n    `battle.vs:<realm>`, `flag`.\n- **At a Tidings:** play up to 3 eligible scenes in priority order (opening 100, story 50, recruit 30, flavour 10); the\n  rest roll over. An event marked `expires` drops after its window passes.\n- **Effects** are data: `{ addKnight, removeKnight, moveKnight, addMonster: [species, level, castle], addItem, mana,\n  flag, aiFlag: [realm, key, value], unlockSite, setTune }`, applied through `CampaignSim` commands, so effects are\n  saved and replayable.\n- **A stage** is one of 8 sets (§7.4). The cast stands on it, and the camera frames the speaker (`on.look`, as in the\n  tactics kit).\n\n#### 6.12.4 Scripts (write these as given; the rest follow the beats in §6.12.5)\n**`prologue` (an opening crawl over the title diorama; narrator; auto-advance every 5 s, or confirm):**\n1. In the Age of the Wheel, four crowns kept one calendar.\n2. Spring to Verdance. Summer to Solmark. Autumn to Amberlyn. Winter to Hoarfast.\n3. And in Meridian, the Calendar City, the Keeper of the Wheel wound the Great Clock, that each season might yield to the next.\n4. Last winter the Keeper fell into a sleep no physician could break, and the Great Clock began to falter.\n5. From the silent city rode Lord Chancellor Meliant, beneath a banner with no season.\n6. \"When the Thirteenth Month comes,\" he swore, \"I will stop the Wheel, and no one we love will ever grow old.\"\n7. Four crowns answered with steel. Every knight became a brigand; every road, a war.\n8. The chroniclers named the age the Brigantime.\n\n**`open_verdance` \"The Last Blossom\"** (stage: orchard court):\n- NARRATOR: Avalorn, the orchard court of Verdance. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime.\n- AMRIS: Your mother asked to rest beneath the oldest apple, my prince. It has not blossomed since the Clock faltered.\n- GARETH: Then it will blossom when the Wheel turns again. Not before.\n- LYNETTE: Brave words. Solmark is sharpening its swords, and Hoarfast's Duke laughs alone in his ice hall.\n- GARETH: Let them. We do not ride to take a throne, Lynette. We ride to wake a king.\n- PELLEAS: And should a throne fall into our laps along the way? I ask only for the ballads.\n- WREN: The unicorns won't graze. They smell the Clock's sickness on the east wind.\n- GARETH: Then we march before the petals fall. {shake}Sound the horn!{/shake}\n\n**`open_solmark` \"Noon Without End\"** (stage: sun hall):\n- NARRATOR: Brazenhold, the furnace-throne of Solmark. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime.\n- HESPER: Majesty, the Chancellor promises the Wheel will stop. Imagine it: a summer without end.\n- MORGAUSE: I have imagined it, Hesper. Every harvest burned to dust. Every child born into drought.\n- AGRAVAIN: Then we take Meridian and set the Wheel ourselves! Our summer, on our terms!\n- MORGAUSE: Now you sound like a Solmarker. {w=.4}A long noon, Sir Agravain, is still a noon that ends.\n- ELIDURE: The brigands at Beltane and Lammas grow fat on our roads. Shall I clear them, my queen?\n- BRENNOC: Take the wyverns. They've not flown proper since the Clock went sick.\n- MORGAUSE: We march. Let every crown in Forseason learn what the sun can do.\n\n**`open_amberlyn` \"The Quiet King\"** (stage: harvest hall):\n- NARRATOR: Ambergate, the harvest hall of Amberlyn. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime.\n- LAMORAK: The granaries stand half full, Majesty. The rest rotted where the Clock's sickness touched the fields.\n- ENID: Father has not slept. He watches the old sundial in the garden, as if it might tell him something.\n- DAGONET: It tells me it's noon, my lady. But it told me that yesterday as well.\n- VESNA: The lanterns on the Lantern Road burn blue now. The dead grow restless when time limps.\n- PELLAM: {w=.8}...\n- PELLAM: We will end this.\n- LAMORAK: Then we ride, my king. Four words from you are worth a hundred from any other crown.\n\n**`open_hoarfast` \"A Crown of Icicles\"** (stage: ice hall):\n- NARRATOR: Rimeholt, the frozen court of Hoarfast. Spring, Year 1 of the Brigantime. The snow has not melted.\n- MORDRAIN: Ragnell! What has a face and hands, and never stops running?\n- RAGNELL: A clock, Your Grace. You asked me yesterday.\n- MORDRAIN: Did I? Then the clock has not stopped yet. Pity. {w=.3}In winter nothing rots, Ragnell. Nothing ends.\n- NIMUE: The Chancellor would agree with you, Duke. That is what frightens me.\n- GORM: My yeti won't eat. They don't like the stopped hour. I don't like it either.\n- SAFIR: Wolves are out of Thawgate, and brigands ride with them.\n- MORDRAIN: Then we go hunting! Safir, the bows. Ragnell, the banners. Gorm, bring the bears.\n- RAGNELL: And I shall bring the sense. As always.\n\n**`banner_without_season`** (stage: Meridian clock chamber, with the Keeper asleep on a bier):\n- NARRATOR: Meridian. Within the Great Clock, the hands tremble between two seconds.\n- MELIANT: Do you hear it, Sir Nonesuch? Every tick is a funeral bell.\n- GRAY KNIGHT: I hear nothing, Chancellor. That is the gift I bring.\n- MELIANT: My wife died in the turning of an autumn. My son, in a winter. I will not give the Wheel another year.\n- GRAY KNIGHT: Then hold the city until the Thirteenth Month. When it comes, the hands will stop. So will grief.\n- MELIANT: The four crowns will come for it.\n- GRAY KNIGHT: Let them spend their springs and summers on one another. Time is the only army I need.\n\n**`candle_lit`** (stage: clock chamber):\n- NARRATOR: Meridian. Spring, Year 2 of the Brigantime.\n- GRAY KNIGHT: A candle of hours, Chancellor. Twelve seasons tall. When it is ash, the Thirteenth Month begins.\n- MELIANT: And the Keeper?\n- GRAY KNIGHT: He will sleep through the end of time. Is that not a mercy? *(emote: dots)*\n- *Effect: the Hour-Candle appears on the HUD showing 12 (difficulty-adjusted, §4.1).*\n\n**`meridian_falls`** (stage: clock chamber; the player's ruler and the knights who took the city):\n- MELIANT: *(kneels)* So it is done. {w=.5}Forgive me, Keeper. I only wanted the clocks to stop.\n- GRAY KNIGHT: And they shall, Chancellor. You were a key, nothing more. A stopped city is only a seed.\n- RULER: GARETH \"Who are you?\" / MORGAUSE \"Name yourself, before I burn the name off your tomb.\" / PELLAM \"...Who?\" /\n  MORDRAIN \"A riddle for you: who are you?\"\n- GRAY KNIGHT: The month that never was. The hour between hours. Every season you ever lost belongs to me.\n- GRAY KNIGHT: Come down into the Sanctum, little crown. Let us see whether your Wheel still turns.\n- If Lunete is with you, LUNETE: \"My father's clock is not yours to break. Stand on the dials with me, and we will turn\n  it together.\" If not, a knight of yours: \"The dials, my liege. The old tales say the Wheel answers four seasons\n  together.\"\n- *Effect: the Clockwork Sanctum battle starts at once (§6.10).*\n\n**`ending_verdance` \"The Wheel Turns Again\":**\n- NARRATOR: The thirteenth bell never rang.\n- GRAY KNIGHT: *(fading)* Then turn, little Wheel. Turn, and lose everything again. I will wait between the seconds.\n- NARRATOR: The Great Clock shuddered, and its hands moved on.\n- KEEPER: Spring... I dreamed of spring. Thank you, child of the Bough.\n- GARETH: Rest now, Keeper. The Wheel is in good hands.\n- NARRATOR: In Avalorn, the oldest apple blossomed that very morning.\n- Epilogue cards, one per surviving named knight (2 lines each), for example:\n  - \"Sir Pelleas wrote four hundred verses about the Sanctum. Captain Elidure read none of them, and married him anyway.\"\n    (if `v_elidure_joins`)\n  - \"Dame Lynette kept the Concord's peace for forty years, and never once admitted she enjoyed it.\"\n  - With Lunete: \"Lunete was crowned Keeper of the Wheel. Gareth knelt first.\" Without her: \"Gareth wound the Great\n    Clock each midwinter until a new Keeper was found.\"\n\n**`brigands_no_more_hob`** (an example of the captain pattern; the other three follow it in their own voices):\n- HOB: All right, all right! I yield! Mind the boots, they're new.\n- RULER: You robbed our roads all winter, Hob Mudspur.\n- HOB: And I'd rob 'em for you all summer, if the pay's honest. Better a brigand who knows the passes.\n- Choice: \"Take his oath\" (Hob joins your realm with his surviving monsters) or \"Exile him\" (+60 mana from his hoard).\n\n#### 6.12.5 Event list (beats; write each scene in the style above)\n\n| id | When / if | Cast and stage | Beats | Effects |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `prologue` | new campaign | narrator, title diorama | §6.12.4 | — |\n| `open_<realm>` | Tidings, Spring Y1, each human realm | its court | §6.12.4 | an objective toast: \"Take a brigand castle. Reach Meridian before the Thirteenth Month.\" |\n| `tutorial` | after `open_<realm>` | ruler | \"A brigand patrol blocks the border road.\" Choice: fight (tutorial) or skip | starts Border Meadow (§6.13) |\n| `banner_without_season` | Spring Y1, world | clock chamber | §6.12.4 | — |\n| `free_companies` | the player's first March | herald card | brigand castles hold the cross-quarter roads; the Keep rule | tutorial tip |\n| `first_victory` / `first_loss` | after the first battle won / lost | ruler and a knight | pride or grief; a tip on EXP and promotions, or on Delegate and Retreat | tip |\n| `long_winter` | Tidings, Winter Y1, world | ice hall (Mordrain) or herald | \"The thaw did not come.\" Mordrain laughs at the snow | the Winter Tide is +30% this season |\n| `candle_lit` | Tidings, Spring Y2, world | clock chamber | §6.12.4 | the candle appears |\n| `dominion_awakens` | Tidings, Summer Y2, world | war tent (Bertilak) | \"The Hour marches.\" Bertilak salutes his foes | Dominion aggression on (§4.15) |\n| `lunete_letter` | Autumn Y1 if the player holds Rainmere, Goldspur or Beltane; otherwise Spring Y2 | road | a letter signed \"L.\": \"the Keeper's daughter lives; seek the Old Mill\" | unlocks the story site at Beltane Ford |\n| `lunete_joins` | the Old Mill quest returns | mill | Gerrow: \"Take her, then. She eats more than my bats.\" Lunete: \"I am no prize, my lord. I am a promise.\" | adds Lunete (Lv 8) |\n| `lunete_arrives` | Spring Y3 if she hasn't joined | your capital's court | she walks in alone, soaked from the road | adds Lunete |\n| `brigands_no_more_<hob, gerrow, dafydd, abbot>` | the player captures that brigand castle | that castle | the yield; §6.12.4 | the choice: captain joins, or +60 mana |\n| `owain` | the player's realm first binds a wyvern or frost wyrm | stable | Owain: \"I lost my Kerrow in the Long Winter. Let me teach yours to fly.\" | adds Owain |\n| `galeron`, `ettard`, `blanchefleur` | a Wanderer outcome | road | the meeting, and why they join | adds the knight |\n| `blanchefleur_hire` | the Lammas Fair quest returns | fair | \"One hundred and fifty, and I don't fight children.\" | choice: pay 150 mana for Blanchefleur, or refuse |\n| `stillness` | the first stilling (Autumn Y3) | clock chamber | Gray Knight: \"Listen. A castle has stopped breathing.\" | — |\n| `thirteenth_warning` | the candle at 1 | herald | \"One season remains.\" | — |\n| `meridian_falls` | the player takes Meridian | clock chamber | §6.12.4 | the Sanctum battle |\n| `sanctum_retry` | the Sanctum battle is lost | clock chamber | \"The Wheel trembles, but it holds.\" | the Sanctum can be attacked again |\n| `rival_meridian` / `rival_failed` | an AI realm takes Meridian / loses its Sanctum battle | herald | the warning, then the relief | — |\n| `realm_falls_<realm>` | a realm is eliminated | that ruler | a lament (Gareth: \"Forgive me, Mother\"; Morgause: \"Even suns set\"; Pellam: \"...Enough.\"; Mordrain: \"Ice melts. Who knew?\") | knights freed |\n| `v_pelleas_letter` | Summer Y1, Verdance | orchard | Pelleas has written to Captain Elidure, whom he met at the last Concord | choice: send it (flag `v_letter`) or burn it |\n| `v_elidure_joins` | `v_letter`, and Verdance beats a troop led by Elidure or takes Goldspur | war tent | Elidure: \"Your poetry is dreadful. Your cause is not.\" | Elidure moves to Verdance |\n| `v_unicorn_herd` | Autumn Y1, Verdance holds Thornwick, Wren alive | glade | Wren finds a herd | a unicorn (Wren's level) and a Spring Seed |\n| `v_green_oath` | Verdance takes its first Hour satellite | war tent | Gareth swears to wake the Keeper | Gareth +2 Bond; learns Verdant Tempest now |\n| `v_amris_past` | Winter Y2, Verdance | chapel | Amris was once a knight of Hoarfast. Choice: write to the Duke, or keep silent | write: Hoarfast won't march on Verdance for 2 seasons (`aiFlag`) |\n| `s_hesper_offer` | Autumn Y1, Solmark | sun hall | Hesper offers the Hour's magic | accept: Lionsreach may summon minutes and stillwraiths, and `s_hesper_betrays` will come; refuse: Hesper +2 levels |\n| `s_hesper_betrays` | Summer Y3 if accepted | sun hall | Hesper: \"Time was always the better master, Majesty.\" | Hesper and her troop join the Dominion at the nearest satellite |\n| `s_wyvern_eggs` | Spring Y2, Solmark holds Goldspur | roost | Brennoc hatches eggs | a wyvern (Lv 5) and a Summer Ember |\n| `s_agravain_duel` | before the first Solmark–Hoarfast battle with Agravain | battlefield | he challenges Ragnell | Agravain has Valor in bell 1 |\n| `a_dagonet_jest` | Summer Y1, Amberlyn | harvest hall | a prank unmasks an Hourless spy | a Signet of Command |\n| `a_kings_cough` | Winter Y1, Amberlyn | bedchamber | Pellam's illness. Choice: name Enid heir now, or wait | name her: Enid +3 levels and learns Renewal |\n| `a_lanterns` | Autumn Y2, Amberlyn (All-Hallows) | the Lantern Road | Vesna lights the lanterns for the dead | 2 jack-o'-lamps (Lv 6) and an Autumn Acorn |\n| `a_lamorak_stand` | before a battle where Lamorak defends Ashbarrow | battlefield | the old knight's oath | Lamorak is Warded for bells 1–2 |\n| `w_nimue_bargain` | Summer Y1, Hoarfast | frozen mere | an egg for a memory. Choice: accept or refuse | accept: a frost wyrm (Lv 4) and Mordrain \"forgets a name\" (flag); refuse: Nimue +1 level |\n| `w_gorm_cub` | Autumn Y1, Hoarfast | snowfield | Gorm's lost yeti cub comes home | a yeti (Lv 5) |\n| `w_ragnell_doubt` | Winter Y2, Hoarfast | battlements | \"Do I follow a madman?\" Choice: trust him, or watch him | trust: Ragnell +2 levels; watch: Ragnell gets a Warding Charm |\n| `w_lucid_hour` | Hoarfast takes its first Hour satellite | ice hall | lucid for once, Mordrain tells of his sister, drowned in the lake beneath Rimeholt: if winter never ends, the lake never gives her back | Mad Gambit never misfires again |\n| `ending_<realm>` | the Gray Knight falls | per realm | Verdance in §6.12.4; Solmark \"The Long Noon Ends\" (Morgause: \"Even the sun must set, or it is only a fire.\"); Amberlyn \"The Last Harvest\" (Pellam's last word: \"Turn.\" Enid is crowned); Hoarfast \"Spring Thaw\" (Mordrain: \"Let the ice go, Ragnell. Let her go.\") | credits |\n| `ending_candle` | the candle burns out | clock chamber | Gray Knight: \"Hush now. Nothing will ever end again.\" The picture drains to grey: THE LEGEND ENDS IN SILENCE | Retry (latest save) or Title |\n| `ending_wheel_<realm>` | a rival sets the Wheel | Hour Throne | that ruler's line; the land floods, burns, rots or freezes: THE LEGEND ENDS IN FLOOD / FIRE / DUST / ICE | Retry or Title |\n| `ending_fallen` | the player's last castle falls | road | the ruler in exile: THE LEGEND FORGETS YOU | Retry or Title |\n\n#### 6.12.6 Rival lines (2 lines before a battle when both are on the field; the first match plays)\n- AGRAVAIN / RAGNELL: \"Ice-Eye! I've waited all summer to melt you.\" / \"Then you'll wait all winter to stand back up.\"\n- PELLEAS / ELIDURE: \"Captain! Did you read my letter?\" / \"I'm reading your formation, Sir Pelleas. It's worse.\"\n- GARETH / MORGAUSE: \"The Wheel isn't yours to take, Your Majesty.\" / \"Then come and stop me, princeling. Bring your blossoms.\"\n- MORDRAIN / PELLAM: \"The Quiet King! Say something, old man!\" / \"...No.\"\n- LYNETTE / AGRAVAIN: \"Cinderjaw. Still shouting?\" / \"Still standing in my way?\"\n- DAGONET / HOB: \"A brigand with a funny name! Finally, a rival.\" / \"Oi! Mudspur is a proud name!\"\n- MORGAUSE / PELLAM: \"Step aside, old king. Summer has no patience for harvests.\" / \"...Patience.\"\n- MORDRAIN / GARETH: \"Little sprout! Do you know why snow is so quiet?\" / \"Because it's waiting for spring.\"\n- MELIANT / LUNETE: \"Princess... you should be asleep beside your father.\" / \"Somebody has to stay awake, Chancellor.\"\n- BERTILAK / anyone: \"Courtesy first: I shall kill you slowly, and with every respect.\"\n- TIC and TAC / anyone: \"Tic says—\" / \"—Tac agrees!\"\n- AURELIE / anyone: \"Must you? I was enjoying the silence.\"\n- GRAY KNIGHT (the Sanctum opens): \"Twelve bells, little crown. Then nothing, ever again.\"\n\n### 6.13 Tutorial: \"The Border Road\" (Border Meadow, Spring)\n- **Sides:** the player's ruler and the realm's Squire (Lynette, Agravain, Lamorak or Ragnell) with their troops, against\n  a brigand patrol: a Brigand Captain, the \"Patrol Sergeant\" at Lv 3, with a slime, two bats and a skeleton at Lv 2–3.\n- **Teaching:** non-modal tip cards walk through these steps. Each one appears when its situation first arises, waits for\n  the action it asks for, and never blocks other play:\n  1. Choose a unit.\n  2. Move (the blue hexes).\n  3. Attack (reading the forecast: hit, damage, ▲ ▼ elements).\n  4. Ward rings (a monster outside its ring is weaker).\n  5. Spells need planted feet (cast before moving).\n  6. The season badge (the Spring Tide).\n  7. Surround a foe for more damage.\n  8. Fell the captain, and his monsters flee or are captured.\n  9. Twelve bells and the Keep rule.\n- Winning returns to the campaign map. The first opening of each Muster panel shows its own one-card tip (turn tips off\n  in Settings).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Presentation: art, rendering and animation\n\n### 7.1 Look target and palettes\nFollow the engine's look target (API.md, \"Look target\") in every scene:\n- `res: 'ps1', expand: true`; HD Humanoids at size 1.1–1.6, dressed;\n- textured floors; 3–8 props per screen; lights in every scene; effects on every hit; the title font; shading with\n  `E.tones` everywhere.\n","numLines":330,"startLine":1189,"totalLines":2417}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012uSfkVVDLRmkqWh1EurczD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
