{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QH4yXeHAa1qxBQPbR78KbD","type":"tool_result","content":"1978\t---\n1979\t\n1980\t## 10. Modes and meta\n1981\t\n1982\t### 10.1 Boot and title\n1983\t- **Boot steps** (`game.start({ boot: { title: 'BRIGANTIME', steps } })`):\n1984\t  1. register and validate all data (it fails loudly on a bad reference);\n1985\t  2. build the icon and glyph sprites;\n1986\t  3. compose the songs;\n1987\t  4. bake the title diorama;\n1988\t  5. warm the first beast portraits.\n1989\t  Boot messages: \"Winding the Great Clock\", \"Teaching wyverns to sit\", \"Counting the bells\", \"Sweeping the cross-quarter\n1990\t  roads\".\n1991\t- **The title** (§8.5.1) and the setup menus before play (campaign setup, skirmish setup) track idle time: any key,\n1992\t  mouse button, pointer move over 4 px, pad button, stick past .5 or touch resets it. At 10 s they go to `attract`.\n1993\t  Reading screens (About, How to Play) and anything in play never do.\n1994\t- **On a touch-only device** (coarse pointer, no fine pointer, touch points, no gamepad or keyboard seen): show the\n1995\t  \"Controller or keyboard required\" panel with a large Settings button (`game.menu('settings')`) and no touch controls\n1996\t  (`touch: []` in every scene, `input.touchEnabled = false`). The idle timer still runs. A gamepad connecting or a key\n1997\t  pressed removes the notice for good.\n1998\t\n1999\t### 10.2 Attract mode (`67-scene-attract.js`)\n2000\tA scripted reel of about 90 s that loops and cheats freely (canned data, a fixed seed per loop, a showcase AI). A\n2001\t\"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" banner pulses at the bottom, with the logo in a corner.\n2002\t\n2003\t| Time | Beat | Shows |\n2004\t|---|---|---|\n2005\t| 0–12 s | **The Wheel turns** | the world map pans across the four regions while the seasons wipe every 3 s. `CampaignSim` runs AI-only on a canned seed, so banners flip and march arrows fly. Caption: \"FOUR SEASONS. FOUR CROWNS. ONE STOPPED CLOCK.\" |\n2006\t| 12–20 s | **Summoning** | Rimeholt's circle flares and a Frost Wyrm rises. Caption: \"BIND MONSTERS TO YOUR BANNER.\" |\n2007\t| 20–65 s | **A battle at 2× speed** | a rotation of three canned battles, one per loop: Winter Lakeside (Solmark against Hoarfast, the lake frozen); Spring River Ford (Verdance against Amberlyn, the fords flooded); and the Sanctum with every dial lit. The showcase AI prefers specials and spells. Scripted inserts make sure a Tide banner, a capture, a level-up and a promotion flash appear. Captions name each mechanic. |\n2008\t| 65–80 s | **The Gray Knight** | the clock chamber, three lines on auto-advance |\n2009\t| 80–90 s | **Logo** | \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\", then the loop starts again |\n2010\t\n2011\tAny input (the same set as the idle timer) calls `input.consumeAll()` and goes to the title. On a touch-only device a\n2012\ttap goes to the title with its notice, and attract returns after 10 idle seconds.\n2013\t\n2014\t### 10.3 Dev mode (pause menu → Dev Mode; absent in hub sessions)\n2015\tA full-screen panel with tabs (L1/R1, or click), built from the UI kit, so it works with a pad, keys or a mouse.\n2016\tAnything touched marks the campaign \"DEV\" in its save and on the HUD.\n2017\t\n2018\t| Tab | Tools |\n2019\t|---|---|\n2020\t| Cheats | God mode (the player's units take no damage); one-hit KOs; infinite MP; free summons; +1000 mana; heal all; level up the selected unit (+1, +5); give an item (a list); add a free knight; spawn a monster into the selected castle or troop; unlock all class changes; reveal the AI's planned marches |\n2021\t| Battle | win now; lose now; KO the selected unit; set the bell; set the season (terrain re-applies); toggle AI control of the player's side (autoplay); Delegate the rest of the battle; light all Sanctum dials |\n2022\t| Campaign | jump to a season and year; skip to Muster or March; trigger any event (a list of every event id); set a castle's owner; run N AI seasons; autoplay the player's realm; burn or refill the candle; go to any ending |\n2023\t| Balance | **live sliders for every tunable in Appendix A**, grouped (combat, magic, economy, AI, pacing). Left/right adjusts (hold to accelerate); the mouse drags the bar; △ resets one slider; **\"Reset all to defaults\"** at the top. Changes apply at once because the sims read `G.tune` |\n2024\t| View | hex coordinates; the AI's danger map; every unit's Ward; the AI's top 3 plans per unit; a free camera; HUD on/off; weather on/off; time scale (.25×–8×); the gallery (`#gallery`); a frame-time readout (the engine's own setting) |\n2025\t| Info | seed, build, state hash, the last 50 sim events, `game.errors`, a \"Copy report\" button (`E.diagnose()`) |\n2026\t\n2027\t### 10.4 About & Credits (`66-scene-about.js`, data in `10-data-about.js`)\n2028\tPages, flipped with left/right or L1/R1, at most 8 lines each in 10-foot text. **The builder fills in every value at\n2029\tthe end and writes \"unknown\" for anything it can't confirm:**\n2030\t1. **The game:** title, tagline (\"Four seasons. Four crowns. One stopped clock.\"), version and build date.\n2031\t2. **Source Information**, each field from TASK.md:\n2032\t   - Date: 2026-11-03 17:47:58;\n2033\t   - Source: Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin / Atlus, PlayStation, 1998);\n2034\t   - Plan: PLAN.md;\n2035\t   - Genre and Perspective;\n2036\t   - Tech;\n2037\t   - Art Direction;\n2038\t   - Animation;\n2039\t   - Audio;\n2040\t   - Online;\n2041\t   - Testing;\n2042\t   - Research;\n2043\t   - Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown;\n2044\t   - Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max;\n2045\t   - Usage.\n2046\t3. **Testing Feedback:** the four answers.\n2047\t4. **Engine Feedback:** the six answers (draw on ENGINE-CHANGES.md).\n2048\t5. **Prompt Feedback:** the four answers.\n2049\t6. **Credits:**\n2050\t   - the my-3D2dge engine (MIT) by Michael Crosato; the AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0;\n2051\t   - any asset sets used: Kenney, KayKit and ambientCG, all CC0, as in their catalogs;\n2052\t   - \"Inspired by Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena. The world, characters, music and art are original.\"\n2053\tThe same text feeds `exit-interview.json` (§15), so the two always agree.\n2054\t\n2055\t### 10.5 How to Play (from the title, the pause menu and F1)\n2056\tEight pages, each with a live diorama of rigs:\n2057\t1. The Wheel and the seasons.\n2058\t2. Muster.\n2059\t3. Summon and Bond.\n2060\t4. Quests.\n2061\t5. March.\n2062\t6. Bells and the Keep.\n2063\t7. Ward, size and elements.\n2064\t8. Knights, retreat and capture.\n2065\t\n2066\t### 10.6 Game settings (beside the engine's standard settings)\n2067\t\n2068\t| key | Label | Options (default first) |\n2069\t|---|---|---|\n2070\t| glyphs | Controller glyphs | PlayStation, Xbox |\n2071\t| battleAnim | Battle animations | Full, Fast, Minimal |\n2072\t| battleCam | Battle camera | Dynamic, Fixed |\n2073\t| battleView | Battle view | Board, Isometric |\n2074\t| grid | Grid lines | Subtle, Bold, Off |\n2075\t| tips | Tutorial tips | On, Off |\n2076\t| textSpeed | Text speed | Normal, Slow, Fast, Instant |\n2077\t| voices | Voices | On, Off |\n2078\t| uiScale | UI scale | Normal, Large |\n2079\t| edgePan | Edge panning (mouse) | Off, On |\n2080\t| aiBattles | Battles between AI realms | Show result, Skip |\n2081\t| confirmEnd | Confirm before ending a turn | On, Off |\n2082\t| hotseatTimer | Hot-seat turn timer | Off, 60 s, 30 s |\n2083\t| privacy | Hot-seat privacy cards | On, Off |\n2084\t\n2085\tDifficulty is chosen per campaign, and the Realm screen shows it.\n2086\t\n2087\t### 10.7 Skirmish (`skirmishSetup`)\n2088\t- **Choose:**\n2089\t  - a map (any of the 13 except the tutorial and the Sanctum);\n2090\t  - a season (Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter, or \"Wheel\": it turns every bell);\n2091\t  - 2–4 sides, each Human (P1–P4, claimed by pressing ✕ on a pad or with the keyboard) or CPU (Easy, Normal or Hard);\n2092\t  - an army per side: a realm (one of the four, the Dominion or Brigands) and a level band (5, 10, 15 or 20). This builds\n2093\t    up to 3 troops from that realm's roster, scaled.\n2094\t- **Banners of the Wheel:** a preset that sets the Wheel Shrine map and its free-for-all rules (§6.10).\n2095\t- After the battle: Rematch, Change setup or Title.\n2096\t\n2097\t### 10.8 Hot-seat and local play (`81-local-mp.js`)\n2098\t- **Seats:**\n2099\t  - Seat 1 is the keyboard, the mouse and the first pad.\n2100\t  - Others join with `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` (Start or ✕ on a free pad, or the right half of the keyboard as the\n2101\t    engine allows), or play on the shared device.\n2102\t  - Each human realm stores a seat.\n2103\t- **Turn routing:** during a human realm's Muster, March or troop turn, the UI kit reads only that seat's input (if it\n2104\t  has one) or every input (if shared). Other seats can move a passive \"look\" cursor.\n2105\t- **Privacy:** if Settings → \"Privacy cards\" is On, a ruler card (\"pass the controller\") separates humans.\n2106\t- **Human against human:** each side's troops read their own seat. The optional turn timer (Settings) auto-delegates\n2107\t  units that run out of time.\n2108\t- Saves keep seats and the human/AI flags. Loading asks seats to be claimed again.\n2109\t\n2110\t---\n2111\t\n2112\t## 11. Online: AI Hub (Session Protocol v1)\n2113\t\n2114\t### 11.1 Mode and game\n2115\t- **Mode:** `shared-world`, with 2–4 players.\n2116\t- **The game:** \"Banners of the Wheel\": the Wheel Shrine map with its free-for-all rules (§6.10). Each seat fields one\n2117\t  ruler at level 10 with two monsters at level 10:\n2118\t\n2119\t| Seat | Ruler | Monsters | Corner |\n2120\t|---|---|---|---|\n2121\t| 0 | Gareth (Spring) | unicorn, pixie | NE |\n2122\t| 1 | Morgause (Summer) | cinderhound, sunbird | SE |\n2123\t| 2 | Pellam (Autumn) | scarecrow, griffin (level 9) | SW |\n2124\t| 3 | Mordrain (Winter) | frostwolf, ice golem (level 9) | NW |\n2125\t\n2126\t- With 2 players use seats 0 and 2 (the NE and SW corners). Balance the four with 200 AI-only four-way runs: each\n2127\t  seat's win rate should land between 20% and 30% (§14.5).\n2128\t\n2129\t### 11.2 Tags (in `<head>`, after the session client, the first script)\n2130\t```html\n2131\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n2132\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n2133\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n2134\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Most glory wins: rout rivals and hold the Shrine\">\n2135\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD: cursor · ✕/Enter: select · ○/Esc: back · □/Space: end turn\">\n2136\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"9\">\n2137\t```\n2138\t\n2139\t### 11.3 Session flow\n2140\t1. If `AIHub.active`:\n2141\t   - skip the title, attract mode, menus, tutorial and deep links. The boot screen may show but asks nothing;\n2142\t   - disable saves, dev mode, Quit to title and `autoPause` (`new E.Game({ autoPause: !AIHub.active })`).\n2143\t2. Call `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] })`. If it returns `null`, carry on with\n2144\t   the normal title.\n2145\t3. Build the battle for `info.players` (seat i takes realm i). Setup randomness comes from `AIHub.rng('setup')`, so\n2146\t   every copy builds the same field. Names come from `info.players[i].name` and are drawn on the canvas, never inserted\n2147\t   as HTML. The seat colours tint the pennants.\n2148\t4. Call `AIHub.ready()` once the scene is built, with no key press. Use the hub's own card (`card` left off).\n2149\t5. On `start`, show 3-2-1 in large numerals while `AIHub.time() < 0`. At 0 the host starts bell 1.\n2150\t\n2151\t### 11.4 Roles and messages\n2152\t- **The host** (`info.isHost`) runs `BattleSim`:\n2153\t  - it is seeded from `AIHub.rng('battle')` and its state lives in G.Rng;\n2154\t  - it owns the turn order and the deadlines: 15 s per troop, measured on `AIHub.time()`. Animations run at Fast in\n2155\t    sessions;\n2156\t  - it validates every command and broadcasts the results.\n2157\t- **The other copies** draw the host's state, animate its events and send commands only for their own troop during its\n2158\t  turn.\n2159\t- **`G.NetDriver`** runs on `setInterval(50)`, outside the engine's pausable update, on every copy. Opening the pause\n2160\t  menu (for Settings) never stalls the host. Incoming messages are queued and applied in order.\n2161\t\n2162\t| `t` | Direction | Payload | When |\n2163\t|---|---|---|---|\n2164\t| `snap` | host → all | `{ n, state }`: the compact `BattleSim.serialize()` (units, cells, HP, MP, effects, bell, order, season, glory), about 2–3 KB | at each bell's start, after each troop's turn, and on request |\n2165\t| `ev` | host → all | `{ n, events }`: what `apply` returned, for animation | after each applied command |\n2166\t| `turn` | host → all | `{ n, seat, troop, deadline }` | when a troop's turn starts |\n2167\t| `cmd` | a client → host | `{ seq, cmd }` (move, act, guard, wait, end) | during that client's own turn |\n2168\t| `need` | a client → host | `{ n }` | when a gap in `n` is seen; the host answers with `snap` |\n2169\t| `cur` | a client → all (`reliable: false`, at most 4 a second) | `{ seat, cell }` | other players' cursors, drawn as hex outlines in their colours |\n2170\t| `over` | host → all | `{ standings, glory }` | at the end, just before `finish` |\n2171\t\n2172\t- `n` is the host's event counter, and clients apply `ev` strictly in order.\n2173\t- **An illegal or stale `cmd`** (not that seat's turn, or `sim.legal` false) is ignored, and the host sends that client a\n2174\t  `snap`.\n2175\t- **At a deadline,** the host plays the rest of that troop with the battle AI and marks the player's banner \"AUTO\".\n2176\t- Traffic stays far under the hub's limits (20 messages a second, 16 KB each).\n2177\t\n2178\t### 11.5 Ending a round\n2179\t- The round ends:\n2180\t  - after bell 6;\n2181\t  - when only one player's knight still stands;\n2182\t  - or on `time-up`, when the host finishes at once, within `graceMs`.\n2183\t- The host then sends `over`, then calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores: glory, stats: { id: { damage, kos, shrine\n2184\t  } }, awards: [{ id, title: 'Shrine Keeper' | 'Giant Slayer' | 'Last Standing', detail }] })`. Standings are grouped by\n2185\t  glory (ties share a place).\n2186\t- **`leave`:** the host removes that seat's troop (it retreats). If fewer than 2 players remain, it finishes.\n2187\t- **`end`:** stop all input and sound (stop the music, mute the effects bus, ignore actions), and show \"Round over\" with\n2188\t  the standings until the hub removes the game.\n2189\t- **Server mode** (`info.server`): the host has no player of its own. It runs exactly the same host code with no camera\n2190\t  or input, and draws a quiet spectator view.\n2191\t\n2192\t### 11.6 The hub's rules\n2193\t- The network goes only through `AIHub`; the game has no other network code at all.\n2194\t- No chat, emotes or custom names.\n2195\t- No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation.\n2196\t- Fullscreen requests go through the engine as usual (the client hands them to the hub).\n2197\t- **Create + Options belong to the hub:** bind a `create: ['Pad8']` action, and on every step while it is down call\n2198\t  `input.suppress('pause')`.\n2199\t- **A touch-only device in a session** calls `AIHub.fail('Controller or keyboard required')`.\n2200\t- `Math.random` is not seeded in shared world, and the sim never uses it anyway.\n2201\t\n2202\t### 11.7 Standalone\n2203\tThe same rules are Skirmish → \"Banners of the Wheel\" with local seats and CPUs (§10.7). The hub layer is never loaded\n2204\tinto play when `AIHub.active` is false.\n2205\t\n2206\t---\n2207\t\n2208\t## 12. Build order and milestones\n2209\tThe two riskiest pieces go first (the hex field, then the beasts), because everything visual depends on them. Then the\n2210\tpure sims, before the scenes that show them. The AI comes early, because Delegate, the bots and the balance runs all\n2211\tneed it. Every milestone ends with its suites green and the full run green.\n2212\t\n2213\t| # | Milestone | Build | Done when |\n2214\t|---|---|---|---|\n2215\t| M0 | Scaffold | the dev folder; the engine and hub copied in; `build.mjs` (concatenation, the single file, the guards); `tests/run.mjs`; the `TMPDIR` set-up; an empty title scene with the logo | the single HTML opens from `file://` with no errors (`tools/check.mjs`); the hub client is the first script; `node tests/run.mjs` prints its count line |\n2216\t| M1 | Hex field spike | `G.hex`; the floor baked through `floorTex` for 2 terrains and 4 seasons, with edges; range and cursor decals; picking through `mouseGround`; cursor stepping by screen direction; the `board` view, 60° turns, zoom; a Humanoid walking a `grid.reach` path; one `hexblock` shape with x-ray | the `hex` suite is green; Border Meadow screenshots in all four seasons look right |\n2217\t| M2 | BattleSim | everything in §5: deployment, bells, legality, actions, formulas, effects, Ward, capture, death, Keep, wins, EXP, forecast, serialize, hash | the `rules` and `determinism` suites are green |\n2218\t| M3 | Battle scene and AI | `EventPlayer`; Humanoid moves, projectiles, effects, numbers; the HUD; the player's command flows; the camera; the battle AI; Delegate; results | `ai-battle` is green (all 13 maps × 4 seasons); the input-driven tutorial win passes in `ui-flow` |\n2219\t| M4 | Beasts and bestiary | `engine-ext/beasts.js` (the 4 kinds and their presets), `E.Wings`, all 30 species × 3 forms, Blob overlays, portraits, the gallery; the custom shapes (castles, keep, hexblock, clock tower) | the gallery runs with no errors; filmstrips of every kind's walk, bite and breath are reviewed; `asset-sheet` checks of the custom shapes are reviewed |\n2220\t| M5 | CampaignSim and realm AI | everything in §4, the event trigger engine (without scenes), save serialization | `campaign`, `ai-campaign` and `save` are green |\n2221\t| M6 | Campaign scene | the world map (continent, roads, castles, banners, figures, markers, season wipes); the HUD; every Muster panel; March; resolution with Command and Delegate; Tidings; `game.saves` | the `ui-flow` campaign path runs (one full season with a commanded battle) |\n2222\t| M7 | Story | stages, every event in §6.12, vignettes, recruitment, endings and credits, rival lines, the Dialog voice hook and the babble synth, tutorial tips | `story` is green; the first `playthrough` run reaches a good ending |\n2223\t| M8 | Audio | every song, sting, sound effect and voice profile; music by scene and season; layers | `audio` is green; a browser check finds sound starts after the first input with no errors |\n2224\t| M9 | Front end | title, setup, skirmish setup, How to Play, About, settings, the touch-only notice, the attract mode, the prompt bar and glyphs, UI scale | `attract`, `touch` and `prompts` are green |\n2225\t| M10 | Dev mode | the panel, every tool, the sliders with Reset | `dev` is green |\n2226\t| M11 | Multiplayer | hot-seat and local seats; Banners of the Wheel locally; the AI Hub layer (§11) | `localmp` and `hub-unit` are green; the harness passes every scenario (§14.6) |\n2227\t| M12 | Content and balance | every knight, monster, item, map and event; balance passes with `simulate.mjs` | the balance targets in §14.5 are met; all five `playthrough` runs pass |\n2228\t| M13 | Polish and ship | act on every look note from `check.mjs`; review 1920 × 1080 and 1280 × 720 screenshots for 10-foot reading; the final bundle; the About text and `exit-interview.json` | every item in §15 is checked |\n2229\t\n2230\t---\n2231\t\n2232\t## 13. Risks and how to defuse them\n2233\t\n2234\t| Risk | Why | Defusing it |\n2235\t|---|---|---|\n2236\t| A hex battlefield on an engine built for square tiles | the floor, picking, turning and decals are all ours | M1 is a spike before anything else. Baking the floor through `floorTex` keeps the engine's renderer, lighting and GPU path. The field is flat, so picking through `mouseGround` is exact. Raised hexes are shapes that sort like props. Fallback: per-terrain `floorMats` with hex outlines drawn only as decals |\n2237\t| Beast rigs, a new art system | 13 species need them, in 3 forms each, and they must read at 12–70 px | M4 comes early. Build `quad` first (it covers 9 species), then `drake` (4), `avian` (2) and `serpent` (3); presets and recolours carry the forms; the gallery and filmstrips check them. Fallback per species: a winged cat quad for the griffin, a Blob-headed quad, and so on |\n2238\t| Battle pacing with up to 42 units | AI turns drag | Turns go by troop; Fast and Minimal animations; hold to fast-forward; Delegate a battle or one troop. Target: an early battle under 10 minutes, a late one under 20 |\n2239\t| The campaign AI stalls or snowballs | pacing breaks; the game becomes unwinnable or trivial | `simulate.mjs` runs 50 AI-only seeds and 50 seeds with the player on autoplay per difficulty, and reports castles over time, winners and the season Meridian falls. Thresholds are tunables, and the Dominion's aggression is scripted by year |\n2240\t| Determinism (saves, the hub, tests) | a stray `Math.random`, clock read or iteration order | all sim randomness goes through `G.Rng`; a test greps the sims and AI for `Math.random`, `Date.now` and `performance`; double runs compare hashes; state is plain JSON |\n2241\t| The shared world | latency, loss, the host leaving, a paused host | host authority with ordered events, snapshots and resync; `NetDriver` runs outside the pause; the harness runs with latency, jitter and loss, and the host-leave and server scenarios |\n2242\t| Reading at 10 feet | pixel UIs grow dense | the rules in §8.1; screenshots at 1080p and 720p; the Large UI scale |\n2243\t| Content volume (36 knights, 90 monster forms, 13 maps, about 40 events) | time | registries and the data suite; templates for vignettes; the maps are already drawn and checked in this plan |\n2244\t| Engine unknowns (naming a custom view, the Dialog voice hook, the effects bus, Esc vs pause) | each could block a feature | changing the engine is allowed: patch it in place and log it. Look at the pinball kit's `E.View` use; settle all four in M0–M1 |\n2245\t| The single-file bundle | escaping, size, load order | guards in `build.mjs`, and the `bundle` suite opens the built file in Chromium |\n2246\t| This machine's full `/tmp` | Chromium and Playwright need temp space | `TMPDIR` on the main disk, checked in M0 |\n2247\t| Auto-pause in the harness's frames | an unfocused host frame would pause | `autoPause: false` in sessions, and the `NetDriver` interval |\n2248\t\n2249\t---\n2250\t\n2251\t## 14. Testing\n2252\t\n2253\t### 14.1 The one command\n2254\t- `node tests/run.mjs [suite ...] [--browser]` runs the Node suites; `--browser` adds the Playwright ones. It prints only\n2255\t  failures (`suite › test: message`) and one final line, `N passed, M failed (S suites, T s)`, and exits with 1 on\n2256\t  failure.\n2257\t- The Node harness loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, `engine-ext/beasts.js` and `dist/game.js` into a `vm` context with the\n2258\t  stand-ins `kits/test.mjs` uses (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`). It drives the game with `game.advance`,\n2259\t  `input.tap` / `hold` / `feed` and `game.debug`.\n2260\t- As TASK.md asks: test with headless tools and scripts that play the game and read its state; take screenshots only\n2261\t  for what a script can't check (§14.4); rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (§14.7); and don't use\n2262\t  subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n2263\t\n2264\t### 14.2 Suites (each line names what it proves)\n2265\t\n2266\t| Suite | Covers |\n2267\t|---|---|\n2268\t| `data` | every reference resolves; the counts (25 castles, 36 roads, 30 species × 3 forms, 36 knights, 13 maps, 90 skills, 33 items); the map checker from planning (row lengths, anchors, room, the Keep reachable in every season, floods and ice included); the road graph is connected and the same shape for every realm; a deny-list of the source's proper names (§1.2) over data and story; no TODO, FIXME or placeholder |\n2269\t| `hex` | neighbours, distances, lines, cones and rings match `E.Grid`; `center` and `toCell` round-trip for every hex; screen direction → neighbour at all 6 turns; picking: a hex centre projected to the screen comes back through `mouseGround` as the same hex |\n2270\t| `rules` | each formula with fixed rolls: hit (size, flank, guard, terrain, range); damage (strong and same element, Tide ±, terrain, guard, surround, crit); magic; healing; statuses (chance, duration, Sleep waking, Stop immunity); the Ward penalty. Also: spells illegal after moving; mobile specials legal after moving; Charge and Dive needing 2 hexes; Keep healing and the last-bell seizure; a ruler's retreat losing the battle; a fallen knight taking its troop and the capture chances; monsters dying for good; EXP and level-ups; every season's transforms (flood, ice, drying, fire → ash); the Sanctum's dials, hand and Timeless; hub glory |\n2271\t| `determinism` | the same seed and commands give the same hash, in battle and campaign; no `Math.random`, `Date.now` or `performance` in sims or AI |\n2272\t| `ai-battle` | the AI only issues legal commands; it wins clearly favourable fights at least 90% of 200 runs; rulers keep out of danger; attackers go for the Keep late; every map × season ends within 12 bells; an auto-resolved 3-against-3 battle takes under 150 ms |\n2273\t| `campaign` | the phases cycle; income, upkeep and desertion; summon limits and summon level; Bond limits; moving only to adjacent castles; quest outcome rates (10,000 rolls within ±2% of the weights) and modifiers; march rules (adjacency, 3 troops, once a season); resolution order; empty castles taken without a battle; aftermath (retreat paths, wounds, captures into reserves, treasuries); elimination; Stillness; the candle; every way to win or lose, a rival setting the Wheel included |\n2274\t| `ai-campaign` | 20 AI-only seeds per difficulty reach an end; no realm wins more than 45% of them; there is at least one battle every two seasons; the Dominion stays home in Year 1 |\n2275\t| `save` | serialize → load → equal hash (mid-Muster, with knights away, wounded and stilled castles); the `game.saves` slots; migration from a v1 fixture |\n2276\t| `story` | every event's speakers, conditions and effects are valid; every event fires from the dev trigger without errors; each realm's chain is reachable in a scripted campaign; all 4 good endings and the 3 kinds of bad ending are reachable; rival lines fire for their pairs |\n2277\t| `ui-flow` | input only (taps, holds, `feed` for the mouse): title → new campaign (each realm) → prologue → tutorial win → Muster (summon, bind, move, quest, equip, promote) → March → a commanded battle (select, move, attack, spell, wait, end) → results → Tidings; pause → save → load; How to Play and About open and close; ○ / Esc backs out of every panel; mouse hover focuses, a click confirms, a right click goes back |\n2278\t| `prompts` | a gamepad shows ✕ ○ □ △; with the Xbox setting, A B X Y; a keyboard shows key names; a mouse shows its buttons; prompts change on the step after the device does |\n2279\t| `attract` | 10 s idle on the title starts attract; a key, a mouse move, a pad button or a touch returns to the title within a step; a full 95 s loop runs with no errors and reaches every beat (`snapshot().attract.beat`) |\n2280\t| `touch` | with `G.forceTouchOnly`, the title shows the notice and its Settings button; no scene has touch buttons; attract still starts |\n2281\t| `dev` | the panel opens from the pause menu; spot checks of each tab's tools (god mode, win now, give an item, trigger an event, jump a season); a slider changes the outcome (`dmgScale` 2 doubles a fixed-roll hit); Reset restores the defaults; the DEV flag is set |\n2282\t| `audio` | every song's tokens parse; every scene and season has music; every sound id used is defined; `voice.plan` gives the same syllables for the same line; no audio files are referenced |\n2283\t| `localmp` | in hot-seat with 2 humans, input reaches only the active seat; privacy cards show; a human-against-human battle reads each seat; a 4-seat local Banners of the Wheel with CPUs finishes |\n2284\t| `hub-unit` | `NetDriver` against a fake `AIHub` in Node: host and client exchange messages; ordering; a gap → `need` → `snap`; illegal commands rejected; a deadline → AUTO; `leave`; `time-up` → `finish` standings; `end` stops input |\n2285\t| `playthrough` | for each realm, a new Normal campaign on autoplay: the player's realm uses the campaign and battle AIs through the same commands; battles are Delegated except the tutorial and one battle a year, which the bot fights through the battle scene with real inputs. `tune.aiPlayerBoost` may be raised to make the win reliable. It must reach `meridian_falls`, win the Sanctum and play the ending and credits with no errors. A fifth run lets the candle burn out (the defeat path) |\n2286\t| `bundle` (`--browser`) | build; the single HTML has no external URLs; the first script after `<meta charset>` is the unmodified session client; the hub tags are present; it opens from `file://` in headless Chromium (`engine/tools/check.mjs`) with no errors; boot → title; attract starts after 10 s |\n2287\t| `hub` (`--browser`) | the harness procedure in §14.6 |\n2288\t| `about` | the About pages carry every Source Information field and the three feedback lists; `exit-interview.json` parses and every key has a value (run at the end) |\n2289\t\n2290\t### 14.3 Bots\n2291\t- **Battle bot:** drives the battle scene through `game.input`. It moves the cursor with taps, then confirms, using the\n2292\t  battle AI's chosen command, so it tests the real UI path.\n2293\t- **Campaign bot:** works the Muster panels through input for at least one season per realm, then switches to sim-level\n2294\t  autoplay for speed.\n2295\t\n2296\t### 14.4 Looking (only what a script can't check)\n2297\t- **Screenshots:** `node engine/tools/check.mjs dist/index.html#<link> --size 1920x1080` (and `1280x720`) of the title,\n2298\t  the campaign in each season, the castle card and the Organize and Summon panels, a battle in each season (River Ford),\n2299\t  the Sanctum, a story stage, results, and About. Act on every look note.\n2300\t- **Filmstrips:** `engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1` of every class move, each beast kind's walk, bite and breath, a\n2301\t  summon, a capture and a promotion.\n2302\t- **The gallery:** every species in all 3 forms.\n2303\t\n2304\t### 14.5 Balance runs (`tools/simulate.mjs`)\n2305\t- **Commands:** `--campaigns 50 --difficulty normal`; `--battles 500 --map river_ford`; `--hub 200`. Each prints summary\n2306\t  tables.\n2307\t- **Targets:**\n2308\t  - AI-only campaigns: no realm wins more than 40%; they end in seasons 12–16 on average;\n2309\t  - the player's realm on autoplay (Normal) reaches Meridian between seasons 10 and 14 in at least 60% of seeds;\n2310\t  - early battles average 8 bells or fewer;\n2311\t  - hub seats each win 20–30% of the time.\n2312\t\n2313\t### 14.6 The AI Hub harness\n2314\t1. Copy `vendor/hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` and the built game HTML into `dist/hub/`.\n2315\t2. Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (with `TMPDIR` set) and note its PID and port.\n2316\t3. Fetch `/<game>.html` and check its `<title>` is ours.\n2317\t4. Run `tools/hub-check.mjs` (Playwright) on each of these:\n2318\t   - `harness.html?game=<game>.html&players=2&auto=1`\n2319\t   - `harness.html?game=<game>.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n2320\t   - `harness.html?game=<game>.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\n2321\t   - `harness.html?game=<game>.html&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n2322\t\n2323\t   Each must end with `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` and `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`.\n2324\t5. Open the game outside a session and check it still runs normally.\n2325\t6. Stop the server by its PID.\n2326\t\n2327\t### 14.7 When to rerun\n2328\tAfter a change, rerun only the suites that cover the changed files:\n2329\t\n2330\t| Changed | Rerun |\n2331\t|---|---|\n2332\t| `20–21` | `rules`, `determinism`, `ai-battle` |\n2333\t| `22–24` | `campaign`, `ai-campaign`, `save` |\n2334\t| `0x` data | `data`, plus the suites that use it |\n2335\t| `09` | `story` |\n2336\t| `3x` art | the `ui-flow` smoke run, and look checks on demand |\n2337\t| `4x` | `audio` |\n2338\t| `5x–6x` | `ui-flow`, `prompts`, `attract`, `touch` |\n2339\t| `70` | `dev` |\n2340\t| `80–81` | `hub-unit`, `localmp`, `hub` |\n2341\t\n2342\tRun everything at each milestone's exit and at the end.\n2343\t\n2344\t---\n2345\t\n2346\t## 15. Done: the checklist\n2347\t- [ ] Every system in §4–§11 works, with no TODO, FIXME, placeholder or stub (the build guard and the `data` suite).\n2348\t- [ ] All the content in §6 is in the game (the counts in the `data` suite).\n2349\t- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs --browser` passes. All five playthroughs pass, and the harness passes all four scenarios.\n2350\t- [ ] The single file sits in this folder's root under the exact name in §0. It opens from `file://`; its first script\n2351\t      is the unmodified hub client; the hub tags are present.\n2352\t- [ ] About & Credits is complete. The final chat reply carries the same Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine\n2353\t      Feedback and Prompt Feedback, with \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed.\n2354\t- [ ] `exit-interview.json` sits beside the HTML, in exactly TASK.md's shape, with every value filled in, and it\n2355\t      parses. Suggested `aiHub` values:\n2356\t  - name \"Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons\"; tagline \"Four seasons. Four crowns. One stopped clock.\";\n2357\t  - description \"A seasonal war of monster-binding knights: muster castles, summon beasts and fight twelve-bell hex\n2358\t    battles to restart the Wheel of Seasons before time stops forever.\";\n2359\t  - type \"Game\"; genre \"Strategy\"; source \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena\"; series \"Brigandine\"; players \"1–4\";\n2360\t  - controls \"Stick/WASD: cursor · ✕/Enter: select · ○/Esc: back · □/Space: commands · △/I: info · L1/R1 or Tab:\n2361\t    cycle\";\n2362\t  - tags `[\"fantasy\", \"story\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"retro\", \"boss fights\"]`.\n2363\t- [ ] ENGINE-CHANGES.md is complete.\n2364\t- [ ] Every server you started is stopped, by PID. This folder gains only the dev folder, the HTML and\n2365\t      `exit-interview.json`.\n2366\t\n2367\t---\n2368\t\n2369\t## Appendix A: Tunables (`G.TUNE_DEFAULTS`; each is a dev-mode slider)\n2370\t\n2371\t| key | Default | Slider range | Used by |\n2372\t|---|---|---|---|\n2373\t| dmgScale | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | physical damage |\n2374\t| defFactor | 0.5 | 0–1 | physical damage |\n2375\t| magicScale | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | magic damage |\n2376\t| healScale | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | healing |\n2377\t| baseHit | 85 | 50–100 | hit chance |\n2378\t| largeVsSmall | −30 | −60–0 | the size table (L against S) |\n2379\t| critBase | 3 | 0–30 | crit chance |\n2380\t| wardPenalty | 0.20 | 0–0.6 | monsters outside their Ward |\n2381\t| surroundBonus | 0.10 | 0–0.3 | damage per adjacent ally |\n2382\t| elemStrong | 1.30 | 1–2 | opposed elements |\n2383\t| elemSame | 0.80 | 0.5–1 | matching elements |\n2384\t| tideBonus | 0.15 | 0–0.5 | the Seasonal Tide |\n2385\t| forestDef | 0.20 | 0–0.5 | forest DEF |\n2386\t| statusScale | 1.0 | 0–2 | status chances |\n2387\t| captureBase | 0.25 | 0–1 | capture chance |\n2388\t| expScale | 1.0 | 0–5 | EXP |\n2389\t| bells | 12 | 4–20 | battle length |\n2390\t| manaIncome | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | castle yields |\n2391\t| summonCost | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | summon costs |\n2392\t| upkeepScale | 1.0 | 0–3 | upkeep |\n2393\t| seasonYield | 0.25 | 0–1 | the in-season yield bonus |\n2394\t| winterUpkeep | 0.25 | 0–1 | wintering |\n2395\t| questLuck | 1.0 | 0–2 | good quest outcome weights |\n2396\t| aiAggression | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | campaign AI (multiplies personality) |\n2397\t| aiManaBonus | 0 | −0.5–1 | AI income, on top of difficulty |\n2398\t| aiPlayerBoost | 0 | 0–1 | playthrough tests only: the player's units' stats × (1 + x) |\n2399\t| candleSeasons | 12 (by difficulty) | 4–30 | the Hour-Candle |\n2400\t| animSpeed | 1.0 | 0.25–4 | presentation speed |\n2401\t| hubTurnSeconds | 15 | 5–60 | hub troop timer (sessions always use the default) |\n2402\t\n2403\t## Appendix B: Research done while planning (for the \"Research\" field)\n2404\t- **Wikipedia, \"Brigandine (video game)\"** (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)):\n2405\t  - monthly Organize and Attack phases; mana income and upkeep; quests; Rune Power;\n2406\t  - up to three troops a side; the attacker's 12-turn limit; the leader and ruler retreat rules; the Rune Area;\n2407\t  - permanent monster death; the five colour elements; no spells after moving;\n2408\t  - the Grand Edition's 6-player multiplayer, final boss and hold-the-castle rule.\n2409\t- **RPGFan's review** (https://www.rpgfan.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena):\n2410\t  - the rulers' archetypes (the silent wise king, the prince, the queen, the war-loving king, the mad duke);\n2411\t  - brief dialogue between turns; the Risk-like map;\n2412\t  - big monsters struggling against small ones; formations; quest rewards.\n2413\t- **Read during planning:**\n2414\t  - my-3D2dge handoff v0.85.2: README, API.md, the relevant AI_GUIDE.md sections, the grid, story, arcade, strategy,\n2415\t    songs and rpg module headers, the TACTICS kit, docs/ASSETS.md and the asset catalogs;\n2416\t  - AI Hub `lib/hub`: README, retrofit.md and the examples.\n2417\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"25e14d4f-d445-4f02-91a7-eb114f4a1f96","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:02:48.412Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/PLAN.md","content":"---\n\n## 10. Modes and meta\n\n### 10.1 Boot and title\n- **Boot steps** (`game.start({ boot: { title: 'BRIGANTIME', steps } })`):\n  1. register and validate all data (it fails loudly on a bad reference);\n  2. build the icon and glyph sprites;\n  3. compose the songs;\n  4. bake the title diorama;\n  5. warm the first beast portraits.\n  Boot messages: \"Winding the Great Clock\", \"Teaching wyverns to sit\", \"Counting the bells\", \"Sweeping the cross-quarter\n  roads\".\n- **The title** (§8.5.1) and the setup menus before play (campaign setup, skirmish setup) track idle time: any key,\n  mouse button, pointer move over 4 px, pad button, stick past .5 or touch resets it. At 10 s they go to `attract`.\n  Reading screens (About, How to Play) and anything in play never do.\n- **On a touch-only device** (coarse pointer, no fine pointer, touch points, no gamepad or keyboard seen): show the\n  \"Controller or keyboard required\" panel with a large Settings button (`game.menu('settings')`) and no touch controls\n  (`touch: []` in every scene, `input.touchEnabled = false`). The idle timer still runs. A gamepad connecting or a key\n  pressed removes the notice for good.\n\n### 10.2 Attract mode (`67-scene-attract.js`)\nA scripted reel of about 90 s that loops and cheats freely (canned data, a fixed seed per loop, a showcase AI). A\n\"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" banner pulses at the bottom, with the logo in a corner.\n\n| Time | Beat | Shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0–12 s | **The Wheel turns** | the world map pans across the four regions while the seasons wipe every 3 s. `CampaignSim` runs AI-only on a canned seed, so banners flip and march arrows fly. Caption: \"FOUR SEASONS. FOUR CROWNS. ONE STOPPED CLOCK.\" |\n| 12–20 s | **Summoning** | Rimeholt's circle flares and a Frost Wyrm rises. Caption: \"BIND MONSTERS TO YOUR BANNER.\" |\n| 20–65 s | **A battle at 2× speed** | a rotation of three canned battles, one per loop: Winter Lakeside (Solmark against Hoarfast, the lake frozen); Spring River Ford (Verdance against Amberlyn, the fords flooded); and the Sanctum with every dial lit. The showcase AI prefers specials and spells. Scripted inserts make sure a Tide banner, a capture, a level-up and a promotion flash appear. Captions name each mechanic. |\n| 65–80 s | **The Gray Knight** | the clock chamber, three lines on auto-advance |\n| 80–90 s | **Logo** | \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\", then the loop starts again |\n\nAny input (the same set as the idle timer) calls `input.consumeAll()` and goes to the title. On a touch-only device a\ntap goes to the title with its notice, and attract returns after 10 idle seconds.\n\n### 10.3 Dev mode (pause menu → Dev Mode; absent in hub sessions)\nA full-screen panel with tabs (L1/R1, or click), built from the UI kit, so it works with a pad, keys or a mouse.\nAnything touched marks the campaign \"DEV\" in its save and on the HUD.\n\n| Tab | Tools |\n|---|---|\n| Cheats | God mode (the player's units take no damage); one-hit KOs; infinite MP; free summons; +1000 mana; heal all; level up the selected unit (+1, +5); give an item (a list); add a free knight; spawn a monster into the selected castle or troop; unlock all class changes; reveal the AI's planned marches |\n| Battle | win now; lose now; KO the selected unit; set the bell; set the season (terrain re-applies); toggle AI control of the player's side (autoplay); Delegate the rest of the battle; light all Sanctum dials |\n| Campaign | jump to a season and year; skip to Muster or March; trigger any event (a list of every event id); set a castle's owner; run N AI seasons; autoplay the player's realm; burn or refill the candle; go to any ending |\n| Balance | **live sliders for every tunable in Appendix A**, grouped (combat, magic, economy, AI, pacing). Left/right adjusts (hold to accelerate); the mouse drags the bar; △ resets one slider; **\"Reset all to defaults\"** at the top. Changes apply at once because the sims read `G.tune` |\n| View | hex coordinates; the AI's danger map; every unit's Ward; the AI's top 3 plans per unit; a free camera; HUD on/off; weather on/off; time scale (.25×–8×); the gallery (`#gallery`); a frame-time readout (the engine's own setting) |\n| Info | seed, build, state hash, the last 50 sim events, `game.errors`, a \"Copy report\" button (`E.diagnose()`) |\n\n### 10.4 About & Credits (`66-scene-about.js`, data in `10-data-about.js`)\nPages, flipped with left/right or L1/R1, at most 8 lines each in 10-foot text. **The builder fills in every value at\nthe end and writes \"unknown\" for anything it can't confirm:**\n1. **The game:** title, tagline (\"Four seasons. Four crowns. One stopped clock.\"), version and build date.\n2. **Source Information**, each field from TASK.md:\n   - Date: 2026-11-03 17:47:58;\n   - Source: Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin / Atlus, PlayStation, 1998);\n   - Plan: PLAN.md;\n   - Genre and Perspective;\n   - Tech;\n   - Art Direction;\n   - Animation;\n   - Audio;\n   - Online;\n   - Testing;\n   - Research;\n   - Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown;\n   - Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max;\n   - Usage.\n3. **Testing Feedback:** the four answers.\n4. **Engine Feedback:** the six answers (draw on ENGINE-CHANGES.md).\n5. **Prompt Feedback:** the four answers.\n6. **Credits:**\n   - the my-3D2dge engine (MIT) by Michael Crosato; the AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0;\n   - any asset sets used: Kenney, KayKit and ambientCG, all CC0, as in their catalogs;\n   - \"Inspired by Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena. The world, characters, music and art are original.\"\nThe same text feeds `exit-interview.json` (§15), so the two always agree.\n\n### 10.5 How to Play (from the title, the pause menu and F1)\nEight pages, each with a live diorama of rigs:\n1. The Wheel and the seasons.\n2. Muster.\n3. Summon and Bond.\n4. Quests.\n5. March.\n6. Bells and the Keep.\n7. Ward, size and elements.\n8. Knights, retreat and capture.\n\n### 10.6 Game settings (beside the engine's standard settings)\n\n| key | Label | Options (default first) |\n|---|---|---|\n| glyphs | Controller glyphs | PlayStation, Xbox |\n| battleAnim | Battle animations | Full, Fast, Minimal |\n| battleCam | Battle camera | Dynamic, Fixed |\n| battleView | Battle view | Board, Isometric |\n| grid | Grid lines | Subtle, Bold, Off |\n| tips | Tutorial tips | On, Off |\n| textSpeed | Text speed | Normal, Slow, Fast, Instant |\n| voices | Voices | On, Off |\n| uiScale | UI scale | Normal, Large |\n| edgePan | Edge panning (mouse) | Off, On |\n| aiBattles | Battles between AI realms | Show result, Skip |\n| confirmEnd | Confirm before ending a turn | On, Off |\n| hotseatTimer | Hot-seat turn timer | Off, 60 s, 30 s |\n| privacy | Hot-seat privacy cards | On, Off |\n\nDifficulty is chosen per campaign, and the Realm screen shows it.\n\n### 10.7 Skirmish (`skirmishSetup`)\n- **Choose:**\n  - a map (any of the 13 except the tutorial and the Sanctum);\n  - a season (Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter, or \"Wheel\": it turns every bell);\n  - 2–4 sides, each Human (P1–P4, claimed by pressing ✕ on a pad or with the keyboard) or CPU (Easy, Normal or Hard);\n  - an army per side: a realm (one of the four, the Dominion or Brigands) and a level band (5, 10, 15 or 20). This builds\n    up to 3 troops from that realm's roster, scaled.\n- **Banners of the Wheel:** a preset that sets the Wheel Shrine map and its free-for-all rules (§6.10).\n- After the battle: Rematch, Change setup or Title.\n\n### 10.8 Hot-seat and local play (`81-local-mp.js`)\n- **Seats:**\n  - Seat 1 is the keyboard, the mouse and the first pad.\n  - Others join with `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` (Start or ✕ on a free pad, or the right half of the keyboard as the\n    engine allows), or play on the shared device.\n  - Each human realm stores a seat.\n- **Turn routing:** during a human realm's Muster, March or troop turn, the UI kit reads only that seat's input (if it\n  has one) or every input (if shared). Other seats can move a passive \"look\" cursor.\n- **Privacy:** if Settings → \"Privacy cards\" is On, a ruler card (\"pass the controller\") separates humans.\n- **Human against human:** each side's troops read their own seat. The optional turn timer (Settings) auto-delegates\n  units that run out of time.\n- Saves keep seats and the human/AI flags. Loading asks seats to be claimed again.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Online: AI Hub (Session Protocol v1)\n\n### 11.1 Mode and game\n- **Mode:** `shared-world`, with 2–4 players.\n- **The game:** \"Banners of the Wheel\": the Wheel Shrine map with its free-for-all rules (§6.10). Each seat fields one\n  ruler at level 10 with two monsters at level 10:\n\n| Seat | Ruler | Monsters | Corner |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | Gareth (Spring) | unicorn, pixie | NE |\n| 1 | Morgause (Summer) | cinderhound, sunbird | SE |\n| 2 | Pellam (Autumn) | scarecrow, griffin (level 9) | SW |\n| 3 | Mordrain (Winter) | frostwolf, ice golem (level 9) | NW |\n\n- With 2 players use seats 0 and 2 (the NE and SW corners). Balance the four with 200 AI-only four-way runs: each\n  seat's win rate should land between 20% and 30% (§14.5).\n\n### 11.2 Tags (in `<head>`, after the session client, the first script)\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Most glory wins: rout rivals and hold the Shrine\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD: cursor · ✕/Enter: select · ○/Esc: back · □/Space: end turn\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"9\">\n```\n\n### 11.3 Session flow\n1. If `AIHub.active`:\n   - skip the title, attract mode, menus, tutorial and deep links. The boot screen may show but asks nothing;\n   - disable saves, dev mode, Quit to title and `autoPause` (`new E.Game({ autoPause: !AIHub.active })`).\n2. Call `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] })`. If it returns `null`, carry on with\n   the normal title.\n3. Build the battle for `info.players` (seat i takes realm i). Setup randomness comes from `AIHub.rng('setup')`, so\n   every copy builds the same field. Names come from `info.players[i].name` and are drawn on the canvas, never inserted\n   as HTML. The seat colours tint the pennants.\n4. Call `AIHub.ready()` once the scene is built, with no key press. Use the hub's own card (`card` left off).\n5. On `start`, show 3-2-1 in large numerals while `AIHub.time() < 0`. At 0 the host starts bell 1.\n\n### 11.4 Roles and messages\n- **The host** (`info.isHost`) runs `BattleSim`:\n  - it is seeded from `AIHub.rng('battle')` and its state lives in G.Rng;\n  - it owns the turn order and the deadlines: 15 s per troop, measured on `AIHub.time()`. Animations run at Fast in\n    sessions;\n  - it validates every command and broadcasts the results.\n- **The other copies** draw the host's state, animate its events and send commands only for their own troop during its\n  turn.\n- **`G.NetDriver`** runs on `setInterval(50)`, outside the engine's pausable update, on every copy. Opening the pause\n  menu (for Settings) never stalls the host. Incoming messages are queued and applied in order.\n\n| `t` | Direction | Payload | When |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `snap` | host → all | `{ n, state }`: the compact `BattleSim.serialize()` (units, cells, HP, MP, effects, bell, order, season, glory), about 2–3 KB | at each bell's start, after each troop's turn, and on request |\n| `ev` | host → all | `{ n, events }`: what `apply` returned, for animation | after each applied command |\n| `turn` | host → all | `{ n, seat, troop, deadline }` | when a troop's turn starts |\n| `cmd` | a client → host | `{ seq, cmd }` (move, act, guard, wait, end) | during that client's own turn |\n| `need` | a client → host | `{ n }` | when a gap in `n` is seen; the host answers with `snap` |\n| `cur` | a client → all (`reliable: false`, at most 4 a second) | `{ seat, cell }` | other players' cursors, drawn as hex outlines in their colours |\n| `over` | host → all | `{ standings, glory }` | at the end, just before `finish` |\n\n- `n` is the host's event counter, and clients apply `ev` strictly in order.\n- **An illegal or stale `cmd`** (not that seat's turn, or `sim.legal` false) is ignored, and the host sends that client a\n  `snap`.\n- **At a deadline,** the host plays the rest of that troop with the battle AI and marks the player's banner \"AUTO\".\n- Traffic stays far under the hub's limits (20 messages a second, 16 KB each).\n\n### 11.5 Ending a round\n- The round ends:\n  - after bell 6;\n  - when only one player's knight still stands;\n  - or on `time-up`, when the host finishes at once, within `graceMs`.\n- The host then sends `over`, then calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores: glory, stats: { id: { damage, kos, shrine\n  } }, awards: [{ id, title: 'Shrine Keeper' | 'Giant Slayer' | 'Last Standing', detail }] })`. Standings are grouped by\n  glory (ties share a place).\n- **`leave`:** the host removes that seat's troop (it retreats). If fewer than 2 players remain, it finishes.\n- **`end`:** stop all input and sound (stop the music, mute the effects bus, ignore actions), and show \"Round over\" with\n  the standings until the hub removes the game.\n- **Server mode** (`info.server`): the host has no player of its own. It runs exactly the same host code with no camera\n  or input, and draws a quiet spectator view.\n\n### 11.6 The hub's rules\n- The network goes only through `AIHub`; the game has no other network code at all.\n- No chat, emotes or custom names.\n- No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation.\n- Fullscreen requests go through the engine as usual (the client hands them to the hub).\n- **Create + Options belong to the hub:** bind a `create: ['Pad8']` action, and on every step while it is down call\n  `input.suppress('pause')`.\n- **A touch-only device in a session** calls `AIHub.fail('Controller or keyboard required')`.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded in shared world, and the sim never uses it anyway.\n\n### 11.7 Standalone\nThe same rules are Skirmish → \"Banners of the Wheel\" with local seats and CPUs (§10.7). The hub layer is never loaded\ninto play when `AIHub.active` is false.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Build order and milestones\nThe two riskiest pieces go first (the hex field, then the beasts), because everything visual depends on them. Then the\npure sims, before the scenes that show them. The AI comes early, because Delegate, the bots and the balance runs all\nneed it. Every milestone ends with its suites green and the full run green.\n\n| # | Milestone | Build | Done when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Scaffold | the dev folder; the engine and hub copied in; `build.mjs` (concatenation, the single file, the guards); `tests/run.mjs`; the `TMPDIR` set-up; an empty title scene with the logo | the single HTML opens from `file://` with no errors (`tools/check.mjs`); the hub client is the first script; `node tests/run.mjs` prints its count line |\n| M1 | Hex field spike | `G.hex`; the floor baked through `floorTex` for 2 terrains and 4 seasons, with edges; range and cursor decals; picking through `mouseGround`; cursor stepping by screen direction; the `board` view, 60° turns, zoom; a Humanoid walking a `grid.reach` path; one `hexblock` shape with x-ray | the `hex` suite is green; Border Meadow screenshots in all four seasons look right |\n| M2 | BattleSim | everything in §5: deployment, bells, legality, actions, formulas, effects, Ward, capture, death, Keep, wins, EXP, forecast, serialize, hash | the `rules` and `determinism` suites are green |\n| M3 | Battle scene and AI | `EventPlayer`; Humanoid moves, projectiles, effects, numbers; the HUD; the player's command flows; the camera; the battle AI; Delegate; results | `ai-battle` is green (all 13 maps × 4 seasons); the input-driven tutorial win passes in `ui-flow` |\n| M4 | Beasts and bestiary | `engine-ext/beasts.js` (the 4 kinds and their presets), `E.Wings`, all 30 species × 3 forms, Blob overlays, portraits, the gallery; the custom shapes (castles, keep, hexblock, clock tower) | the gallery runs with no errors; filmstrips of every kind's walk, bite and breath are reviewed; `asset-sheet` checks of the custom shapes are reviewed |\n| M5 | CampaignSim and realm AI | everything in §4, the event trigger engine (without scenes), save serialization | `campaign`, `ai-campaign` and `save` are green |\n| M6 | Campaign scene | the world map (continent, roads, castles, banners, figures, markers, season wipes); the HUD; every Muster panel; March; resolution with Command and Delegate; Tidings; `game.saves` | the `ui-flow` campaign path runs (one full season with a commanded battle) |\n| M7 | Story | stages, every event in §6.12, vignettes, recruitment, endings and credits, rival lines, the Dialog voice hook and the babble synth, tutorial tips | `story` is green; the first `playthrough` run reaches a good ending |\n| M8 | Audio | every song, sting, sound effect and voice profile; music by scene and season; layers | `audio` is green; a browser check finds sound starts after the first input with no errors |\n| M9 | Front end | title, setup, skirmish setup, How to Play, About, settings, the touch-only notice, the attract mode, the prompt bar and glyphs, UI scale | `attract`, `touch` and `prompts` are green |\n| M10 | Dev mode | the panel, every tool, the sliders with Reset | `dev` is green |\n| M11 | Multiplayer | hot-seat and local seats; Banners of the Wheel locally; the AI Hub layer (§11) | `localmp` and `hub-unit` are green; the harness passes every scenario (§14.6) |\n| M12 | Content and balance | every knight, monster, item, map and event; balance passes with `simulate.mjs` | the balance targets in §14.5 are met; all five `playthrough` runs pass |\n| M13 | Polish and ship | act on every look note from `check.mjs`; review 1920 × 1080 and 1280 × 720 screenshots for 10-foot reading; the final bundle; the About text and `exit-interview.json` | every item in §15 is checked |\n\n---\n\n## 13. Risks and how to defuse them\n\n| Risk | Why | Defusing it |\n|---|---|---|\n| A hex battlefield on an engine built for square tiles | the floor, picking, turning and decals are all ours | M1 is a spike before anything else. Baking the floor through `floorTex` keeps the engine's renderer, lighting and GPU path. The field is flat, so picking through `mouseGround` is exact. Raised hexes are shapes that sort like props. Fallback: per-terrain `floorMats` with hex outlines drawn only as decals |\n| Beast rigs, a new art system | 13 species need them, in 3 forms each, and they must read at 12–70 px | M4 comes early. Build `quad` first (it covers 9 species), then `drake` (4), `avian` (2) and `serpent` (3); presets and recolours carry the forms; the gallery and filmstrips check them. Fallback per species: a winged cat quad for the griffin, a Blob-headed quad, and so on |\n| Battle pacing with up to 42 units | AI turns drag | Turns go by troop; Fast and Minimal animations; hold to fast-forward; Delegate a battle or one troop. Target: an early battle under 10 minutes, a late one under 20 |\n| The campaign AI stalls or snowballs | pacing breaks; the game becomes unwinnable or trivial | `simulate.mjs` runs 50 AI-only seeds and 50 seeds with the player on autoplay per difficulty, and reports castles over time, winners and the season Meridian falls. Thresholds are tunables, and the Dominion's aggression is scripted by year |\n| Determinism (saves, the hub, tests) | a stray `Math.random`, clock read or iteration order | all sim randomness goes through `G.Rng`; a test greps the sims and AI for `Math.random`, `Date.now` and `performance`; double runs compare hashes; state is plain JSON |\n| The shared world | latency, loss, the host leaving, a paused host | host authority with ordered events, snapshots and resync; `NetDriver` runs outside the pause; the harness runs with latency, jitter and loss, and the host-leave and server scenarios |\n| Reading at 10 feet | pixel UIs grow dense | the rules in §8.1; screenshots at 1080p and 720p; the Large UI scale |\n| Content volume (36 knights, 90 monster forms, 13 maps, about 40 events) | time | registries and the data suite; templates for vignettes; the maps are already drawn and checked in this plan |\n| Engine unknowns (naming a custom view, the Dialog voice hook, the effects bus, Esc vs pause) | each could block a feature | changing the engine is allowed: patch it in place and log it. Look at the pinball kit's `E.View` use; settle all four in M0–M1 |\n| The single-file bundle | escaping, size, load order | guards in `build.mjs`, and the `bundle` suite opens the built file in Chromium |\n| This machine's full `/tmp` | Chromium and Playwright need temp space | `TMPDIR` on the main disk, checked in M0 |\n| Auto-pause in the harness's frames | an unfocused host frame would pause | `autoPause: false` in sessions, and the `NetDriver` interval |\n\n---\n\n## 14. Testing\n\n### 14.1 The one command\n- `node tests/run.mjs [suite ...] [--browser]` runs the Node suites; `--browser` adds the Playwright ones. It prints only\n  failures (`suite › test: message`) and one final line, `N passed, M failed (S suites, T s)`, and exits with 1 on\n  failure.\n- The Node harness loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, `engine-ext/beasts.js` and `dist/game.js` into a `vm` context with the\n  stand-ins `kits/test.mjs` uses (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`). It drives the game with `game.advance`,\n  `input.tap` / `hold` / `feed` and `game.debug`.\n- As TASK.md asks: test with headless tools and scripts that play the game and read its state; take screenshots only\n  for what a script can't check (§14.4); rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (§14.7); and don't use\n  subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n### 14.2 Suites (each line names what it proves)\n\n| Suite | Covers |\n|---|---|\n| `data` | every reference resolves; the counts (25 castles, 36 roads, 30 species × 3 forms, 36 knights, 13 maps, 90 skills, 33 items); the map checker from planning (row lengths, anchors, room, the Keep reachable in every season, floods and ice included); the road graph is connected and the same shape for every realm; a deny-list of the source's proper names (§1.2) over data and story; no TODO, FIXME or placeholder |\n| `hex` | neighbours, distances, lines, cones and rings match `E.Grid`; `center` and `toCell` round-trip for every hex; screen direction → neighbour at all 6 turns; picking: a hex centre projected to the screen comes back through `mouseGround` as the same hex |\n| `rules` | each formula with fixed rolls: hit (size, flank, guard, terrain, range); damage (strong and same element, Tide ±, terrain, guard, surround, crit); magic; healing; statuses (chance, duration, Sleep waking, Stop immunity); the Ward penalty. Also: spells illegal after moving; mobile specials legal after moving; Charge and Dive needing 2 hexes; Keep healing and the last-bell seizure; a ruler's retreat losing the battle; a fallen knight taking its troop and the capture chances; monsters dying for good; EXP and level-ups; every season's transforms (flood, ice, drying, fire → ash); the Sanctum's dials, hand and Timeless; hub glory |\n| `determinism` | the same seed and commands give the same hash, in battle and campaign; no `Math.random`, `Date.now` or `performance` in sims or AI |\n| `ai-battle` | the AI only issues legal commands; it wins clearly favourable fights at least 90% of 200 runs; rulers keep out of danger; attackers go for the Keep late; every map × season ends within 12 bells; an auto-resolved 3-against-3 battle takes under 150 ms |\n| `campaign` | the phases cycle; income, upkeep and desertion; summon limits and summon level; Bond limits; moving only to adjacent castles; quest outcome rates (10,000 rolls within ±2% of the weights) and modifiers; march rules (adjacency, 3 troops, once a season); resolution order; empty castles taken without a battle; aftermath (retreat paths, wounds, captures into reserves, treasuries); elimination; Stillness; the candle; every way to win or lose, a rival setting the Wheel included |\n| `ai-campaign` | 20 AI-only seeds per difficulty reach an end; no realm wins more than 45% of them; there is at least one battle every two seasons; the Dominion stays home in Year 1 |\n| `save` | serialize → load → equal hash (mid-Muster, with knights away, wounded and stilled castles); the `game.saves` slots; migration from a v1 fixture |\n| `story` | every event's speakers, conditions and effects are valid; every event fires from the dev trigger without errors; each realm's chain is reachable in a scripted campaign; all 4 good endings and the 3 kinds of bad ending are reachable; rival lines fire for their pairs |\n| `ui-flow` | input only (taps, holds, `feed` for the mouse): title → new campaign (each realm) → prologue → tutorial win → Muster (summon, bind, move, quest, equip, promote) → March → a commanded battle (select, move, attack, spell, wait, end) → results → Tidings; pause → save → load; How to Play and About open and close; ○ / Esc backs out of every panel; mouse hover focuses, a click confirms, a right click goes back |\n| `prompts` | a gamepad shows ✕ ○ □ △; with the Xbox setting, A B X Y; a keyboard shows key names; a mouse shows its buttons; prompts change on the step after the device does |\n| `attract` | 10 s idle on the title starts attract; a key, a mouse move, a pad button or a touch returns to the title within a step; a full 95 s loop runs with no errors and reaches every beat (`snapshot().attract.beat`) |\n| `touch` | with `G.forceTouchOnly`, the title shows the notice and its Settings button; no scene has touch buttons; attract still starts |\n| `dev` | the panel opens from the pause menu; spot checks of each tab's tools (god mode, win now, give an item, trigger an event, jump a season); a slider changes the outcome (`dmgScale` 2 doubles a fixed-roll hit); Reset restores the defaults; the DEV flag is set |\n| `audio` | every song's tokens parse; every scene and season has music; every sound id used is defined; `voice.plan` gives the same syllables for the same line; no audio files are referenced |\n| `localmp` | in hot-seat with 2 humans, input reaches only the active seat; privacy cards show; a human-against-human battle reads each seat; a 4-seat local Banners of the Wheel with CPUs finishes |\n| `hub-unit` | `NetDriver` against a fake `AIHub` in Node: host and client exchange messages; ordering; a gap → `need` → `snap`; illegal commands rejected; a deadline → AUTO; `leave`; `time-up` → `finish` standings; `end` stops input |\n| `playthrough` | for each realm, a new Normal campaign on autoplay: the player's realm uses the campaign and battle AIs through the same commands; battles are Delegated except the tutorial and one battle a year, which the bot fights through the battle scene with real inputs. `tune.aiPlayerBoost` may be raised to make the win reliable. It must reach `meridian_falls`, win the Sanctum and play the ending and credits with no errors. A fifth run lets the candle burn out (the defeat path) |\n| `bundle` (`--browser`) | build; the single HTML has no external URLs; the first script after `<meta charset>` is the unmodified session client; the hub tags are present; it opens from `file://` in headless Chromium (`engine/tools/check.mjs`) with no errors; boot → title; attract starts after 10 s |\n| `hub` (`--browser`) | the harness procedure in §14.6 |\n| `about` | the About pages carry every Source Information field and the three feedback lists; `exit-interview.json` parses and every key has a value (run at the end) |\n\n### 14.3 Bots\n- **Battle bot:** drives the battle scene through `game.input`. It moves the cursor with taps, then confirms, using the\n  battle AI's chosen command, so it tests the real UI path.\n- **Campaign bot:** works the Muster panels through input for at least one season per realm, then switches to sim-level\n  autoplay for speed.\n\n### 14.4 Looking (only what a script can't check)\n- **Screenshots:** `node engine/tools/check.mjs dist/index.html#<link> --size 1920x1080` (and `1280x720`) of the title,\n  the campaign in each season, the castle card and the Organize and Summon panels, a battle in each season (River Ford),\n  the Sanctum, a story stage, results, and About. Act on every look note.\n- **Filmstrips:** `engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1` of every class move, each beast kind's walk, bite and breath, a\n  summon, a capture and a promotion.\n- **The gallery:** every species in all 3 forms.\n\n### 14.5 Balance runs (`tools/simulate.mjs`)\n- **Commands:** `--campaigns 50 --difficulty normal`; `--battles 500 --map river_ford`; `--hub 200`. Each prints summary\n  tables.\n- **Targets:**\n  - AI-only campaigns: no realm wins more than 40%; they end in seasons 12–16 on average;\n  - the player's realm on autoplay (Normal) reaches Meridian between seasons 10 and 14 in at least 60% of seeds;\n  - early battles average 8 bells or fewer;\n  - hub seats each win 20–30% of the time.\n\n### 14.6 The AI Hub harness\n1. Copy `vendor/hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` and the built game HTML into `dist/hub/`.\n2. Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (with `TMPDIR` set) and note its PID and port.\n3. Fetch `/<game>.html` and check its `<title>` is ours.\n4. Run `tools/hub-check.mjs` (Playwright) on each of these:\n   - `harness.html?game=<game>.html&players=2&auto=1`\n   - `harness.html?game=<game>.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n   - `harness.html?game=<game>.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\n   - `harness.html?game=<game>.html&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n\n   Each must end with `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` and `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`.\n5. Open the game outside a session and check it still runs normally.\n6. Stop the server by its PID.\n\n### 14.7 When to rerun\nAfter a change, rerun only the suites that cover the changed files:\n\n| Changed | Rerun |\n|---|---|\n| `20–21` | `rules`, `determinism`, `ai-battle` |\n| `22–24` | `campaign`, `ai-campaign`, `save` |\n| `0x` data | `data`, plus the suites that use it |\n| `09` | `story` |\n| `3x` art | the `ui-flow` smoke run, and look checks on demand |\n| `4x` | `audio` |\n| `5x–6x` | `ui-flow`, `prompts`, `attract`, `touch` |\n| `70` | `dev` |\n| `80–81` | `hub-unit`, `localmp`, `hub` |\n\nRun everything at each milestone's exit and at the end.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Done: the checklist\n- [ ] Every system in §4–§11 works, with no TODO, FIXME, placeholder or stub (the build guard and the `data` suite).\n- [ ] All the content in §6 is in the game (the counts in the `data` suite).\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs --browser` passes. All five playthroughs pass, and the harness passes all four scenarios.\n- [ ] The single file sits in this folder's root under the exact name in §0. It opens from `file://`; its first script\n      is the unmodified hub client; the hub tags are present.\n- [ ] About & Credits is complete. The final chat reply carries the same Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine\n      Feedback and Prompt Feedback, with \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed.\n- [ ] `exit-interview.json` sits beside the HTML, in exactly TASK.md's shape, with every value filled in, and it\n      parses. Suggested `aiHub` values:\n  - name \"Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons\"; tagline \"Four seasons. Four crowns. One stopped clock.\";\n  - description \"A seasonal war of monster-binding knights: muster castles, summon beasts and fight twelve-bell hex\n    battles to restart the Wheel of Seasons before time stops forever.\";\n  - type \"Game\"; genre \"Strategy\"; source \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena\"; series \"Brigandine\"; players \"1–4\";\n  - controls \"Stick/WASD: cursor · ✕/Enter: select · ○/Esc: back · □/Space: commands · △/I: info · L1/R1 or Tab:\n    cycle\";\n  - tags `[\"fantasy\", \"story\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"retro\", \"boss fights\"]`.\n- [ ] ENGINE-CHANGES.md is complete.\n- [ ] Every server you started is stopped, by PID. This folder gains only the dev folder, the HTML and\n      `exit-interview.json`.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: Tunables (`G.TUNE_DEFAULTS`; each is a dev-mode slider)\n\n| key | Default | Slider range | Used by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| dmgScale | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | physical damage |\n| defFactor | 0.5 | 0–1 | physical damage |\n| magicScale | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | magic damage |\n| healScale | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | healing |\n| baseHit | 85 | 50–100 | hit chance |\n| largeVsSmall | −30 | −60–0 | the size table (L against S) |\n| critBase | 3 | 0–30 | crit chance |\n| wardPenalty | 0.20 | 0–0.6 | monsters outside their Ward |\n| surroundBonus | 0.10 | 0–0.3 | damage per adjacent ally |\n| elemStrong | 1.30 | 1–2 | opposed elements |\n| elemSame | 0.80 | 0.5–1 | matching elements |\n| tideBonus | 0.15 | 0–0.5 | the Seasonal Tide |\n| forestDef | 0.20 | 0–0.5 | forest DEF |\n| statusScale | 1.0 | 0–2 | status chances |\n| captureBase | 0.25 | 0–1 | capture chance |\n| expScale | 1.0 | 0–5 | EXP |\n| bells | 12 | 4–20 | battle length |\n| manaIncome | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | castle yields |\n| summonCost | 1.0 | 0.25–3 | summon costs |\n| upkeepScale | 1.0 | 0–3 | upkeep |\n| seasonYield | 0.25 | 0–1 | the in-season yield bonus |\n| winterUpkeep | 0.25 | 0–1 | wintering |\n| questLuck | 1.0 | 0–2 | good quest outcome weights |\n| aiAggression | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | campaign AI (multiplies personality) |\n| aiManaBonus | 0 | −0.5–1 | AI income, on top of difficulty |\n| aiPlayerBoost | 0 | 0–1 | playthrough tests only: the player's units' stats × (1 + x) |\n| candleSeasons | 12 (by difficulty) | 4–30 | the Hour-Candle |\n| animSpeed | 1.0 | 0.25–4 | presentation speed |\n| hubTurnSeconds | 15 | 5–60 | hub troop timer (sessions always use the default) |\n\n## Appendix B: Research done while planning (for the \"Research\" field)\n- **Wikipedia, \"Brigandine (video game)\"** (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)):\n  - monthly Organize and Attack phases; mana income and upkeep; quests; Rune Power;\n  - up to three troops a side; the attacker's 12-turn limit; the leader and ruler retreat rules; the Rune Area;\n  - permanent monster death; the five colour elements; no spells after moving;\n  - the Grand Edition's 6-player multiplayer, final boss and hold-the-castle rule.\n- **RPGFan's review** (https://www.rpgfan.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena):\n  - the rulers' archetypes (the silent wise king, the prince, the queen, the war-loving king, the mad duke);\n  - brief dialogue between turns; the Risk-like map;\n  - big monsters struggling against small ones; formations; quest rewards.\n- **Read during planning:**\n  - my-3D2dge handoff v0.85.2: README, API.md, the relevant AI_GUIDE.md sections, the grid, story, arcade, strategy,\n    songs and rpg module headers, the TACTICS kit, docs/ASSETS.md and the asset catalogs;\n  - AI Hub `lib/hub`: README, retrofit.md and the examples.\n","numLines":440,"startLine":1978,"totalLines":2417}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QH4yXeHAa1qxBQPbR78KbD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
