{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VXLEnKqLennQDaZUboHqgU","type":"tool_result","content":"96:- 1430 Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js); E.Fog: fog, E.Grid: grid, E.GridMover: gridmover, E.Turns: turns\n163:- `E.hex(h)`: '#rrggbb' or '#rgb' (or an [r, g, b] array) -> [r, g, b]\n210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n735:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n736:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].roof })`: the top's material: 'speckle' (default) | 'plain' | 'tiles' (roof shingles) | 'slab' (paving) | 'leaves' | 'grass' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n780:- `map.floorMat` †: a material (E.MATERIALS id or '#hex pattern') for every floor cell\n796:- `E.MATERIALS: brick, stone, rock, plank, timber, plaster, hedge, speckle, plain, tiles, slab, leaves, grass, flagstone, ... (61)`: the materials by id: { color, pattern, ...its numbers, ramp, glow } or a painter of a surface (face, roof, floor, tile); add your own: E.MATERIALS.oak = { color: '#8a5a36', pattern: 'planks', bw: 3 }. Any material id takes '#hex pattern key=value' too\n838:- `E.tex.flagstone(x, y, pal, size = 16)`: stone flagstones with running-bond rows. pal: {stones:[hex..], mortar, hi, lo, speck}\n839:- `E.tex.grass(x, y, o = {})`: grass with darker tufts and a few flowers. o: { base, dark, light, flower } hex colors\n1430:## Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js)\n1439:- `new E.Grid(w, h, o = {}) → grid`: new E.Grid(w, h, { hex: false | 'pointy' | 'flat', walkable(cx, cy), cost(cx, cy), height(cx, cy), opaque(cx, cy), diagonal }): w x h cells, every one walkable at cost 1 and height 0 unless the functions say otherwise\n1441:- `grid.center(c, T = 16)`: a cell's centre in world units, T a cell across (square: T wide; hex: T across its flats)\n1443:- `grid.dist(a, b)`: steps from a to b: Manhattan, Chebyshev (diagonal) or hex steps\n1446:- `grid.fov(c, radius = 8)`: what c sees within radius: a Set of 'cx,cy' (symmetric shadowcasting, Albert Ford's: a sees b exactly when b sees a; walls at the edge of what it sees are in it; hex grids: a line to each cell)\n1449:- `grid.inside(c)`: is [cx, cy] on the grid?\n1450:- `grid.line(a, b)`: the cells on a line from a to b, both ends included (Bresenham; hex: one step at a time)\n1451:- `grid.neighbours(c)`: the cells next to c on the grid: 4, 8 (diagonal) or 6 (hex), walkable or not\n1453:- `grid.path(a, b, o = {})`: the cheapest way from a to b, [a, ..., b], or [] (A*; ties broken the same way every time). o: { blocked(cx, cy): cells taken (other units), climb, drop (the most a step rises and falls), ends: b may be unwalkable (a target), max: give up past this cost }\n1454:- `grid.reach(a, budget, o = {})`: every cell within budget of a: { cells: [[cx, cy, cost]], has(c), cost(c) (or Infinity), path(c) } (Dijkstra: move ranges). o: { blocked, climb, drop } as path's, and pass(cx, cy): cells it may cross but not stop on (allies)\n1456:- `grid.shape(c, kind = 'diamond', n = 1, dir = [1, 0])`: the cells a shape of effect covers round c (square grids; on the grid only): 'cross' (n each way), 'diamond' (n steps: dist), 'square' (n each way, corners too), 'ring' (exactly n steps), 'line' (n cells from c along dir [dx, dy], not c), 'cone' (n rows along dir, each a cell wider each side)\n1458:- `grid.threat(units, o = {})`: what a side can strike on its next turn: units ([{ cx, cy, move, range: [min, max] or n (1), climb, drop }]) each moving within its reach (o.blocked: cells it can't enter) and striking within range of where it stops. { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) -> [units] }: a threat map, for an AI's safe cells and a player's warning tint\n1459:- `grid.toCell(x, y, T = 16)`: the cell under world point (x, y), T a cell across (center's inverse)\n1460:- `grid.walk(c)`: can [cx, cy] be walked (on the grid, and walkable)?\n1463:- `grid.hex`: false, 'pointy' (offset rows) or 'flat' (offset columns)\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"d1f43c80-dd32-4132-a2d6-53bdbda126fd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:00.256Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"96:- 1430 Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js); E.Fog: fog, E.Grid: grid, E.GridMover: gridmover, E.Turns: turns\n163:- `E.hex(h)`: '#rrggbb' or '#rgb' (or an [r, g, b] array) -> [r, g, b]\n210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n735:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n736:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].roof })`: the top's material: 'speckle' (default) | 'plain' | 'tiles' (roof shingles) | 'slab' (paving) | 'leaves' | 'grass' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n780:- `map.floorMat` †: a material (E.MATERIALS id or '#hex pattern') for every floor cell\n796:- `E.MATERIALS: brick, stone, rock, plank, timber, plaster, hedge, speckle, plain, tiles, slab, leaves, grass, flagstone, ... (61)`: the materials by id: { color, pattern, ...its numbers, ramp, glow } or a painter of a surface (face, roof, floor, tile); add your own: E.MATERIALS.oak = { color: '#8a5a36', pattern: 'planks', bw: 3 }. Any material id takes '#hex pattern key=value' too\n838:- `E.tex.flagstone(x, y, pal, size = 16)`: stone flagstones with running-bond rows. pal: {stones:[hex..], mortar, hi, lo, speck}\n839:- `E.tex.grass(x, y, o = {})`: grass with darker tufts and a few flowers. o: { base, dark, light, flower } hex colors\n1430:## Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js)\n1439:- `new E.Grid(w, h, o = {}) → grid`: new E.Grid(w, h, { hex: false | 'pointy' | 'flat', walkable(cx, cy), cost(cx, cy), height(cx, cy), opaque(cx, cy), diagonal }): w x h cells, every one walkable at cost 1 and height 0 unless the functions say otherwise\n1441:- `grid.center(c, T = 16)`: a cell's centre in world units, T a cell across (square: T wide; hex: T across its flats)\n1443:- `grid.dist(a, b)`: steps from a to b: Manhattan, Chebyshev (diagonal) or hex steps\n1446:- `grid.fov(c, radius = 8)`: what c sees within radius: a Set of 'cx,cy' (symmetric shadowcasting, Albert Ford's: a sees b exactly when b sees a; walls at the edge of what it sees are in it; hex grids: a line to each cell)\n1449:- `grid.inside(c)`: is [cx, cy] on the grid?\n1450:- `grid.line(a, b)`: the cells on a line from a to b, both ends included (Bresenham; hex: one step at a time)\n1451:- `grid.neighbours(c)`: the cells next to c on the grid: 4, 8 (diagonal) or 6 (hex), walkable or not\n1453:- `grid.path(a, b, o = {})`: the cheapest way from a to b, [a, ..., b], or [] (A*; ties broken the same way every time). o: { blocked(cx, cy): cells taken (other units), climb, drop (the most a step rises and falls), ends: b may be unwalkable (a target), max: give up past this cost }\n1454:- `grid.reach(a, budget, o = {})`: every cell within budget of a: { cells: [[cx, cy, cost]], has(c), cost(c) (or Infinity), path(c) } (Dijkstra: move ranges). o: { blocked, climb, drop } as path's, and pass(cx, cy): cells it may cross but not stop on (allies)\n1456:- `grid.shape(c, kind = 'diamond', n = 1, dir = [1, 0])`: the cells a shape of effect covers round c (square grids; on the grid only): 'cross' (n each way), 'diamond' (n steps: dist), 'square' (n each way, corners too), 'ring' (exactly n steps), 'line' (n cells from c along dir [dx, dy], not c), 'cone' (n rows along dir, each a cell wider each side)\n1458:- `grid.threat(units, o = {})`: what a side can strike on its next turn: units ([{ cx, cy, move, range: [min, max] or n (1), climb, drop }]) each moving within its reach (o.blocked: cells it can't enter) and striking within range of where it stops. { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) -> [units] }: a threat map, for an AI's safe cells and a player's warning tint\n1459:- `grid.toCell(x, y, T = 16)`: the cell under world point (x, y), T a cell across (center's inverse)\n1460:- `grid.walk(c)`: can [cx, cy] be walked (on the grid, and walkable)?\n1463:- `grid.hex`: false, 'pointy' (offset rows) or 'flat' (offset columns)\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VXLEnKqLennQDaZUboHqgU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
