{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CvuQapvn7o1WzfBThavie9","type":"tool_result","content":"1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"1a03b58f-3244-4124-8d37-94e4d8c96201","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:04.830Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CvuQapvn7o1WzfBThavie9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghrbmvd9oHoimX8xAyQf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019NVosDSZavtyynSMH6xfP7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/Brig*/engine; grep -n \"^- \\`game\\.audio\\.\\|^- \\`game\\.saves\\|^- \\`game\\.settings\\|^- \\`game\\.menu\\|^- \\`new E.Story\\|^- \\`story\\.\\|^- \\`game\\.debug\\|^- \\`input\\.\\(feed\\|tap\\|hold\\|clicked\\|pointer\\|wheel\\|anyPressed\\|idle\\)\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-230 | head -90","description":"List audio, saves, settings, story, input APIs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":206656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"05bbcb27-96f0-44cf-8f36-d56071fd595f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:08.720Z","request_id":"req_011CghrbmZYH79QEViZStKYW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019NVosDSZavtyynSMH6xfP7":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/Brig*/engine; grep -n \"^- \\`game\\.audio\\.\\|^- \\`game\\.saves\\|^- \\`game\\.settings\\|^- \\`game\\.menu\\|^- \\`new E.Story\\|^- \\`story\\.\\|^- \\`game\\.debug\\|^- \\`input\\.\\(feed\\|tap\\|hold\\|clicked\\|pointer\\|wheel\\|anyPressed\\|idle\\)\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-230 | head -90","description":"List audio, saves, settings, story, input APIs"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019NVosDSZavtyynSMH6xfP7","type":"tool_result","content":"276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menu\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse a\n291:- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n314:- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu(\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n519:- `game.debug = null`: a game's own handle for tools and tests: game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }. tools/check.mjs prints snapshot() and tools/replay.mjs logs it at the end\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n1051:- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n1052:- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n1053:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 t\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1055:- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle'\n1058:- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n1059:- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n1060:- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, \n1061:- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n1062:- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03)\n1064:- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n1065:- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n1066:- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n1067:- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n1069:- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n1070:- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n1071:- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n1072:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n1073:- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n1074:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1076:- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n1077:- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n1648:- `new E.Story(game, o = {}) → story`: new E.Story(game, { people, nodes, vars, on, dialog }): the talk of a game (the manual above)\n1649:- `story.done(id)`: finish a quest (taken now if it wasn't)\n1650:- `story.draw(r)`: draw the balloons over their targets and the box (anywhere in draw: both go to the overlay)\n1651:- `story.emote(target, kind = '!', seconds = 1.5)`: a balloon over target (x, y, z; h: its height) for seconds: '!', '?', 'heart', 'dots', 'note'\n1652:- `story.get(key)`: a flag or value (key may be a dotted path into vars)\n1653:- `story.quest(id, title = id, text = '')`: take a quest (or change its title and text): it joins the log\n1654:- `story.restore(s)`: put back what state() gave (a load)\n1655:- `story.resume()`: after an event with wait: true, go on (to the choice's goto, or the next step)\n1656:- `story.run(id, o = {})`: start node id (stopping any other); o.onDone(story) when it ends\n1657:- `story.set(key, value = true)`: set a flag (value true) or a value\n1658:- `story.state()`: its vars and quests, as JSON (for a save)\n1659:- `story.stop()`: stop the node running (its box closes; onDone isn't called)\n1660:- `story.test(c)`: does a condition hold? (the manual's conditions)\n1661:- `story.update(dt)`: run the talk and the balloons; true while a node runs (play waits)\n1662:- `story.auto = 0`: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself (0: it waits for the player)\n1663:- `story.game`: its game\n1664:- `story.log = []`: what was said and chosen, oldest first ({ who, name, text }, the last 200: a visual novel's backlog)\n1665:- `story.node = null`: its id\n1666:- `story.nodes`: the conversations by id (lists of steps)\n1667:- `story.on`: the game's event handlers by name\n1668:- `story.people`: who speaks, by id ({ name, portrait, at })\n1669:- `story.quests = []`: the quest log, in the order taken ({ id, title, text, done })\n1670:- `story.running = false`: a node runs\n1671:- `story.skip = false`: pages type at once and turn at once (choices still wait)\n1672:- `story.talk`: the E.Dialog it speaks through\n1673:- `story.vars`: every flag and value (a line's {$name} reads them)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"361f6a97-5e1c-4bcd-8f0f-1db1e196e11b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:08.736Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menu\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse a\n291:- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n314:- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu(\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n519:- `game.debug = null`: a game's own handle for tools and tests: game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }. tools/check.mjs prints snapshot() and tools/replay.mjs logs it at the end\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n1051:- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n1052:- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n1053:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 t\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1055:- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle'\n1058:- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n1059:- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n1060:- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, \n1061:- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n1062:- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03)\n1064:- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n1065:- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n1066:- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n1067:- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n1069:- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n1070:- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n1071:- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n1072:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n1073:- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n1074:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1076:- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n1077:- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n1648:- `new E.Story(game, o = {}) → story`: new E.Story(game, { people, nodes, vars, on, dialog }): the talk of a game (the manual above)\n1649:- `story.done(id)`: finish a quest (taken now if it wasn't)\n1650:- `story.draw(r)`: draw the balloons over their targets and the box (anywhere in draw: both go to the overlay)\n1651:- `story.emote(target, kind = '!', seconds = 1.5)`: a balloon over target (x, y, z; h: its height) for seconds: '!', '?', 'heart', 'dots', 'note'\n1652:- `story.get(key)`: a flag or value (key may be a dotted path into vars)\n1653:- `story.quest(id, title = id, text = '')`: take a quest (or change its title and text): it joins the log\n1654:- `story.restore(s)`: put back what state() gave (a load)\n1655:- `story.resume()`: after an event with wait: true, go on (to the choice's goto, or the next step)\n1656:- `story.run(id, o = {})`: start node id (stopping any other); o.onDone(story) when it ends\n1657:- `story.set(key, value = true)`: set a flag (value true) or a value\n1658:- `story.state()`: its vars and quests, as JSON (for a save)\n1659:- `story.stop()`: stop the node running (its box closes; onDone isn't called)\n1660:- `story.test(c)`: does a condition hold? (the manual's conditions)\n1661:- `story.update(dt)`: run the talk and the balloons; true while a node runs (play waits)\n1662:- `story.auto = 0`: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself (0: it waits for the player)\n1663:- `story.game`: its game\n1664:- `story.log = []`: what was said and chosen, oldest first ({ who, name, text }, the last 200: a visual novel's backlog)\n1665:- `story.node = null`: its id\n1666:- `story.nodes`: the conversations by id (lists of steps)\n1667:- `story.on`: the game's event handlers by name\n1668:- `story.people`: who speaks, by id ({ name, portrait, at })\n1669:- `story.quests = []`: the quest log, in the order taken ({ id, title, text, done })\n1670:- `story.running = false`: a node runs\n1671:- `story.skip = false`: pages type at once and turn at once (choices still wait)\n1672:- `story.talk`: the E.Dialog it speaks through\n1673:- `story.vars`: every flag and value (a line's {$name} reads them)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019NVosDSZavtyynSMH6xfP7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
