{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrdVkLWbYoVNVk6qubK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013mCYZfKJqHQQ9BHoWcXXLK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/Brig*/engine; grep -n \"Mouse1\\|WheelUp\\|'Wheel\\|PadAxis\" API-INDEX.md | head -8; grep -n \"^- \\`game.saves\\.\\|^- \\`saves\\.\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-250 | head -20; grep -n \"idle\\b\\|idleTime\\|lastInput\" API-INDEX.md | head","description":"Look up input codes, saves, idle APIs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2488,"cache_read_input_tokens":214501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2488},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"8e8408ee-113b-4663-b102-12798b9adbf3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:47.661Z","request_id":"req_011CghrdVVxiY5y1zpYsHTB3","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013mCYZfKJqHQQ9BHoWcXXLK":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050223__x7910ab/work/Brig*/engine; grep -n \"Mouse1\\|WheelUp\\|'Wheel\\|PadAxis\" API-INDEX.md | head -8; grep -n \"^- \\`game.saves\\.\\|^- \\`saves\\.\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-250 | head -20; grep -n \"idle\\b\\|idleTime\\|lastInput\" API-INDEX.md | head","description":"Look up input codes, saves, idle APIs"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013mCYZfKJqHQQ9BHoWcXXLK","type":"tool_result","content":"618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n645:- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n646:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n650:- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n660:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n662:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n700:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"0c9f2073-99c5-4081-b53e-6b8d2cb276d9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:47.687Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n645:- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n646:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n650:- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n660:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n662:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n700:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013mCYZfKJqHQQ9BHoWcXXLK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
