{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W9psTn5tnVsLmXAXsnFBpp","type":"tool_result","content":"190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n199:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n200:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n201:- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n202:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n204:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n205:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n206:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n207:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n224:- `view.depth(x, y, z = 0)`: true camera depth: use it to sort parts inside one object\n226:- `view.p(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> projected screen pixels (not yet camera-relative)\n239:- `view.pitch`, `view.yaw`: the same angles in radians\n240:- `view.pitchDeg`: the tilt, 0 side view to 90 straight down\n241:- `view.scale`: screen pixels per world unit\n242:- `view.yawDeg`: the turn about the up axis, degrees (0: north is up the screen; iso is 45)\n578:  p(x, y, z = 0) { return [this.ax * x + this.ay * y, this.bx * x + this.by * y + this.bz * z]; }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"e6a86fbe-326f-469a-98c1-b4246427db61","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:19:48.247Z","