{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: Not satisfied. The single .html is present in the folder root and exit-interview.json parses with all fields filled. The final reply has all four sections. But 'every feature in TASK.md is implemented' is not established: the transcript shows the game was changed to meet a plan that TASK.md overrides where they differ, and the final reply admits the Gray Knight stats and balance values were changed after the plan. Also, the Testing counts (21 issues, 6 critical) and the Usage figure are self-reported estimates not evidenced in the transcript, and the mouse and touch checks rest on single ad hoc runs. The condition's wording (every feature implemented, no stubs) is only partly shown, so it is not clearly met."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"7b015dee-9c14-4140-ae12-199d87061fb1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:20:14.251Z","isSynthetic":true}
