{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghyTbqF6P2fSV18XHG5y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You were right to push on balance: the war could not be won without the test-only stat boost, even on Easy. Autoplay without the boost had won 0 of 15 Easy campaigns per realm. That is fixed: unboosted autoplay now wins 11 of 20 Easy campaigns, and `node tests/run.mjs --browser` passes 99 of 99 after the fixes.\n\n**What was wrong**\n- **The player's realm stalled.** It stopped attacking for six or more seasons, gained no levels, and let mana pile up until the candle ran out.\n- **Bug: the Dominion fought its own Gray Knight.** When the Dominion retook Meridian it was treated as a rival realm. That could end the game with a false loss.\n- **The Sanctum battle was skipped** when fewer than two knights survived taking Meridian. The Dominion then retook the city before the battle happened.\n- **A plan rule was missing:** the Sanctum's \"plus one more troop from a castle next to Meridian\" reinforcement.\n\n**What I changed**\n- **Autoplay planner:**\n  - It now gathers its troops in the castles next to Meridian.\n  - It gets bolder after idle seasons, and after two idle seasons it may leave a border castle empty to attack.\n  - This planner is the one the attract reel, the playthrough tests and dev-mode autoplay use. The rival realms' AI is unchanged.\n- **New dev slider, \"Player drill EXP\" (default 30):** each season, the player's garrisoned knights and their monsters gain experience, so a stalled war still progresses.\n- **The Gray Knight now scales with difficulty:** ×0.75 on Easy, ×1.1 on Hard.\n- **Dominion garrisons outside Meridian are one to two levels lower.**\n- **Four new tests** each win an Easy campaign with no boost, one per realm. The four boosted runs through the real scenes and the candle-defeat run still pass.\n\n**Win rates now (no boost, every battle auto-resolved)**\n\n| Difficulty | Wins | Before this round |\n|---|---|---|\n| Easy | 11 of 20 (Verdance 4/5, Solmark 2/5, Amberlyn 3/5, Hoarfast 2/5) | 0 |\n| Normal | 2 of 20 | — |\n| Hard | 0 of 16 | — |\n\nThe AI auto-resolves every battle, so these are worst-case figures. Normal and Hard should be winnable by commanding battles yourself, but nothing measures that: no bot fights battles by hand.\n\nAll TASK.md features are in place and tested one requirement each in `tests/t-task.mjs`. The single `.html` is in the folder root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:23\n- **Source:** Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin / Atlus, PlayStation, 1998)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** turn-based grand strategy with a tactical RPG battle layer. The campaign uses a three-quarter overhead world map. Battles use a tilted overhead hex board (a custom 50° view that rotates, with an isometric alternative). Story scenes are side-on stages.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full build), plain JavaScript in one IIFE, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0, Node 24 for the build and tests; no other libraries.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native PS1-style pixel look. It uses the engine's character and blob rigs, a new procedural beast rig, hex terrain baked per season, and custom castle and clock-tower shapes.\n- **Animation:** the engine's skeletal moves and poses and blob squash-and-stretch, plus new procedural beast animation, particles, lights and weather.\n- **Audio:** all in code: step-sequencer songs, stings, synthesized sound effects and Animalese-style babble voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world mode for 2–4 players, \"Banners of the Wheel\", with the host's copy authoritative. Local hot-seat supports 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 10 headless Node suites and 7 browser checks behind one command, plus the AI Hub harness (all 4 scenarios passed).\n- **Research:** none during the build; the plan records its own.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** session time from the system clock, 1 h 30 min (05:02:23 to 06:32:45); API cost and token counts unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 25, each fixed:\n   - the campaign AI never marched;\n   - the Dominion snowballed across the map;\n   - autoplay never pushed toward Meridian;\n   - the Sanctum was unwinnable at realistic levels;\n   - experience came far too slowly;\n   - beaten brigand captains stayed on the map;\n   - a duplicate top-level name broke the bundle;\n   - a story event crashed when its flag was unset;\n   - the tutorial battle was queued after the Muster;\n   - dev tools read stale state instead of the live scene;\n   - Owain joined too early;\n   - dev mode was blocked during a battle dialog;\n   - the online client that isn't the host sent no messages;\n   - deep links were dropped;\n   - characters missing from the font showed as \"?\";\n   - the Sanctum deep link put the wrong sides on the field;\n   - the Summon prompt mangled its cost;\n   - the Gray Knight looked like a red-haired man;\n   - the camera chased the mouse;\n   - without the boost the player never won;\n   - the Dominion fought its own Gray Knight;\n   - the Sanctum was skipped when few knights survived;\n   - the Sanctum reinforcement rule was missing;\n   - two mistakes in my own test scripts.\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 8:\n   - the duplicate name (the game would not load);\n   - the AI never marching;\n   - the unwinnable Sanctum;\n   - the war being unwinnable without a boost;\n   - the Dominion fighting itself (it could end the game with a false loss);\n   - the tutorial running out of order;\n   - the silent online client;\n   - the camera chasing the mouse.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The autoplay campaign run. In its no-boost form it found this round's balance problems and the Dominion bug.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** Testing the dialog box outside the game loop: it couldn't see key presses, so it only exposed my harness.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The deterministic headless clock and the debug handle. The character rigs, pause menu, settings and save slots came free.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - scenes are wrapped, so the registered object isn't the live scene;\n   - timers set before the first scene starts are cleared;\n   - the font has gaps that show as \"?\";\n   - camera-follow combined with mouse hover made the board slide under the pointer.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The hex battlefield and the beast rig.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Fitting hex tactics onto a square-tile renderer.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?** A per-letter voice callback in the dialog box, so babble follows the text, and a new module, `engine-ext/beasts.js`, for creature bodies the engine lacked.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** First-class hex maps, plus a documented list of the font's glyphs.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** The precise deliverables, the freedom to change the engine, and the clear testing rules.\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan was written for another run and assumed far more scope. The multiplayer wording about \"the game on its own\" was ambiguous.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope, and tuning the campaign so it is winnable without help.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark plan items as required or stretch, give a scope budget, and have the plan take its run-specific names from TASK.md instead of hard-coding them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":763014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":617},"output_tokens":792,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"475aab25-54c0-455a-adbc-9e888f038b29","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:34:25.189Z","request_id":"req_011CghyTbUQXPppZ4DT4Lk1z"}
