{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghyofPNYT7nu8tCUkSBu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing has changed since the last pass, and the evidence for each point the check raises is already in this session.\n\n- **Deliverables:** the single `.html` is in the folder root. `exit-interview.json` parses and every field is filled; the about suite checks that.\n- **TASK.md requirements:** each has its own test in `tests/t-task.mjs`, all 15 passing. The output earlier shows what each one exercised in the running game:\n  - the file name and the inlined engine;\n  - audio written entirely in code;\n  - all 127 unit visuals animating;\n  - a full campaign won through the real scenes;\n  - dev mode reached from the pause menu, with live sliders and Reset;\n  - attract mode starting after 10 s idle;\n  - hub tags and hot-seat play;\n  - PlayStation, Xbox, keyboard and mouse prompts;\n  - mouse clicks on menus;\n  - the touch-only notice;\n  - all 13 settings in use;\n  - no TODO or stub markers;\n  - the About and Credits pages.\n- **Separate browser checks:**\n  - **Mouse:** hovering moves the cursor, and clicking a unit opens its commands.\n  - **Phone:** an emulated phone shows the touch-only notice.\n  - **AI Hub harness:** passed all 4 scenarios.\n- **Full run:** `node tests/run.mjs --browser` passed 99 of 99.\n- **Balance:** TASK.md sets no stat values and says \"Balance is key\". The Sanctum, the Gray Knight, the Season Dials and the candle are all implemented. I tuned their numbers until the war can be won without the test boost. Win rates come from an autoplay bot that auto-resolves every battle, 20 campaigns per difficulty:\n\n  | Difficulty | Wins | Losses |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | Easy | 12 | 8 |\n  | Normal | 6 | 14 |\n  | Hard | 0 | 20 |\n\n  Four tests each win an Easy campaign without the boost, one per realm.\n- **Counts:** the 25 issues and 8 critical ones are the bugs listed below; each was found and fixed in this session.\n- **Usage:** session time comes from the system clock. The API reports no cost or token counts to me, so those are \"unknown\", as TASK.md allows.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:23\n- **Source:** Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin / Atlus, PlayStation, 1998)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** turn-based grand strategy with a tactical RPG battle layer. Campaign on a three-quarter overhead world map; battles on a tilted overhead hex board (a custom 50° view, rotatable, with isometric as an alternative); story on side-on stages.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full build), plain JavaScript in one IIFE, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0, Node 24 for build and tests; no other libraries.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native PS1-style pixel look, using its character and blob rigs plus a new procedural beast rig; hex terrain baked per season; custom castle and clock-tower shapes.\n- **Animation:** the engine's skeletal moves and poses, blob squash and stretch, new procedural beast animation, particles, lights and weather.\n- **Audio:** all in code: step-sequencer songs, stings, synthesized sound effects and Animalese-style babble voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world mode for 2–4 players, \"Banners of the Wheel\", with the host's copy as the authority; local hot-seat for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 10 headless Node suites and 7 browser checks behind one command, plus the AI Hub harness (4 of 4 scenarios passed).\n- **Research:** none during the build; the plan records its own.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** session time by system clock 1 h 35 min (05:02:23 to 06:37:48); API cost and token counts unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 25, each fixed:\n   - the AI never marched;\n   - the Dominion snowballed;\n   - autoplay never pushed for Meridian;\n   - the Sanctum was unwinnable;\n   - EXP was far too slow;\n   - beaten brigand captains lingered;\n   - a duplicate top-level name broke the bundle;\n   - a story event crashed when its flag was unset;\n   - the tutorial was queued after the Muster;\n   - dev tools read stale scene state;\n   - Owain joined too early;\n   - dev mode was blocked during a battle dialog;\n   - the online client sent nothing;\n   - deep links were dropped;\n   - missing font characters showed as \"?\";\n   - the Sanctum deep link fielded the wrong sides;\n   - the Summon prompt showed a garbled cost;\n   - the Gray Knight looked like a red-haired man;\n   - the camera chased the mouse;\n   - the war couldn't be won without the boost;\n   - the Dominion fought its own Gray Knight;\n   - the Sanctum was skipped when few knights survived;\n   - the Sanctum reinforcement rule was missing;\n   - two mistakes in my own test scripts.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 8:\n   - the duplicate name (the game would not load);\n   - the AI never marching;\n   - the unwinnable Sanctum;\n   - no win without the boost;\n   - the Dominion fighting itself (a possible false loss);\n   - the tutorial running out of order;\n   - the silent online client;\n   - the camera chasing the mouse.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The autoplay campaign, especially without the boost.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** Testing the dialog box outside the game loop.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The deterministic headless clock and the debug handle; the character rigs, pause menu, settings and saves came free.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - scenes are wrapped, so the registered object isn't the live scene;\n   - timers set before the first scene starts are cleared;\n   - the font has gaps that show as \"?\";\n   - the camera following the cursor made the board slide under the mouse.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The hex battlefield and the beast rig.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Fitting hex tactics onto a square-tile renderer.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?** A per-letter voice callback in the dialog box, so babble follows the text, and a new module, `engine-ext/beasts.js`, for creature bodies the engine lacked.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** First-class hex maps, plus a documented list of the font's glyphs.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** The precise deliverables, the freedom to change the engine, and the clear testing rules.\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan was written for another run and assumed far more scope, and the wording \"as well as for the game on its own\" was ambiguous.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope, and balancing the campaign so it can be won without help.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark plan items as required or stretch, give a scope budget, and have the plan take its run-specific names from TASK.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2947,"cache_read_input_tokens":770012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2947},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"75754595-6b74-4e7d-8874-586877f7f75f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:38:55.116Z","request_id":"req_011Cghyof4mvhMdS8i5K74t7"}
