 › battleView: Board or Isometric picks the battle camera\nok   settings › grid: Off, Subtle and Bold darken the hex edges by different amounts\nok   settings › tips: On shows tutorial tips, Off does not\nok   settings › textSpeed: Slow, Normal, Fast and Instant type at different speeds\nok   settings › voices: On babbles through the effects bus, Off is silent\nok   settings › uiScale: Large doubles list text and shows fewer rows\nok   settings › edgePan: On pans the map when the mouse rests at the screen edge, Off does not\nok   settings › aiBattles: Show result adds a report card for a battle between AI realms, Skip does not\nok   settings › confirmEnd: On asks before ending a troop turn, Off ends at once\nok   settings › hotseatTimer: 30 s delegates a hot-seat troop that runs out of time; Off never does\nok   settings › privacy: On puts a pass-the-controller card between hot-seat players, Off does not\nok   settings › animation: rigs move through their actions over time (humanoid swing, beast bite, blob squash, wings)\nok   task › Package: one html named GameTitle-SOURCE-model-date in the root\nok   task › Tech: the game is built on the my-3D2dge handoff engine (inlined)\nok   task › Audio: music, effects and gibberish voices are code, no audio files\nok   task › Art/Animation: every species x form and every knight builds a visual that animates\nok   task › Scope: the campaign is playable start to finish (one realm, autoplay, through real scenes)\nok   task › Dev mode: in the pause menu; live sliders for the key variables; reset to defaults\nok   task › Attract: 10 s idle on the title starts an AI demo; any input exits\nok   task › Multiplayer: AI Hub layer present (tags, shared-world driver) and local hot-seat\nok   task › Narrative tone: formal court register scenes with narration headings\nok   task › UI: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox option, keys/mouse follow the last device\nok   task › UI: the mouse clicks menu items (a click on a list row picks it)\n