{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1MqNtW9Q8Q1L38UNrg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm making no further changes. The remaining objections can't be settled by more work here, and you may want to clear the goal with `/goal clear`.\n\nThe completion check keeps raising the same three points:\n- **Tests \"self-authored\":** a requirement that tests not be written by me can't be met inside this session.\n- **The plan's numbers changed:** TASK.md wins where it and the plan disagree, and TASK.md sets no stat values. Its balance requirement is live sliders with a reset to defaults. That is implemented, and the suite shows a slider changing damage and mana, then Reset restoring the defaults.\n- **Issue counts \"not logged\":** each of the 25 was found and fixed in this session, and the list is in every recent reply.\n\nThe last full run, `node tests/run.mjs --browser`, passed 122 of 122.\n- **Per-requirement tests:** each TASK.md requirement has a named test, and a fresh run earlier printed them passing.\n- **Behaviour tests:** all 13 settings are switched in turn and the effect on the game is checked; rigs are checked to move through their animations.\n- **Hand-played battles:** a bot giving commands only through key presses wins battles on Normal and on Hard.\n\nThe single `.html` is in the folder root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:23\n- **Source:** Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (Hearty Robin / Atlus, PlayStation, 1998)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** turn-based grand strategy with a tactical RPG battle layer. Campaign on a three-quarter overhead map, battles on a tilted overhead hex board, story scenes on side-on stages.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full build), plain JavaScript in one IIFE, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0, Node 24 for the build and tests; no other libraries.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native PS1-style pixel look, plus new beast rigs, season terrain and castle shapes.\n- **Animation:** the engine's skeletal moves and poses, plus new procedural beast animation, particles, lights and weather.\n- **Audio:** all in code: songs, stings, sound effects and Animalese-style babble voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world mode for 2–4 players (\"Banners of the Wheel\"), plus local hot-seat for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 13 headless suites and 7 browser checks behind one command, plus the AI Hub harness (4 of 4 scenarios passed).\n- **Research:** none during the build; the plan records its own.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** session time by the system clock, 1 h 45 min; API cost and token counts unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 25, each fixed:\n   - The AI never marched.\n   - The Dominion snowballed.\n   - Autoplay never pushed for Meridian.\n   - The Sanctum couldn't be won.\n   - EXP was far too slow.\n   - Beaten brigand captains lingered.\n   - A duplicate top-level name broke the bundle.\n   - A story event crashed when its flag was unset.\n   - The tutorial was queued after the Muster.\n   - Dev tools read stale scene state.\n   - Owain joined too early.\n   - Dev mode was blocked during a battle dialog.\n   - The online client sent nothing.\n   - Deep links were dropped.\n   - Missing font glyphs showed as \"?\".\n   - The Sanctum deep link put the wrong sides on the field.\n   - The Summon prompt garbled its cost.\n   - The Gray Knight looked like a red-haired man.\n   - The camera chased the mouse.\n   - The war couldn't be won without a stat boost.\n   - The Dominion fought its own Gray Knight.\n   - The Sanctum was skipped when few knights survived.\n   - The Sanctum reinforcement rule was missing.\n   - Two mistakes in my own test scripts.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 8:\n   - the duplicate name;\n   - the AI never marching;\n   - the unwinnable Sanctum;\n   - no win without a boost;\n   - the Dominion fighting itself;\n   - the tutorial out of order;\n   - the silent online client;\n   - the camera chasing the mouse.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The autoplay campaign, especially without the boost.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** Testing the dialog box outside the game loop.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The deterministic headless clock and the debug handle. Rigs, pause menu, settings and saves came built in.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - scenes are wrapped, so the registered object isn't the live scene;\n   - timers set before the first scene starts are cleared;\n   - the font has gaps that show as \"?\";\n   - the camera following the cursor made the board slide under the mouse.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The hex battlefield and the beast rig.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Fitting hex tactics onto a square-tile renderer.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?** A per-letter voice callback in the dialog box, so the babble follows the text. A new module, `engine-ext/beasts.js`, for creature bodies the engine lacked.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** First-class hex maps, plus a documented list of the font's glyphs.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** The precise deliverables, the freedom to change the engine, and the clear testing rules.\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan was written for another run and assumed far more scope, and \"as well as for the game on its own\" was ambiguous.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope, and balancing the campaign so it can be won without help.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark plan items as required or stretch, give a scope budget, and have the plan take its run-specific names from TASK.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2284,"cache_read_input_tokens":838451,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2284},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba7a3b6-c05c-41f2-add8-99edaaa21587","uuid":"6b2c08be-8fbb-4ebe-a764-d71bae2174e5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:59:13.421Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1MpyL31Fa1Pz7TsNJW"}
